PVD("malaysia_ndp_2026-2030",{"docs":["","Malaysia NDP 2026 30"],"s":{"1":[[1,"46","1","Public Service Reform Agenda","The public service reform agenda forms the pillar in creating an administrative system that is responsive to the needs of the rakyat, in line with the thrust of strengthening good governance under the Ekonomi MADANI.",""],[1,"46","1","Service Delivery Improvement Based on ILTIZAM Principles","focus will be given on efforts to improve service delivery based on the ILTIZAM principles",""],[1,"46","1","Legislative Reform Programme","Priority will also be given to legislative reform",""],[1,"46","1","Project Management Efficiency Improvement","Priority will also be given to ... project management efficiency",""],[1,"46","1","Fiscal Consolidation Measures","Priority will also be given to ... fiscal consolidation",""],[1,"46","1","Integrity and Accountability Strengthening","The priority will also involve strengthening of integrity and accountability across the entire national administrative system to enhance confidence and trust of the rakyat.",""],[1,"46","1","Whole-of-Nation Public Service Reform Implementation","The implementation of all the strategies under this pillar through the whole-of-nation approach will drive the reform of the public service to become more transparent, timely and thorough.",""],[1,"47","1","Socioeconomic Restructuring and National Development Transition","The Thirteenth Plan, with the theme 'Melakar Semula Pembangunan' is a commitment to restructure socioeconomic development in accelerating the national economic growth, uplifting the living status of the rakyat and strengthening good governance towards realising the aspirations of the Ekonomi MADANI.",""],[1,"47","1","Social System Development Anchored on Insan MADANI","The national development during the Thirteenth Plan period will be supported by a comprehensive transition towards digitalisation and advanced technologies, particularly AI as well as the development of a social system anchored on insan MADANI, with a society that is equitable, harmonious, respectful and united.",""],[1,"120","1","Public Service Reform Agenda","The public service reform is a prerequisite in realising the aspiration of Malaysia towards a responsive and rakyat-oriented administration system by emphasising on good governance.",""],[1,"120","1","GovTech and Artificial Intelligence Mainstreaming","strengthening GovTech by mainstreaming artificial intelligence (AI) and other advanced technologies",""],[1,"123","5","Smart Service Delivery Transition","Priority will be given on efforts to ease regulatory burden that hampered the rakyat and business community as well as facilitate the transition towards smart service delivery.",""],[1,"124","1","Rakyat-Centric Digital Government Initiative","These improvements were continued with the implementation of rakyat- centric digital government in 2020 under the e-Gov 3.0 initiative.",""],[1,"124","1","GovTech Digital Service Delivery Expansion","Efforts in digitalising the public service delivery were expanded through the introduction of the GovTech initiatives encompassing the aspects of AI and other advanced technologies, such as internet of things, blockchain, big data and augmented reality.",""],[1,"124","2","Public Service Digitalisation through GovTech","Strengthening of public service digitalisation through the GovTech that is anchored on good governance will be able to connect the government, the rakyat and business community towards developing an AI nation.",""],[1,"124","3","Digital Government Development Framework","The Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint, 2021-2030, the National Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) Policy, 2021-2030 and the Public Sector Digitalization Strategic Plan, 2021-2025 were developed as guidance to continue the efforts towards developing a digital government.",""],[1,"124","3","National Artificial Intelligence Roadmap and National AI Office","The implementation of the Malaysia National Artificial Intelligence Roadmap, 2021-2025 and the establishment of the National AI Office in December 2024 further reinforced the commitment towards a digital government.",""],[1,"124","3","MyDigital ID Digital Identity Verification Initiative","The MyDigital ID initiative was introduced in November 2023 as a digital identity verification system to facilitate online access with just a single sign-on.",""],[1,"125","6","GovTech-Driven Government Service Delivery Transformation","The transformation of the government service delivery system by strengthening the GovTech under the Thirteenth Plan is in line with the aspiration to develop Malaysia as a high-income nation, driven by technology and digital.",""],[1,"125","6","Digital Service and Business Process Improvement","Strategies will focus on improving services and business processes, strengthening digital governance and enhancing digital talent development towards a digital government.",""],[1,"125","7","Public Sector Enterprise Architecture and Digital Service Integration","Digitalisation of government services and business processes will be improved by focusing on the development of an enterprise architecture3 (EA).",""],[1,"125","8","Government Digital Services Streamlining Initiative","Government digital services will be streamlined to reduce redundancy and development of systems in silos as well as establish a transparent and fair system.",""],[1,"125","8","Public Sector Single Gateway Platform","a public sector single gateway based on the Government as a Platform model will be developed to enable the government, the rakyat and business community to access various services.",""],[1,"125","8","Government Service Systems Integration and Interoperability Enhancement","integration and interoperability of government service systems will be strengthened comprehensively to optimise existing resources.",""],[1,"125","8","Pelan Tindakan Al Kebangsaan 2030 Implementation","The implementation of initiatives under the Pelan Tindakan Al Kebangsaan 2030 will enhance the effectiveness of service delivery, expedite decision making process based on data as well as strengthen cyber security.",""],[1,"125","9","Advanced Technology Adoption Across Ministries","Government administration matters will be improved through adoption of advanced technologies by all ministries, particularly Al application in various sectors such as security, health and education.",""],[1,"126","1","Phased Document Implementation and Pilot Projects","documents will be implemented in stages.",""],[1,"126","2","National Application Evaluation Mechanism Improvement","The evaluation mechanism of national applications will be improved, including assessment on satisfaction level of the rakyat pre-, during and post-implementation to enhance the efficiency of government digital services.",""],[1,"126","2","Technology Practitioner Feedback Platform","A specific platform will be developed for technology practitioners to channel opinions and suggestions for improvement.",""],[1,"126","2","Sludge Audit National Assessment Tool","In addition, sludge audit4, which is one of behavioural insights (BI) approaches, will be introduced as a national assessment tool to reduce red tape and increase satisfaction of the rakyat.",""],[1,"126","2","GovTech Data Transparency Initiative","The GovTech initiatives will also emphasise data transparency aspect in strengthening governance.",""],[1,"126","2","Digital Governance Strengthening Ecosystem","Strengthening of digital governance will establish an ecosystem that supports digital government transformation and increase participation of the rakyat towards improving public service delivery.",""],[1,"126","3","Digital Talent Development for Civil Servants","Digital talent development will be enhanced to produce knowledgeable, skilled and experienced civil servants in line with advancement in technology.",""],[1,"126","3","Digital and AI Training for Civil Servants","civil servants at all levels, especially young officials will be given exposure and intensive training in digital and AI as well as other focus areas related to megatrends.",""],[1,"126","3","Information Technology Service Scheme Enhancement","the information technology service scheme will be enhanced through the empowerment of talent and expansion of the job scopes to encompass digitalisation as a whole, beyond the field of information and communications technology.",""]],"2":[[1,"41","6","Whole-of-Nation Collaboration Framework","The whole-of-nation approach, through collaboration between the rakyat, businesses, CSOs and governments, will be adopted to increase efficiency and effectiveness",""]],"3":[[1,"18","2","Integrated Economic Restructuring and Service Delivery Reform","This transition requires integrated planning and action to boost economic growth akin to raising the ceiling, uplift the living status of the rakyat akin to raising the floor and strengthen service delivery towards excellent governance.",""],[1,"42","4","Public Service Reform Agenda","The public service reform agenda will be implemented by improving service delivery based on the principles of ILTIZAM as well as strengthening the GovTech and the ecosystem of the social economy.",""],[1,"42","4","Regulatory Burden Reduction and Institutional Restructuring under ILTIZAM","Through the ILTIZAM, efforts will be intensified to reduce regulatory burdens, enhance governance and talent capacity of the public sector as well as restructure institutions.",""],[1,"42","5","Government Department, Agency, and GLC Rationalisation","Institutional restructuring will also be intensified by implementing rationalisation of the government departments and agencies as well as government-owned companies in phases.",""],[1,"119","4","Regulatory Instrument Review","Strategy C1.1: Implementing Regulatory Instrument Review",""],[1,"120","1","Public Service Reform Agenda","The public service reform is a prerequisite in realising the aspiration of Malaysia towards a responsive and rakyat-oriented administration system by emphasising on good governance.",""],[1,"120","1","Government Service Delivery Enhancement Based on ILTIZAM Principles","the implementation of strategies and initiatives will be focused on enhancing government service delivery based on ILTIZAM1 principles",""],[1,"120","1","Governance, Project Management, Fiscal, and Social Economy Strengthening","Emphasis will also be given to enhance governance, reform project management and fiscal as well as strengthen the ecosystem of social economy.",""],[1,"122","2","Government Service Delivery Enhancement Based on ILTIZAM Principles","The enhancement of government service delivery based on the ILTIZAM principles aims to ensure that the rakyat and the business community benefit from quality, efficient and effective government services.",""],[1,"122","2","Good Governance Structural Reform","Strengthening of good governance through structural reform that is implemented based on four major shifts will ensure regulatory instruments remain relevant.",""],[1,"122","4","Public Service Reform Agenda","The Special Task Force on Agency Reform (STAR), established in March 2023, served as the primary platform for the implementation of the public service reform agenda.",""],[1,"122","4","Bureaucratic Reform and Regulatory Review Circulars","The Pekeliling Am Bilangan 3 Tahun 2024: Pelaksanaan Reformasi Kerenah Birokrasi and the Pekeliling Am Bilangan 4 Tahun 2024: Pelaksanaan Uji Kaji Peraturan were also introduced in November 2024 as references to ensure the implementation of initiatives in improving government services is effective and fulfils the needs of the rakyat.",""],[1,"122","5","PEMUDAH Public-Private Collaboration Platform","The role of the PEMUDAH as a platform to facilitate public-private sector collaboration was strengthened to support the implementation of the ILTIZAM.",""],[1,"123","5","Structural Reform through Enforcement of Act 867","The provision of rakyat-oriented public services will be realised by implementing structural reform through enforcement of the Act 867.",""],[1,"123","5","Regulatory Burden Reduction Initiative","Priority will be given on efforts to ease regulatory burden that hampered the rakyat and business community as well as facilitate the transition towards smart service delivery.",""],[1,"123","7","Periodic Review of Regulatory Instruments","Mandatory review of regulatory instruments2 will be undertaken periodically and within a stipulated time to ensure the instruments remain relevant and in line with current development and needs.",""],[1,"123","7","One In-One Out Regulatory Rationalisation Policy","the One In-One Out policy will be implemented, mandating the abolishment of one existing instrument that is irrelevant prior to introducing a new one.",""],[1,"123","7","Stakeholder Participation in Regulatory Review","The involvement of the rakyat and business community will be intensified to ensure the review is accurate and effective.",""],[1,"123","8","Regulatory Burden Reduction Guideline","A guideline on regulatory burden reduction will serve as a reference to ensure a reduction of at least 25% every three years is achieved.",""],[1,"123","8","State and Local Adoption of Regulatory Burden Reduction Guideline","State governments will be encouraged to adopt the guideline at state and local authority levels.",""],[1,"123","8","Whole-of-Nation Participation Expansion","The whole-of-nation approach will be expanded to ensure a holistic participation of the rakyat and business community.",""],[1,"123","9","Service Performance Rating Enhancement","Service performance rating will be strengthened by improving the criteria and expanding to all levels of government to evaluate the effectiveness of service delivery.",""],[1,"123","9","Standardisation of Service Rating Guidelines and Incentives","the guideline related to rating criteria and the provision of incentive will be standardised and improved.",""],[1,"123","9","Periodic Parliamentary Reporting on ILTIZAM Performance","the implementation performance of the ILTIZAM will be tabled periodically in the Parliament as a manifestation of continuous commitment by the government in providing the best services to the rakyat and business community.",""],[1,"126","5","Implementation of National Policies Based on Good Governance","The implementation of all national policies based on good governance, in line with the Ekonomi MADANI framework, will create a more dynamic, progressive",""],[1,"128","1","Public Service Integrity and Accountability Strengthening","Efforts will be intensified with the emphasis on the aspects of integrity and accountability as well as checks and balances in the public service.",""],[1,"128","1","Rationalisation of Ministry and Agency Functions","In addition, rationalisation of functions and roles of ministries and agencies as well as development of human resource in the public sector will also be prioritised.",""],[1,"128","1","Public Sector Human Resource Development","In addition, rationalisation of functions and roles of ministries and agencies as well as development of human resource in the public sector will also be prioritised.",""],[1,"128","2","Civil Service Integrity and Accountability Strengthening","The integrity and accountability of civil servants, including Members of the Administration, will be strengthened to develop insan MADANI in ensuring a more transparent, efficient and effective government service delivery.",""],[1,"128","2","Ministry Performance Monitoring and Evaluation Enhancement","the performance monitoring and evaluation mechanism for all ministries will be improved by introducing specific outcomes that will be aligned with selected macroeconomic performance indicators.",""],[1,"128","2","Prime Minister Direct Reporting Mechanism","ministry performance mechanism will be developed to enable direct reporting to the Prime Minister",""],[1,"128","2","National Outcome Performance Dashboard","a national outcome performance dashboard accessible by the rakyat will be introduced.",""],[1,"129","2","Government Delivery System Standardisation and Legal Harmonisation Reform","Efforts in standardising several legislation and regulations will be undertaken to improve the government delivery system at all levels.",""],[1,"129","4","Rationalisation of Ministries, Agencies, and State-Owned Enterprises","Efforts to rationalise the functions and roles of ministries and agencies will be accelerated in reducing resource redundancy and wastage.",""],[1,"129","5","Civil Service Job Function and Work Procedure Restructuring","responsibilities of civil servants will also be improved through the restructuring of job functions and work procedures in line with technology development towards enhancing the quality and productivity of public service.",""],[1,"129","5","Federal Government Facilities Management and Utilisation Improvement","The management and utilisation mechanisms of the Federal Government facilities, including quarters and public training institutions will be improved to ensure optimal sharing and usage.",""],[1,"132","3","Lean Public Sector Reform","Measures to realise a lean public sector will be accelerated to save operating costs and improve effectiveness of service delivery.",""]],"4":[[1,"42","5","Civil Service Competency and Expertise Development","The development of competency and expertise will be given emphasis to ensure civil servants remain relevant, competitive and responsive towards current needs.",""],[1,"129","6","Public Sector Human Resource Development Programme","The public sector human resource development will be enhanced to produce more competitive and future-proof civil servants.",""],[1,"129","6","Flexible Career Pathways and Placement Reform","Efforts in ensuring career pathways and flexible placement based on the field of job interest will also be intensified to motivate and increase productivity.",""],[1,"129","6","Public Service Talent Management Improvement","The management of the Kelompok Bakat Terbaik Perkhidmatan Awam will also be improved in developing the best talent by the field of job interest.",""],[1,"129","6","Civil Service Appointment Transfer Option","In addition, option for transfer of appointment will be introduced in providing civil servants with flexibility to change the service scheme according to expertise and job interest.",""]],"5":[[1,"26","8","AI-Enabled Data-Driven Government Decision-Making Reform","The adoption of AI in the government administration also offers reform in data driven decision making through real time information analysis.",""],[1,"27","5","Digital and Data Infrastructure Enhancement","The provision of digital infrastructure and infostructure, such as data centres, cloud computing and internet connectivity, particularly high-speed connectivity will be enhanced to support the extensive adoption of AI, including in the rural areas.",""],[1,"27","5","Integrated Data Repository Expansion","In addition, expansion of the integrated data repository will facilitate access and sharing of information as well as support more accurate decision-making process.",""]],"6":[[1,"126","2","Electoral Boundary Redelineation Using Big Data Analytics","In this regard, data transparency in the democracy system will be improved by re-delineation of electoral boundaries using big data analytics to address risks related to gerrymandering5.",""],[1,"128","6","Legislative and Institutional Reform to Strengthen Checks and Balances","Legislation and institutional reforms will be implemented to strengthen the national legislation system for Malaysia to be a fair and just nation.",""],[1,"129","1","Study on Separation of Powers Implementation","a study will be conducted to ensure expeditious implementation of the separation of powers between the Attorney General and the Public Prosecutor.",""]],"7":[[1,"18","3","Public Service Integrity and Fiscal Management Reform","In establishing excellent governance, MADANI administration will focus on efforts to strengthen integrity and accountability, enhance the efficiency of public service delivery as well as improve fiscal management.",""],[1,"23","2","National Anti-Corruption Strategy 2024-2028","policies formulated during the Twelfth Plan period include the National Anti-Corruption Strategy 2024-2028",""],[1,"24","2","Good Governance Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening of good governance will be focused on enhancing integrity and accountability aspects as well as increasing the efficiency and effectiveness of service delivery.",""],[1,"27","1","AI-Based Administrative Integrity and Accountability System","AI can also strengthen integrity and accountability of the national administrative system when the risks of non-compliance, malpractices or abuses of power are detected at an early stage.",""],[1,"41","6","Integrity, Accountability, and Public Service Efficiency Strengthening","During the Thirteenth Plan period, the MADANI Government will continue the efforts to strengthen integrity and accountability, increase efficiency of public service delivery as well as enhance fiscal management.",""],[1,"42","2","National Anti-Corruption Strategy Implementation","the implementation of initiatives under the National Anti-Corruption Strategy, 2024-2028 and the CPI Special Task Force will be intensified to address corruption issues and improve the position of the country in the CPI.",""],[1,"42","2","Strengthening of the Integrity Unit","The role of the Integrity Unit will also be strengthened to curb corruption in the public sector, with emphasis on initiatives based on behavioural insights approach towards developing civil servants with integrity and accountability.",""],[1,"42","3","Public Service Checks and Balances Strengthening Mechanism","Checks and balances mechanism in the public service will be strengthened to enhance accountability and transparency of the Government administration.",""],[1,"127","2","National Anti-Corruption Strategy","The National Anti-Corruption Strategy, 2024-2028 (NACS) was launched in May 2024 as a continuity of and improvement to the National Anti-Corruption Plan, 2019-2023.",""],[1,"127","2","CPI Special Task Force","The CPI Special Task Force was also established in October 2024 in spearheading efforts to improve performance of Malaysia to be in the top 25 in 2033.",""],[1,"127","2","Anti-Rent-Seeking Bill","Emphasis was also given on anti rent-seeking aspect through the drafting of a bill that is expected to be tabled in the Parliament in 2026.",""],[1,"128","3","Intensified Anti-Corruption Initiatives under NACS and CPI Special Task Force","The implementation of initiatives under the NACS and the CPI Special Task Force will be intensified in addressing corruption issues to improve the ranking of the country",""],[1,"128","4","Strengthening Integrity Units in Government Agencies","The role of the Integrity Unit (UI) in all government agencies will be enhanced in combatting corruption with emphasis on the implementation of initiatives based on the BI approach to drive behavioural change among civil servants.",""],[1,"128","4","Establishment of Integrity Units in Local Authorities","the UI will be established in all local authorities by 2027 to curb wrongdoings as well as violation of a code of conduct and ethics at the agency level.",""],[1,"128","5","Integrity Culture Awareness and Behaviour Change Programmes","Thus, efforts in enculturating integrity practices will be intensified through the implementation of various targeted awareness and behaviour intervention programmes as well as integration of teaching and learning modules.",""],[1,"128","5","Targeted Integrity and Noble Character Awareness Campaigns","Targeted awareness campaigns will also be implemented to improve insaniah values and develop noble character.",""],[1,"128","5","Expansion of Integrity Initiatives to GLCs and Private Sector","In addition, implementation of these initiatives will be expanded to include government-linked companies and the private sector.",""]],"8":[[1,"27","1","AI-Assisted Judicial Decision Support","help judges and magistrates in making more accurate rulings based on a comprehensive analysis of past case facts.",""]],"9":[[1,"130","5","Government Procurement Bill Drafting","These measures include drafting of the Government Procurement Bill, introduction of the Life Cycle Cost Guidelines Version 2.0 for public asset management, enhancement of the MyProjek system as well as introduction of value at entry (VAE) assessment.",""],[1,"130","5","Life Cycle Cost Guidelines for Public Asset Management","These measures include drafting of the Government Procurement Bill, introduction of the Life Cycle Cost Guidelines Version 2.0 for public asset management, enhancement of the MyProjek system as well as introduction of value at entry (VAE) assessment.",""],[1,"130","5","MyProjek System Enhancement","These measures include drafting of the Government Procurement Bill, introduction of the Life Cycle Cost Guidelines Version 2.0 for public asset management, enhancement of the MyProjek system as well as introduction of value at entry (VAE) assessment.",""],[1,"130","5","Value at Entry Assessment","These measures include drafting of the Government Procurement Bill, introduction of the Life Cycle Cost Guidelines Version 2.0 for public asset management, enhancement of the MyProjek system as well as introduction of value at entry (VAE) assessment.",""],[1,"131","7","Public Project Implementation and Cost Control Improvement","These efforts include improving effectiveness of project implementation and cost control as well as strengthening public-private partnership (PPP).",""],[1,"132","1","Public Sector Comparator Database Improvement","The Public Sector Comparator database will be improved to be more up-to-date and comprehensive, based on the life cycle cost concept and in comparison, with the implementation cost by the private sector.",""]],"10":[[1,"130","3","Government Project Planning and Implementation Governance Reform","Governance reform in the aspects of planning and implementation of government projects will improve public financial management efficiency and reduce leakages, in line with the thrust of good governance under the Ekonomi MADANI.",""],[1,"131","7","Development Project Management Reform","Several strategies were identified to reform development project management and accelerate fiscal consolidation in improving efficiency of project governance and public financial management.",""],[1,"131","8","Holistic Development Project Management Mechanism","A new and holistic development project management mechanism will be introduced to enable a more strategic and effective planning and implementation.",""],[1,"131","8","Ministry Strategic Planning Teams","a strategic planning team with specific skills will be established in every ministry",""],[1,"131","8","Strategic Planning Module for Civil Servants","a strategic planning module will be developed to enhance the competency of civil servants in development project management.",""],[1,"131","10","Strategic Development Project Evaluation Mechanism","An evaluation mechanism for strategic development projects will be established to improve control over development project costs.",""]],"11":[[1,"130","4","Fiscal Consolidation Continuation","The fiscal consolidation that will be continued in the Thirteenth Plan enable the achievement of a stable fiscal position and more sustainable debt targets, as well as the enhancement of the competitiveness of the country.",""],[1,"131","7","Fiscal Consolidation and Revenue Enhancement","Fiscal consolidation and improvement in Government revenue will be continued to strengthen the fiscal position of the country.",""],[1,"132","3","Targeted and Phased Subsidy Rationalisation","Targeted and phased subsidy rationalisation will also be implemented to reduce the financial commitment of the Government.",""],[1,"132","3","Monitoring of Federal Government Loan Guarantees for SOEs","the Federal Government guarantees on loans by the SOEs will be closely monitored to reduce the risk of Government contingent liabilities.",""]],"12":[[1,"12","8","Regulatory Instrument Review","Strategy C1.1: Implementing Regulatory Instrument Review",""],[1,"42","4","Regulatory Instrument Review and One In-One Out Policy","Mandatory reviews of regulatory instruments on a regular and periodic basis as well as the One In-One Out Policy will be implemented to ensure the effectiveness of these instruments.",""],[1,"42","4","State and Local Regulatory Burden Deduction Guideline","A guideline on regulatory burden deduction will be encouraged to be adopted at the state and PBT levels.",""]],"13":[[1,"132","1","Mandatory Building Information Modelling for Large Projects","The Building Information Modelling will be made mandatory for projects above RM10 million to enhance project planning and implementation efficiency.",""],[1,"132","1","Expansion of Industrialised Building System Use","the use of the Industrialised Building System will be expanded, particularly in the construction of public housing.",""],[1,"151","2","Accelerated Industrialised Building System and BIM Adoption","The transition to a construction system that utilises the Industrialised Building System (IBS) technology on a large- scale basis and a wider usage of the Building Information Modeling (BIM), particularly for affordable houses, will be accelerated.",""],[1,"151","2","Nationwide IBS Infrastructure Delivery Entity","These efforts will be supported through the establishment or selection of a government-linked company or a private entity that will be responsible in building IBS infrastructure nationwide, including in Sabah and Sarawak.",""]],"14":[[1,"25","8","AI-Based Incubation Centres, Research Hubs and Sandbox","The establishment of AI-based incubation centres, research hubs and sandbox within the research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) ecosystem will facilitate the development and testing of local solutions.",""],[1,"25","8","Advanced Simulation Modelling for Innovation Development","This approach is further supported by the usage of advanced simulation modelling, which can accelerate new technology creations as well as enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of the overall innovation process.",""],[1,"31","3","R&D&C&I Investment Model Improvement","The R&D&C&I investment model will be improved to increase high-value research as well as the creation",""],[1,"31","4","Intellectual Property Commercialisation Support","commercialisation of intellectual property (IP) through the provision of research facilities and targeted incentives.",""]],"15":[[1,"53","4","Third National Mineral Policy","The introduction of the Third National Mineral Policy in 2025, among others, aimed to drive the development of the local REE industry along the value chain",""],[1,"56","1","Rare Earth Elements Value Chain Development","Efforts for HGHV industries will focus on reforming the semiconductor industry, accelerating energy transition, developing the REE value chain, diversifying high-value agriculture products, strengthening development of the digital economy as well as leveraging science, technology and innovation (STI).",""],[1,"57","4","Rare Earth Elements Industry Ecosystem Development","The development of the REE industry will be accelerated by improving the entire ecosystem as well as intensifying activities along the value chain.",""],[1,"57","4","Rare Earth Elements Local Capacity Development and Strategic Collaboration","Focus will be given to develop local capacity, particularly in mining technology as well as in refining and separation of REE, through strategic collaborations with foreign countries.",""],[1,"57","4","Domestic Restriction of Rare Earth Raw Materials","REE raw materials will be restricted solely for domestic use to develop potential midstream and downstream industries.",""],[1,"57","5","Local Talent Development and REE Industry Support Package","Priorities will be given to the development of local talent as well as provision of infrastructure with advanced technology, and comprehensive financing and incentives to enhance the competitiveness of the industry.",""],[1,"57","5","REE Resources Inventory Mapping Mechanism","a more precise and detailed mapping mechanism will be deployed to expedite the development of REE resources inventory.",""],[1,"57","5","REE Industry Governance and Enforcement Reform","Policies and governance will be improved to increase efficiency and transparency of the REE industry management as well as ensure fair distribution of benefits to all stakeholders.",""],[1,"57","5","Federal-State Coordination and REE Enforcement Strengthening","Collaboration and coordination between the Federal and state governments will also be strengthened and enforcement will be enhanced to support sustainable development of the REE industry, thus protecting the environment and ensuring resource sustainability.",""]],"16":[[1,"56","1","Halal Industry Strengthening","the development of high impact strategic sectors will emphasise efforts to expand the air transport industry as well as strengthen the tourism, halal and creative industries.",""],[1,"60","4","Halal Commission Establishment","A halal commission will be established as a single entity responsible for halal governance and development.",""],[1,"60","4","Halal Market Expansion Programme","programmes to expand market of halal products and services to international level will be strengthened to support upscaling of local small and",""],[1,"61","1","Halal Industrial Park Enhancement","The role of halal industrial park will be enhanced to facilitate the development of a high-value halal industry.",""],[1,"61","2","Halal Guidelines Harmonisation Legislation","A legislation will be formulated to standardise halal guidelines, regulations and procedures at the Federal and state levels, complementing the establishment of the commission.",""],[1,"61","2","Halal Certification and Enforcement Harmonisation","The main focus of the harmonisation involves matters related to certification, auditing, promotion and enforcement of halal logo.",""],[1,"61","2","Halal Industry Governance Streamlining","This legislation is critical to resolve various issues that hinder the development of the halal industry as well as streamline the roles and functions of 198 agencies involved.",""]],"17":[[1,"21","7","MSME Supply Chain Integration and Market Expansion Initiatives","Various initiatives were implemented to integrate MSMEs into domestic and global supply chains, focusing on technology, digitalisation, financial support and market expansion.",""],[1,"34","1","MSME Scaling and Supply Chain Upgrading Initiative","Focus will be given to scale up MSMEs in strategic high-impact industries through extensive involvement in supply chains and higher value-added activities.",""],[1,"34","1","MSME Digitalisation, ESG Adoption, and Sandbox Support","Efforts will be undertaken to accelerate digitalisation and adoption of ESG principles as well as to provide sandbox platforms in enabling MSMEs adapt to the changes in the market and technology.",""],[1,"34","1","Whole-of-Nation MSME Innovation and Business Model Support","The whole-of-nation approach with stakeholder collaboration will be expanded to introduce disruptive business models in encouraging MSMEs to produce specialised products and services, based on customer needs.",""],[1,"34","1","SME Export Incentives and Trade Promotion Support","Efforts will also be intensified to provide comprehensive support for small and medium enterprises, such as export incentives as well as trade and investment promotions to enhance the capabilities and competitiveness of local companies in the global market.",""],[1,"34","2","MSME Sustainable Financing Mechanisms","Financing mechanisms for MSMEs will also be improved through sustainable financing methods, such as tiered financing and targeted financing.",""],[1,"37","2","Entrepreneurship Skills and Finance Support Programme","Entrepreneurship programmes will continue to be strengthened by enhancing skills training, technology adoption and digitalisation as well as financial supports.",""],[1,"37","2","Alternative Financing Expansion for Entrepreneurship","A more innovative alternative sources of financing, such as social impact funds, islamic social financing and corporate social responsibility will be explored and expanded.",""]],"18":[[1,"45","1","MSME and Third Sector Empowerment","Priority will also be given to fortify food security, strengthen flood mitigation and adaptation, improve the availability of public transport infrastructure as well as empower MSMEs and the third sector.",""],[1,"46","1","Social Economy Ecosystem Strengthening","Priority will also be given to ... strengthening of the social economy ecosystem in mainstreaming the third sector.",""],[1,"50","1","MSME and Third Sector Strengthening","The roles of micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) as well as the third sector will be strengthened to play a greater role in economic growth.",""]],"19":[[1,"84","1","MSME Scaling-Up Strategy","During the Thirteenth Plan period, two strategies will be implemented to scale up MSMEs, as follows:",""],[1,"84","2","MSME Strengthening through GLC Collaboration and Supply Chain Integration","MSME businesses will be strengthened through the introduction of new approaches involving collaboration with government-linked companies (GLCs) and adoption of disruptive business models, enhancement of operational efficiency as well as greater adoption of the ESG principles.",""],[1,"84","2","Expanded MSME Participation in GLC-Dominated Sectors","Capable MSMEs will be given a larger role in selected sectors dominated by GLCs.",""],[1,"84","2","MSME Supply Chain Study","a comprehensive study on supply chain will be conducted to identify opportunities, gaps and suitable areas for MSME involvement.",""],[1,"84","2","GLC Mandate Review for MSME Empowerment","the role and establishment mandate of GLCs in empowering MSMEs will be explored, including expanding GLC business models to involve MSMEs in the supply chains and higher value-added activities.",""]],"20":[[1,"105","4","Consolidation of Bumiputera Investment Institutions","the Bumiputera investment institutions were consolidated to enhance governance efficiency in realising the Bumiputera empowerment agenda more effectively.",""],[1,"107","2","Bumiputera Empowerment Agenda Implementation and Monitoring","The commitment to successfully implement the Bumiputera empowerment agenda will be continued.",""],[1,"107","3","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship Programme Expansion and Realignment","The entrepreneurship programmes capable of creating values and upscaling Bumiputera enterprises will be expanded to ensure a more meaningful contribution to the national economy.",""],[1,"107","3","Bumiputera Enterprise Relay Race Scaling-Up Programme","The scaling-up programme based on the concept of a relay race will be expanded to provide continuous support to Bumiputera enterprises at every level of business development, starting from the micro level to public listing stage.",""],[1,"107","3","Bumiputera Enterprise Access to High-Growth and Advanced Technology Sectors","Bumiputera enterprises will also be given opportunities to leverage HGHV as well as advanced technologies sectors and industries, including the halal industry.",""],[1,"107","4","Bumiputera Business Ownership Support Initiative","GLCs, government-linked investment companies and private companies will be intensified in supporting the Bumiputera development agenda to create more business owners among Bumiputera professionals.",""]],"21":[[1,"111","3","Corridor and Economic Zone Development Approach","The shift of emphasis to focused development based on corridor and economic zone has further reduced development disparities between regions.",""],[1,"111","3","Inter-Regional and Sub-Regional Economic Integration Cooperation","opportunities for economic integration through inter-regional and sub-regional cooperation must be fully leveraged to support a more balanced development.",""],[1,"114","1","Regional Economic Development and Infrastructure Access Programme","Focus will be given on efforts in promoting economic activities and investment in less developed areas, improving urban development management and increasing access to infrastructure facilities and services.",""],[1,"114","1","Regional Economic Integration and Governance Strengthening","efforts will be undertaken to accelerate economic integration and enhance regional development governance.",""],[1,"116","7","Greater Kuala Lumpur, Negeri Sembilan and Melaka Economic Cluster Investment Intensification","Investment activities in the Greater Kuala Lumpur, Negeri Sembilan and Melaka as a large-scale economic cluster will be intensified to boost economic growth as well as create jobs and entrepreneurship opportunities across sectors and industries.",""],[1,"116","7","Local Champion Enterprise Development Initiative","Potential local companies will be nurtured as local champions to strengthen the domestic supply chain ecosystem.",""],[1,"116","8","JS-SEZ Economic Collaboration and Joint Investment Promotion","The development of JS-SEZ will be realised through economic collaboration and joint investment promotion.",""],[1,"116","8","One-Stop Centre for Ease of Doing Business","This effort will be supported by strengthening the one- stop centre in facilitating ease of doing business and adopting latest technology applications for seamless cross-border mobility as well as developing skilled local talent.",""],[1,"116","8","Strengthening IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA Sub-Regional Initiatives","The sub-regional initiatives under the IMT-GT and the BIMP-EAGA cooperations will be strengthened to improve integration and sustainability of economic development.",""],[1,"116","8","Private Sector Participation in Cross-Border Economic Development","The cross-border economic development will be enhanced through the private sector active participation.",""],[1,"116","8","Special Economic Zone Development Exploration","The establishment of special economic zones focusing on specific sectors, including food production zone will be explored based on the potential and requirement of each area.",""]],"22":[[1,"84","3","MSME Disruptive Business Model Adoption Programme","Disruptive business models will be introduced in encouraging MSMEs to shift from mass generic production to large-scale customised production.",""],[1,"84","3","MSME Mindset Transformation and Sandbox Platform Programme","Mindset transformation programmes will be expanded and sandbox platforms will be provided in enabling MSMEs to adapt to dynamic changes in market and technology.",""],[1,"84","3","Targeted MSME Advisory and Management Enhancement Support","Targeted support programmes in the form of expert advisory services and enhancements of the management structure will be developed to improve operational efficiency, productivity and competitiveness of potential companies.",""],[1,"84","3","MSME Digital Transformation Acceleration Initiative","Digital transformation will also be accelerated by providing access to digital platforms,",""]],"23":[[1,"6","6","High-Value Investment Attraction Strategy","the nation must stand out as a main destination for quality and high-value investment, including in artificial intelligence, semiconductors and renewable energy industries.",""],[1,"6","6","Islamic Finance and Halal Industry Expansion","the steadfast commitment of the Government to drive the global Islamic economy will be sustained through the expansion of Islamic finance products and the strengthening of the halal industry.",""],[1,"6","6","International Market Expansion and Cooperation Initiative","International cooperation ties will also be intensified to explore new markets and broaden access to the global market.",""],[1,"31","2","Quality Investment and Business Environment Improvement Initiative","Focus will also be given to increase quality investment, improve business environment and empower talent.",""],[1,"31","5","Investor-Friendly Ecosystem Strengthening Measures","Measures will be undertaken to strengthen an investor- friendly ecosystem to attract higher quality investment, particularly in supporting production of 'Made by Malaysia' products and services.",""],[1,"31","5","Private Investment Expansion for HGHV Industries","Private investment will be enhanced to encourage more FDI and DDI in high growth high value (HGHV) industries and high-impact strategic sectors.",""],[1,"31","5","Targeted Incentives and Alternative Financing for Knowledge-Based Investment","The shift towards knowledge-based private investment will be accelerated through the provision of more targeted and competitive incentives as well as alternative financing.",""],[1,"31","5","ESG-Oriented Investment Support for Long-Term Value Industries","In addition, investment in potential industries to generate long-term value that adopt environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles will be strengthened to broaden access to domestic and global markets.",""],[1,"34","5","Foreign Investment Attraction in High-Growth and High-Impact Strategic Sectors","The development focus will also be given to attract foreign investors in HGHV industries and high- impact strategic sectors, explore new sources of growth outside the Klang Valley, Pulau Pinang and Johor as well as expand productivity programmes based on locality.",""],[1,"34","6","Global Trade Network Expansion","global trade networks will be expanded to strengthen economic integration, increase production and competitiveness of 'Made by Malaysia' products and services, explore new markets as well as intensify the promotion of trade and investment.",""],[1,"34","6","National Trade Blueprint 2.0","the National Trade Blueprint 2.0 will be introduced.",""],[1,"34","6","Trade War Negotiation and Trade Facilitation Measures","Efforts will also be intensified to address the challenges of tariff wars initiated by the US through continuous negotiations and facilitation of trade process.",""],[1,"34","7","Free Trade Agreement Participation and EU Negotiation Resumption","Focus will be given to strengthen economic integration through participation and commitment of Malaysia in free trade agreements (FTAs) as well as the resumption of negotiation between Malaysia and the European Union.",""],[1,"35","1","CPTPP and MTFTA Trade Agreement Enhancement","Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP) and the Malaysia-Türkiye Free Trade Agreement (MTFTA) will be enhanced to expand markets and strengthen trade relations.",""],[1,"35","1","Leveraging BRICS and ASEAN Trade Partnerships","participation of Malaysia as a BRICS partner country and as a member of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) will continue to be leveraged to reduce dependency on existing trade partners.",""],[1,"35","1","New Market Exploration Initiative","New markets, such as the countries in South America, Africa, the Middle East and Eastern Europe will also be explored to expand access to global market that will boost trade growth.",""],[1,"35","1","IMT-GT and BIMP-EAGA Trade Cooperation Strengthening","Trade cooperation with subregional countries through the Indonesia- Malaysia-Thailand Growth Triangle (IMT-GT) and the Brunei Darussalam-Indonesia-Malaysia-Philippines East ASEAN Growth Area (BIMP-EAGA) platforms will be strengthened.",""],[1,"35","1","Johor-Singapore Special Economic Zone Development","the development of the Johor-Singapore Special Economic Zone (JS-SEZ) will be enhanced to expand economic and investment cooperation with countries in the region.",""]],"24":[[1,"32","3","Expansion of New Growth Sectors and Economy Diversification","focus will continue to be given in exploring new sources of growth, such as industries within the energy transition as well as the green economy, blue economy, orange economy and circular economy.",""],[1,"32","4","Services Sector Development Intensification","The services sector development will continue to be intensified, focusing on strengthening of the existing strategic industries and exploring of new higher-value industries.",""],[1,"32","4","High-Value Sustainable Tourism Development","The tourism industry will be enhanced through the development of high-value and sustainable tourism products and destinations, among others through the establishment of potential tourism investment zones.",""],[1,"32","4","Strategic Industry Revitalisation and Expansion","the development of other strategic industries will include efforts to revitalise the global services industry, enhance the Islamic financial services industry, strengthen the halal industry and intensify the efficiency of the retail and logistics industries.",""],[1,"32","4","Creative Industry and Orange Economy Promotion","The local creative industry or orange economy will be invigorated through the production of local creative works with high commercial value, including those based on arts, cultural and heritage assets, in line with the aim in making Malaysia a regional and global market leader.",""],[1,"33","4","Natural Gas Supply Industry Strengthening","efforts to strengthen the natural gas supply industry will be undertaken to position Malaysia as a leading regional gas trading hub",""],[1,"33","4","Rare Earth Elements Industry Development","efforts to accelerate in the development of rare earth elements (REE) industry as a new source of growth will be given emphasis through international cooperation in developing local REE mining technology",""],[1,"45","1","Economic Complexity Advancement Pillar","Under this pillar, emphasis will be placed on efforts to propel the HGHV industries and high-impact strategic sectors and strengthen the green economy, blue economy, orange economy and circular economy.",""],[1,"50","1","Strategic Sector and Industry Development","In this regard, strategies and initiatives to raise the ceiling will be focused on developing strategic sectors and industries, strengthening ecosystem and empowering industry players.",""],[1,"50","1","High-Growth High-Value Industry Promotion","The development of strategic sectors and industries will be focused on efforts to propel high growth high value (HGHV) industries, high impact strategic sectors as well as the green economy, blue economy and orange economy.",""],[1,"52","3","New Industrial Master Plan 2030","The New Industrial Master Plan (NIMP) 2030 was introduced in 2023 to drive the industrial sector transformation of the country towards achieving the aspirations of the Ekonomi MADANI by emphasising advancement in technology, sustainability and deeper integration into the global value chains.",""],[1,"53","7","NIMP 2030 Strategic Co-Investment Fund","the NIMP 2030 Strategic Co-Investment Fund amounting to RM3.3 billion was approved to increase capital resources and create alternative financing to fund strategic and high-impact projects as well as the Mission-Based Projects identified under the NIMP 2030.",""],[1,"56","1","HGHV Industries and High-Impact Strategic Sectors Development Strategy","Propelling of HGHV industries and high impact strategic sectors as a driver of growth will focus on various areas.",""]],"25":[[1,"208","2","Urban Community Economic Empowerment Programme","Program Pemerkasaan Ekonomi Komuniti Bandar (PEKB), 1-21",""]],"26":[[1,"37","3","Social Integration and Volunteerism Promotion Initiative","The creation of a just and progressive society will emphasise on efforts to strengthen integration and unity, promote goodwill and foster a culture of volunteerism.",""],[1,"39","3","Social Integration and Unity Governance Strengthening","The implementation of more comprehensive social integration and interaction programmes will be enhanced and governance related to unity will be strengthened to develop a just and progressive society.",""],[1,"39","3","Community Integration and National Unity Programmes Expansion","Programmes and initiatives such as the Sejahtera Komuniti MADANI (SejaTi MADANI), the Kembara Perpaduan Malaysia MADANI, the Program Flagship Semarak Perpaduan as well as the Sekolah Angkat MADANI will be expanded to ignite the spirit of nationalism among the rakyat.",""],[1,"39","3","Malaysia Harmony Charter Development","In addition, a harmony charter of Malaysia will be developed as the main reference to strengthen inter-religion and inter-racial relations and harmony.",""],[1,"39","4","Stakeholder Empowerment for National Unity","The role of stakeholders, including local leaders, media practitioners and civil society organisations (CSOs) will be empowered to serve as agents of unity.",""],[1,"39","4","Volunteerism and Sports Participation Promotion","Participation of the rakyat in voluntary and sports activities will be intensified to inculcate the spirit of unity and solidarity.",""],[1,"141","1","Rukun Tetangga Community Leadership Empowerment Plan","The implementation of the Pelan Pemerkasaan Kepimpinan Komuniti Rukun Tetangga 2021-2030 and the Agenda Kerja Komuniti Rukun Tetangga enhanced community safety and harmony as well as strengthened the role of the Rukun Tetangga through voluntary activities.",""],[1,"142","1","Malaysia Harmony Charter Development","A harmony charter of Malaysia will be developed as a main guidance in fostering inter-religion and inter-racial relations and harmony in Malaysia.",""],[1,"142","1","Social Integration and Interaction Programmes","The implementation of more comprehensive social integration and interaction programmes will be enhanced by leveraging various platforms, including social media and digital games.",""],[1,"142","1","Nation-State Building and National Identity Programmes","programmes focusing on building a nation-state will be intensified to strengthen the national spirit and solidify the Malaysian identity.",""],[1,"142","2","Unity Governance Strengthening","Governance related to unity will be strengthened to improve the unity ecosystem.",""],[1,"142","2","Multi-Stakeholder Harmony and Accurate Information Initiative","The role of politicians, media practitioners, academia, NGOs and CSOs in instilling harmony will be enhanced by facilitating sharing of accurate information with the rakyat.",""],[1,"142","2","National Integration Research and Training Centre Upgrade","The Institut Kajian dan Latihan Integrasi Nasional will be upgraded as a centre of excellence in broadening research and training activities related to unity.",""],[1,"142","3","Patriotic Creative Content Production Initiative","Efforts will be intensified to produce creative works and content that showcase patriotism as well as project national identity and self-identity to ignite the spirit of nationalism among the rakyat.",""],[1,"142","3","Patriotism Measurement Index Development","An index to measure the level of patriotism will be developed as a guide in designing more comprehensive and effective programmes and interventions.",""],[1,"142","3","Rukun Negara and Federal Constitution Awareness Programme","Appreciation of the Rukun Negara and the Federal Constitution will be enhanced through various education and awareness initiatives in ensuring these principles continue to be valued and upheld by the rakyat.",""],[1,"142","3","Values, Integrity, and Volunteerism Strengthening Initiative","the inculcation of adab, spiritual values and humane aspects, including based on the principles of Maqasid Syariah, as well as the enculturation of integrity and volunteerism will be strengthened to develop insan MADANI and MADANI society that live in harmony within a more cohesive social system.",""],[1,"142","4","National Service Training Programme Improvement","The implementation of the Program Latihan Khidmat Negara will be further improved through integrated training modules that combine nationalism and basic military training components",""]],"27":[[1,"101","3","Hardcore Poverty Eradication Social Assistance and Income Generation Initiatives","In line with the Government commitment to eradicate hardcore poverty, social assistance and income generating initiatives such as the Sumbangan Tunai Rahmah (STR), targeted subsidies and the Inisiatif Pendapatan Rakyat (IPR) were introduced.",""],[1,"102","8","Inclusive Development Strengthening Strategies","Inclusive development from a multidimensional perspective will be strengthened to enhance social mobility and cohesion.",""],[1,"102","8","Poverty Reduction and Inequality Narrowing Measures","Strategies will continue to focus on efforts to strengthen the management of the cost of living, address poverty, narrow inequalities as well as improve social protection.",""],[1,"103","5","Targeted Social Assistance and Capacity-Building Support","Targeted social assistance will be continued, including cash and equipment assistance for capacity building and entrepreneurship to enable households exit poverty.",""],[1,"103","5","Income-Generating Programme Improvement","In addition, the design and implementation of income- generating programmes, such as the IPR, the Program Pemerkasaan Ekonomi Komuniti Bandar (PEKB) and the Skim Pembangunan Kesejahteraan Rakyat (SPKR) will be improved to enhance effectiveness.",""],[1,"103","5","Behavioural Insights for Programme Design and Targeting","The behavioural insights approach will be adopted in determining the programme design and target group to ensure achievement of programme outcomes.",""],[1,"103","5","Alternative Social Financing Expansion","More innovative alternative sources of financing based on the whole-of- nation approach will be explored and expanded.",""],[1,"104","1","Household Income Generation and Employment Support Initiatives","Efforts to narrow disparities across various dimensions will be intensified through the implementation of initiatives for household to generate income, including provision of job opportunities and entrepreneurship development as well as implementation of policies related to labour market.",""],[1,"104","3","Expansion of Income-Generating Programmes","Income generating programmes, such as the IPR, PEKB and SPKR will be expanded with improved programme designs to ensure maximum outcomes.",""],[1,"104","3","Strengthening of Micro-Entrepreneurship, Cooperatives and Social Enterprise Implementation Models","the implementation models for micro-entrepreneurship, cooperatives and SEs will be strengthened to boost income generation, particularly in localities with high poverty incidence and in remote areas.",""],[1,"105","2","Target Group Socioeconomic Empowerment Initiative","The implementation of this initiative is to empower the target groups in line with the principle of leaving no one behind, aligned with the thrust to raise the floor in achieving the aspirations of the Ekonomi MADANI.",""],[1,"107","1","Target Group Socioeconomic Advancement Strategy Package","Efforts to elevate the socioeconomic status of the target groups will continue to be focused through expansion in access to education and jobs, greater participation in entrepreneurship and economic activities as well as improvement in infrastructure.",""],[1,"117","1","Target Group Socioeconomic Advancement","elevation of the socioeconomic status of the target groups",""]],"28":[[1,"110","5","Men's Character and Family Leadership Strengthening Initiatives","Efforts will be undertaken to strengthen the roles and responsibilities of men, as more competitive and progressive heads of family as well as agents of community development and social change.",""],[1,"110","5","Expansion of Kafe@Teen Interactive Youth Platform","In addition, the role of Kafe@Teen will be expanded as an interactive platform in shaping positive, ethical and visionary teenagers.",""],[1,"110","5","Karamah Insaniah School Curriculum Approach","At the school level, the karamah insaniah approach will be emphasised in the syllabus to ensure the development of self-identity and inculturation of noble values at an early stage.",""],[1,"111","2","National Family Support Agenda","a national agenda on KASIH Keluarga Negara will be introduced to strengthen support for family institutions",""],[1,"111","2","Family and Reproductive Health Research Expansion","Research in the fields of family and reproductive health will be increased to identify the dynamics of families in preparation towards an aged nation",""]],"29":[[1,"109","3","Comprehensive Child Protection Strengthening","Comprehensive protection of children against all forms of negligence, abuse, exploitation, discrimination and violence will be strengthened to ensure that children are not separated from the family without reasonable cause.",""],[1,"109","3","Online Safety Act Enforcement for Child Protection","More effective enforcement of the Online Safety Act 2024 [Act 854] will strengthen the protection of children from cyber threats.",""],[1,"109","3","Age Limit Policy for Gadget Use","a new progressive policy will be explored to introduce age limit on gadget usage in mitigating the risks of negative impacts on mental and emotional development of children.",""]],"30":[[1,"110","6","Universal Design Enforcement and Disability-Friendly Infrastructure Rating Guideline","The Garis Panduan Perancangan Reka Bentuk Sejagat (Universal Design) will be enforced while a standardised star rating guideline by local authorities (PBTs) will be developed in providing a holistic disability-friendly infrastructure.",""],[1,"110","7","Expanded Protected Career Programme for Persons with Disabilities","Efforts will be undertaken to expand the Program Kerjaya Terlindung in collaboration with the private sector for industrial training placements of PWDs, enabling this group to enhance relevant skills and receive income.",""],[1,"111","1","Mainstreaming Persons with Disabilities in Decision-Making","the involvement of PWDs in decision-making process will be mainstreamed to ensure the needs of this group are taken into consideration in the planning of government policies and programmes.",""]],"31":[[1,"41","2","Orang Asli Development Action Plan and Legal Reform","the standard of living of the Orang Asli community will also be enhanced by introducing an action plan for the development of Orang Asli and amending the Aboriginal Peoples Act 1954 [Act 134].",""],[1,"41","2","Orang Asli Customary Council Establishment","a customary council will be established to increase the leadership effectiveness of the Orang Asli community.",""],[1,"107","5","Orang Asli Development Action Plan","an action plan for Orang Asli development will be implemented to strengthen policies and governance as well as to improve the design of development programmes to be more inclusive.",""],[1,"107","5","Amendment to the Aboriginal Peoples Act 1954","Service delivery will be improved through amendment to the Aboriginal Peoples Act 1954 [Act 134].",""],[1,"107","5","Customary Council for Orang Asli Governance","a customary council will be established to reform the governance of Orang Asli community traditional leadership in enhancing the efficiency of the Penghulu or Batin.",""],[1,"107","6","Orang Asli Education and TVET Support Programme","The talent development of the Orang Asli community will be strengthened by improving access to education and TVET, including schooling assistance and scholarships.",""],[1,"107","6","Orang Asli Plantation Redevelopment and Land Survey Initiative","the redevelopment of oil palm and rubber plantations, as well as land survey will be continued",""],[1,"107","6","Orang Asli Entrepreneurship Development through Cooperatives and Social Enterprises","entrepreneurship development through cooperatives and SEs will be expanded.",""],[1,"107","6","Orang Asli Housing and Basic Amenities Provision","The wellbeing of the Orang Asli community will be improved through the provision of housing, infrastructure and basic amenities such as roads, water and electricity as well as telecommunications.",""]],"32":[[1,"40","5","Aged Nation Preparedness and Policy Reform Package","The preparation towards an aged nation will be strengthened to ensure Malaysia is ready in various aspects, particularly in the management of economy and fiscal, development of talent, skills and education, expansion of social protection as well as strengthening of health and long-term care services.",""],[1,"40","5","Retirement Age Review and Re-employment Legislation","This preparation will also consider the need to review acts related to retirement age and enact new legislation concerning re-employment to increase the participation of older workers in the labour market.",""],[1,"40","5","Inclusive Social Protection and Older Persons Support Expansion","A more inclusive social protection system will be introduced and more comprehensive programmes and support services for older persons will be expanded.",""],[1,"40","5","Age-Friendly Infrastructure Provision","In addition, more age-friendly infrastructure will be provided to meet the requirements of population dynamics.",""],[1,"138","1","Ageing Nation Preparedness Reform","enhancing preparedness towards an aged nation",""],[1,"143","8","Ageing Population Support and Caregiving Measures","During the Twelfth Plan period, various initiatives were implemented to address the challenges of an ageing population, encompassing social support and healthcare programmes as well as upskilling and expanding job opportunities.",""],[1,"143","8","Employer Tax Incentive for Caregiving Leave Benefits","An additional tax incentive was introduced for employers that provide leave benefits for caregiving in the period from 2025 to 2027.",""],[1,"144","2","Monthly Cash Assistance for Older Persons","The monthly cash assistance for the older persons, which was increased from RM350 to RM500 in 2024 and subsequently to RM600 in 2025, improved the income of 154,000 older persons.",""],[1,"144","7","Older Persons Wellbeing Enhancement Initiative","This preparation will be intensified by establishing a sustainable LTC ecosystem, strengthening the labour market, skills and education, aligning fiscal priorities and improving social protection as well as enhancing the wellbeing of older persons.",""],[1,"144","7","Social Protection Strengthening for an Ageing Population","This preparation will be intensified by establishing a sustainable LTC ecosystem, strengthening the labour market, skills and education, aligning fiscal priorities and improving social protection as well as enhancing the wellbeing of older persons.",""],[1,"145","7","Social Protection System Reform","Improvement of the social protection system to be more comprehensive and inclusive will be implemented to enhance the effectiveness of assistance and efficiency of public spending.",""],[1,"145","7","Employees Provident Fund Scheme Reform","Focus will be given on efforts to reform the Employees Provident Fund (EPF) scheme in",""],[1,"146","1","EPF Contribution Separation Review","the separation of EPF contributions into two components, namely retirement savings and pension scheme will be explored.",""],[1,"146","1","Digital Platform for Recurring Family Cash Transfers","A dedicated digital platform will be developed to encourage recurring cash transfers from children to parents to ensure post-retirement livelihood and strengthen the role of family institution.",""],[1,"175","5","Comprehensive Lifelong Social Protection System","A comprehensive lifelong social protection system is provided to ensure the target groups are able to lead dignified lives.",""]],"33":[[1,"21","7","Third Sector Socioeconomic Development Support","The participation of the third sector, including cooperatives, social enterprises and agricultural-based associations in socioeconomic development activities of the rakyat also continued to increase.",""],[1,"34","2","Third Sector Capacity Strengthening Initiative","Focus will also be given on efforts to enhance the capabilities of the third sector in driving sustainable development of the social economy by strengthening financial capacity and capability as well as participating in the inclusive business model.",""],[1,"34","2","Buy Social Campaign Expansion","Market access through the 'Buy Social' campaign will be expanded to increase the visibility of the third sector.",""],[1,"43","1","Social Economy Policy Development and Third Sector Policy Review","a social economy policy will be developed and existing policies, acts and action plans related to the third sector will be reviewed",""],[1,"43","1","Third Sector Governance Centralisation Reform","measures will be undertaken by rationalising agencies to centralise governance of the third sector in enhancing the effectiveness of the sector in the national socioeconomic development",""],[1,"85","2","Third Sector Capability Enhancement for Social Economy Development","Capability enhancement of the third sector players will drive the development of sustainable social economy.",""],[1,"85","2","Inclusive Business Model Promotion","Companies will conduct businesses based on inclusive business model that will generate profit, while contributing to social needs.",""],[1,"85","2","Income Generation and Support Services for Vulnerable Households","Target groups, particularly low-income households and vulnerable communities will benefit from opportunities to generate income and from the provision of support services.",""],[1,"86","1","Third Sector Strengthening and Inclusive Business Promotion","The development of the third sector will be strengthened through the whole-of-nation approach to ensure this sector becomes the main driver of growth for inclusive and sustainable social economy.",""],[1,"86","1","Third Sector Resilience and Visibility Enhancement","Focus will be given on efforts to strengthen resilience and enhance visibility of the third sector",""],[1,"86","1","Inclusive Business Participation Promotion","as well as amplify participation of companies in inclusive business.",""],[1,"86","2","Third Sector Capacity Building and ESG Adoption Programme","Capacity building programmes for the third sector players will focus on the provision of training and advisory services, enhancement of skills related to organisational management and administration as well as strengthening of mentor-mentee programmes.",""],[1,"86","2","Third Sector ESG Adoption Initiative","the third sector players will be encouraged to adopt the ESG practices in the efforts to improve competitiveness of the organisation.",""],[1,"86","3","Alternative Financing Source Exploration","Alternative financing sources such as social sukuk, crowdfunding, zakat and waqf will be explored to increase funds and reduce direct dependency on the government.",""],[1,"86","3","Interagency Financing Coordination","Collaboration among government agencies will be enhanced to ensure equitable and transparent distribution of financing sources.",""],[1,"86","3","Blended Finance Expansion","In addition, blended financing models will be expanded to mitigate investment risks, and non-profit based organisations will be encouraged to explore activities that will generate own income in enhancing financial sustainability.",""],[1,"86","4","Integrated Promotion and Market Access Support for the Third Sector","Efforts to enhance visibility of the third sector will be intensified through integrated promotional and marketing activities of products and services.",""],[1,"86","4","Third Sector Participation in Government and GLC Procurement","Opportunities for the third sector to participate in the government and GLC procurements in supplying products and services will be explored.",""],[1,"86","4","Buy Social Campaign for Third Sector Market Access","Market access will also be expanded through the 'Buy Social' campaign that will support 'Made by Malaysia' initiative.",""],[1,"86","4","E-commerce Business Matching and Marketing Collaboration","In addition, business matching and marketing activities through e-commerce platforms will be encouraged through public and private strategic collaborations.",""],[1,"86","4","Social Recognition and Incentives for Third Sector Supporters","Initiatives through social recognition and incentive for parties that support the third sector activities will also be improved to invigorate the social economy.",""],[1,"86","5","Inclusive Business Blueprint and Supportive Ecosystem","An inclusive business blueprint will be developed to establish a supportive ecosystem in facilitating companies that provide economic opportunities for the third sector in the value chain.",""],[1,"86","5","Strategic Collaboration for Inclusive Business","Strategic collaboration among GLCs, multinational companies, NGOs, CSOs, social enterprises, cooperatives and the government will also be intensified to support companies participating in inclusive business.",""],[1,"86","5","Targeted Incentives for Inclusive Business","In addition, targeted incentives, including grants and financing support, will be introduced for companies that either conduct inclusive business or provide funds to parties adopting inclusive business model.",""]],"34":[[1,"99","5","Retirement Income Separation Mechanism","Therefore, a better mechanism to ensure continuous income after retirement will be explored.",""],[1,"99","6","Expanded Social Protection Coverage for Workers","Social protection for all workers will be strengthened to ensure a more comprehensive coverage, including the risks of job loss and accidents.",""],[1,"99","6","Gig Worker Welfare Legislation","Specific legislation will be enacted to guarantee the welfare of gig workers, including the right to work in a safe, healthy and conducive environment.",""],[1,"99","6","Expanded Employment Accident Protection","Protection against employment- related accidents will be improved, including those that occur outside working hours and non-work related.",""],[1,"99","6","SOCSO Rehabilitation and Recovery Services Expansion","Rehabilitation and recovery services under the Social Security Organisation (SOCSO) will also be expanded to enable workers who are involved in accidents receive necessary treatments and return to work.",""],[1,"104","5","Social Protection Reform Continuation","The social protection reform initiated under the Mid- Term Review of the Twelfth Plan will be continued in the Thirteenth Plan, focusing on strengthening social protection holistically.",""],[1,"104","5","National Social Protection Policy Formulation","the National Social Protection Policy will be formulated to ensure the scope of protection for the rakyat is inclusive and comprehensive.",""],[1,"104","5","Retirement and Social Security Framework Enhancement","the retirement system and social security protection frameworks, including the registration mechanisms and coverage of mandatory contribution under the EPF and SOCSO schemes will be enhanced.",""]],"35":[[1,"103","1","Comprehensive National Multidimensional Poverty Policy","A comprehensive national policy will be formulated to provide direction and new approaches in addressing multidimensional poverty.",""],[1,"103","1","PADU-Based Targeting for Social Assistance and Poverty Programmes","The PADU will be the source of reference in identifying target groups in the implementation of intervention comprising social assistance and poverty programmes to minimise inclusion and exclusion errors.",""],[1,"104","1","Targeted Social Assistance and Subsidy Eligibility Reform","The identification of target groups for social assistance and targeted subsidies will be improved.",""],[1,"104","1","Prosperity Gap Indicator Development","In addition, a prosperity gap indicator will be introduced to complement the existing inequality measurement.",""]],"36":[[1,"41","3","Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak Development Support Initiatives","The socioeconomic development of the Anak Negeri Sabah and the Bumiputera Sarawak will continue to be strengthened through initiatives such as human capital empowerment, infrastructure and basic amenities improvement as well as the provision of support to enable the development of Native Customary Rights (NCR) land.",""],[1,"41","3","Indian Household Quality of Life Improvement Programmes","The quality of life of Indian households, particularly the low-income earners will be enhanced through the implementation of initiatives and programmes based on the Malaysian Indian Blueprint and the Indian Community Action Plan.",""],[1,"107","7","Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak Development Support","The socioeconomic development of Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak will continue to be strengthened by accelerating economic growth and community development.",""],[1,"107","7","Talent Empowerment Initiative","Among the initiatives to be implemented include talent empowerment, infrastructure and basic amenities improvement as well as NCR land",""],[1,"107","7","Infrastructure and Basic Amenities Improvement","Among the initiatives to be implemented include talent empowerment, infrastructure and basic amenities improvement as well as NCR land",""],[1,"108","1","Business Opportunities Expansion for Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak","business opportunities for the Anak Negeri Sabah and Bumiputera Sarawak will be expanded through the provision of commercial premises and access to financing.",""]],"37":[[1,"45","2","Inclusive Regional and Rural Development Measures","Measures to improve the socioeconomic status of the target groups and accelerate economic growth in less developed and rural areas aim to achieve a balanced and inclusive growth.",""],[1,"61","3","Infrastructure and Incentives for Investment Outside Major Growth Centres","Infrastructure, basic facilities and incentives will be provided through collaboration with various stakeholders in attracting foreign investors to invest outside of the Klang Valley, Pulau Pinang and Johor.",""],[1,"71","4","Rural Income Initiative Enhancement for Agricultural Entrepreneurs","the Inisiatif Pendapatan Rakyat involving agricultural entrepreneurs will be enhanced by improving the implementation model, diversifying agricultural activities and increasing the utilisation of idle lands.",""]],"38":[[1,"40","1","Rural Community Infrastructure and Basic Services Upgrading","Efforts to empower communities in rural areas and settlement schemes, including in Sabah and Sarawak, will be implemented through the improvement of infrastructure and basic facilities, social amenities as well as housing.",""],[1,"40","1","Basic Facilities, Schools, Clinics and Broadband Expansion","The construction and upgrading of basic facilities, such as schools, health clinics, community centres, sports facilities and multipurpose halls as well as the provision of infrastructure and broadband coverage will be expanded.",""],[1,"116","2","Strengthening State Economic Development Corporations","The functions and roles of state economic development corporations (PKENs) and LKWs will be strengthened to boost economic growth of states, particularly to increase the Bumiputera participation, ownership and control in the economy.",""],[1,"116","3","Basic Rural Infrastructure Masterplan and Infrastructure Mapping","The planning of basic rural infrastructure provision will be strengthened through the development of a comprehensive masterplan and infrastructure mapping.",""],[1,"116","3","Provision of Sites for Cemeteries and Basic Amenities","This planning also includes the need for the provision of sites for cemetery and other basic amenities.",""],[1,"116","3","Improvement of Rural Service Provision","Provision of services in the rural areas will be improved to be on par with those in urban areas to reduce rural-urban migration.",""],[1,"116","6","Rural Leadership Capacity Building and Digital Skills Programme","JPKK, JPKK Persekutuan and JPKK Orang Asli will be strengthened through leadership capacity building and digital skills programmes.",""],[1,"117","1","Regional Economic Balance and Rural Development","balancing of regional economic growth and strengthening of rural development",""]],"39":[[1,"159","2","Non-Revenue Water Reduction and Reclaimed Water Use Initiative","Initiatives to reduce non-revenue water and raw water consumption, as well as diversify the sustainable use of reclaimed water will continue to be implemented.",""],[1,"159","2","Water-Efficient Local Water Technology Development","Focus is also given to the development of innovative, water-efficient, and competitive local water technologies, particularly in water treatment and recycling systems, as well as in the management and smart monitoring of water resources and services.",""]],"40":[[1,"40","4","Flood Mitigation Projects","the Rancangan Tebatan Banjir (RTB) projects.",""],[1,"45","1","Flood Mitigation and Adaptation Measures","Priority will also be given to fortify food security, strengthen flood mitigation and adaptation, improve the availability of public transport infrastructure as well as empower MSMEs and the third sector.",""],[1,"78","1","Flood Mitigation and Adaptation Strategy","Strengthening of flood mitigation and adaptation will increase the national resilience against disasters.",""],[1,"78","2","Flash Flood Mitigation Allocation for Kuala Lumpur","A special allocation of RM500 million on a reimbursement basis was approved in 2022 to mitigate flash floods in the Federal Territory of Kuala Lumpur.",""],[1,"78","2","National Drainage and Retention Pond Upgrade","In addition, a special allocation of RM220 million was provided in 2024 to upgrade drainage systems and maintain retention ponds nationwide.",""],[1,"78","2","Flood Mitigation Projects","During the Twelfth Plan period, a total of 17 flood mitigation projects were successfully completed, which provide protection to approximately another 154,000 residents living across an area of 74 square kilometres.",""],[1,"78","3","High-Priority Flood Mitigation Projects","Flood mitigation efforts were further strengthened through the implementation of 43 high-priority flood mitigation (TBBT) projects since 2024, with a total allocation of RM12 billion.",""],[1,"78","3","Flood Mitigation Project Portfolio","Among the flood mitigation projects being implemented include the Rancangan Tebatan Banjir (RTB) Kota Bharu in Kelantan, the RTB Sungai Langat and the Dual-Function Retention Pond from Sungai Klang to Sungai Rasau in Selangor, the RTB Sungai Tepoh and Banggol Air Lilih Kuala Nerus in Terengganu, as well as the Pembangunan Lembangan Sungai Bersepadu (PLSB) Sungai Skudai in Johor.",""],[1,"78","3","Flood Mitigation Project Implementation Task Force","A special task force was also established to improve the implementation mechanism of flood mitigation projects, including the Projek PLSB Sungai Golok in Kelantan with a total cost of RM3 billion.",""],[1,"78","11","Integrated River Basin Management Development","Development of new integrated river basin management initiated",""],[1,"79","1","Flood Mitigation and Adaptation Programme","Measures will be undertaken to accelerate the development of flood mitigation infrastructure, incorporate alternative approaches for flood adaptation and management as well as strengthen governance mechanism.",""],[1,"79","2","National Flood Mitigation Infrastructure Enhancement","Holistic flood mitigation efforts across the country will be expedited through the enhancement of planning, development and maintenance of the required infrastructure.",""],[1,"79","2","Flood Mitigation Planning Mechanism Improvement","The flood mitigation planning mechanism will be improved, particularly in terms of design and land acquisition process, in the efforts to expedite the implementation of flood mitigation.",""],[1,"79","2","Integrated Drainage and Stormwater Information System","An integrated information system related to drainage and stormwater network based on the Geographic Information System will be developed to enhance the efficiency of flood mitigation infrastructure management.",""],[1,"79","3","TBBT Project Acceleration Initiative","The implementation of 43 TBBT projects, particularly in key economic and high-density areas, will be accelerated by allocating special funds, establishing a dedicated TBBT",""],[1,"79","4","Flood Mitigation Project Acceleration","Among the flood mitigation projects to be expedited are the RTB Bandaraya Kuching in Sarawak, the RTB Lembangan Sungai Johor and the RTB Lembangan Sungai Muar in Johor, the RTB Lembangan Sungai Pahang in Pahang, the RTB Baling in Kedah, the RTB Sungai Likas in Sabah, as well as the RTB Sungai Trolak in Perak.",""],[1,"79","4","AI-Based Flood Early Warning System Expansion","The flood early warning system that uses AI technology in major river basins will also be strengthened and expanded under the TBBT initiative with a total cost of RM398 million to ensure more accurate and timely forecasts and warnings as well as increase society preparedness.",""],[1,"79","5","Flood Retention Pond Conversion Initiative","Existing water catchment areas, such as old mines and recreational lakes will be leveraged to be flood retention ponds as an immediate measure to accommodate water overflow, particularly in high-risk areas.",""],[1,"79","5","Multifunction Flood Mitigation Infrastructure Development","the development of multifunction infrastructure for flood mitigation, generation of hydroelectric power, provision of alternative water supply and recreational activities will be explored to optimise benefits for the rakyat and support economic development.",""],[1,"79","6","Flood-Adaptive Building Standards Enhancement","The implementation of flood-adaptive building concepts, such as the construction of floating houses and buildings with high pillars as well as the use of flood-proof materials, will be enhanced to reduce the impact in high-risk areas nationwide.",""],[1,"79","6","Nature-Based Flood Management Solutions","Sustainable nature-based solutions will be intensified to reduce flood management costs in the long term.",""],[1,"79","6","Disaster-Proof City Development Expansion","the development of cities based on disaster-proof concept will be expanded to enhance resilience against flood risks.",""],[1,"79","6","Sponge City Guideline Development","a sponge city guideline encompassing methods for flood risk reduction as well as water retention and absorption capacity enhancement will be developed as a main reference for PBTs to support sustainable urban development.",""],[1,"80","2","Flood Mitigation Infrastructure and Drainage Governance Strengthening","The governance related to planning, development and maintenance of flood mitigation infrastructure and drainage systems, water catchment areas and river pathways will be strengthened.",""],[1,"80","2","Flood-Resilient Land Use Planning and Development Standards Enforcement","Land use planning will be improved to be more systematic, and the enforcement of development standards will be intensified to increase resilience against flood risks.",""],[1,"80","2","Flood Recovery Plan for Affected Infrastructure","In addition, a recovery plan for flood-affected infrastructure will be developed to expedite access to supplies and resumption of disrupted economic activities.",""]],"41":[[1,"154","5","Public Safety and Security Strengthening Measures","Strategic efforts and comprehensive approaches will be continued to address challenges related to public safety and security threats that are increasingly complex.",""],[1,"154","5","National Sovereignty Protection Initiative","focus will be given on efforts to enhance public safety and security, uphold the national sovereignty, enhance the welfare of security personnel as well as improve the management and rehabilitation of crime offenders.",""],[1,"154","6","Crime Prevention and Crisis Preparedness Strengthening","Efforts in crime prevention and crises preparedness will be strengthened to enhance public safety and security.",""],[1,"154","6","Integrated Law Enforcement Operations and Targeted Patrols","Strategic cooperation among various enforcement agencies will continue to be intensified through integrated operations and targeted patrols in preventing crime.",""],[1,"154","6","AI-Enabled Public Safety Operations","The usage of AI technologies, such as smart scanners, video analytics and automated monitoring systems, will be leveraged in the operational tasks of the public safety and security agencies to enhance service efficiency to the rakyat.",""],[1,"154","6","Crime Awareness Education and Advocacy Campaigns","The implementation of educational programmes, advocacy and campaigns will be continued to instil public awareness on crime risks and the necessary safety measures to be undertaken.",""],[1,"154","6","Crime Prevention Programmes Including Drug Abuse","Prevention programmes on crimes, including drug abuse will also be intensified in collaboration with all stakeholders.",""],[1,"154","6","Urban Area Redevelopment for Crime Reduction","abandoned urban areas will be redeveloped to curb crime and urban safety benchmarks will be introduced to measure the level of public safety.",""],[1,"154","7","Community-Based Crime Prevention Volunteering","Community-based voluntary activities in crime prevention will continue to be encouraged through strategic collaboration between enforcement agencies and the private sector, NGOs, CSOs and local communities.",""],[1,"154","7","Public Safety Reporting Digital Applications","The utilisation of safety digital applications by the public in reporting suspicious incidents directly to the authorities will also be increased.",""]],"42":[[1,"154","5","Security Personnel Welfare Improvement","focus will be given on efforts to enhance public safety and security, uphold the national sovereignty, enhance the welfare of security personnel as well as improve the management and rehabilitation of crime offenders.",""],[1,"156","1","Security Personnel Welfare and Housing Support Programme","Efforts to enhance the welfare of security personnel who are in service and retired will be intensified through provision of better homes, healthcare services and social support.",""],[1,"156","1","Security Personnel Quarters Expansion Initiative","The provision of quarters for security personnel will be expedited through several strategic approaches, including public-private partnership and grouped leasing initiatives.",""],[1,"156","1","Security Quarters Guideline Review","the existing guideline for the provision of quarters will be reviewed to reduce the cost per unit without compromising quality and quantity of quarters.",""],[1,"156","1","Satu Anggota Satu Rumah Home Ownership Expansion","the Satu Anggota Satu Rumah programme will be expanded to provide home ownership opportunity for more personnel, including a provision of 15% quota for army veterans.",""]],"43":[[1,"156","5","Drug Addiction Prevention, Treatment, and Rehabilitation Programme","The issues of addiction to drugs and prohibited substances in society will be addressed more effectively through the enhancement of prevention, treatment and rehabilitation programmes as well as enforcement.",""],[1,"156","5","Integrated Rehabilitation Support System for Drug Addicts","The rehabilitation support system for addicts and individuals who abuse drugs will be strengthened through the implementation of more comprehensive and integrated rehabilitation programmes, involving all relevant agencies.",""]],"44":[[1,"146","7","Strengthening Public Hospital Cardiology Services","As of mid 2025, cardiology services in public hospitals were strengthened with the operationalisation of 24 invasive cardiology laboratories.",""],[1,"146","7","Dilapidated Clinic Upgrading Programme","During the period of 2021 to 2025, a total of RM936.86 million was allocated to upgrade, renovate and repair 2,215 dilapidated clinics, and a total of RM11.95 billion was allocated for",""],[1,"147","1","Nationwide Hospital Upgrading Programme","the implementation of 255 hospital upgrading projects nationwide.",""],[1,"147","1","Integrated Services for Older Persons","healthcare services for older persons were enhanced by integrating seven hospitals with 20 health clinics.",""],[1,"147","1","Skim Perubatan MADANI Private Clinic Network","a total of 2,485 out of 4,042 private clinics registered under the Skim Perubatan MADANI remain active in providing healthcare services for the underprivileged rakyat.",""],[1,"148","5","Healthcare Services Delivery Ecosystem Enhancement","The healthcare services delivery ecosystem will be enhanced in preparation towards an aged nation.",""],[1,"149","2","Expansion of Cluster-Based Integrated Care Facilities","The provision of health facilities based on the cluster concept for integrated care will be expanded to include transitional care.",""]],"45":[[1,"36","5","Rakan KKM Paid Access Initiative","Healthcare services will be improved through the Rakan KKM initiative as an option for private companies to access paid services at public healthcare facilities.",""],[1,"36","5","Health Insurance and Takaful Product Introduction","Health insurance or takaful products will also be introduced, enabling the rakyat to benefit from services of the private healthcare and Rakan KKM at reasonable prices.",""],[1,"36","5","Nationwide Government Hospital and Clinic Construction and Upgrading","The construction and upgrading of government hospitals and clinics nationwide will also be implemented to provide better healthcare services.",""],[1,"39","6","Healthcare Financing System Reform","Reform of the healthcare financing system will be implemented to provide better services options for the rakyat and ensure inclusive and sustainable national healthcare services.",""],[1,"39","6","Primary Healthcare Strengthening and NCD Prevention","Emphasis will be given on strengthening primary healthcare and prevention of non-communicable diseases (NCDs).",""],[1,"146","6","Health Financing Reform and Service Outsourcing","Government allocation will be optimised by implementing proactive and innovative approaches in health financing, such as through outsourcing of high-value services and diversifying funding sources.",""],[1,"147","7","Health Financing, Governance, and Service Delivery Reform","Health reform will focus on the efforts to improve health financing structure and governance, intensify health promotion and awareness activities as well as strengthen the healthcare services delivery.",""],[1,"147","9","Health Financing System Reform","Health financing system will be reformed to enable the rakyat to access better healthcare services.",""],[1,"147","9","Rakan KKM Expansion","The Rakan KKM initiative will be expanded as an option for private companies and insurance policyholders to obtain paid services at public health facilities.",""],[1,"147","9","Continued Public Health Service Provision for Eligible Target Groups","Eligible target groups will continue to receive quality healthcare services from all public health facilities.",""],[1,"147","10","Standardised Base Health Insurance and Takaful Products","Standardised base health insurance or takaful products managed by the private sector will be introduced to enable the rakyat to access private health and the Rakan KKM services at a reasonable rate.",""],[1,"147","11","National Health Fund and Strategic Purchasing Platform","The establishment of a national health fund and the development of a strategic purchasing platform will be explored in the efforts to modernise the national health financing system.",""],[1,"148","2","Healthcare Service Outsourcing and Public-Private Partnership Expansion","Access to quality healthcare services will be enhanced through the outsourcing of services requiring high investment through more public-private partnerships.",""]],"46":[[1,"148","5","Healthcare Workforce Policy Coordination Committee","A high-level policy coordination committee will be formed to coordinate and monitor the needs of healthcare workforce, involving various related ministries and agencies.",""],[1,"148","5","National Professional Development Framework for Health Human Resources","a national-level professional development framework will be developed to ensure human resource management system is responsive to the needs of the rakyat.",""],[1,"148","5","Precision Medicine Research, Innovation and Commercialisation Upgrade","the health talent capability of the country in precision medicine will be improved by enhancing research, innovation and commercialisation.",""],[1,"148","5","Health Research Institutions Centre of Excellence Strengthening","Health research institutions will be strengthened as centres of excellence for clinical research in the Southeast Asia region to spearhead precision medicine.",""]],"47":[[1,"36","6","Affordable Housing Delivery Programmes","The provision of more quality affordable housing for the low- and middle-income groups in urban areas will be enhanced through the implementation of the Program Residensi MADANI and the Program Residensi Rakyat.",""],[1,"36","6","Rent-to-Own Housing Scheme Expansion","In addition, the rent-to-own scheme will be expanded and existing affordable home financing schemes will be improved to assist less capable rakyat in owning a house.",""],[1,"40","1","Housing Supply, Financing and Regulatory Reform","Housing reform will focus on increasing the supply of quality, liveable and inclusive houses, improving access to financing as well as strengthening the efficiency of housing regulation and management.",""],[1,"40","1","Smart and Sustainable Cities Development","The development of smart and sustainable cities will be strengthened to ensure an inclusive urbanisation process and meet the needs of the rakyat.",""],[1,"40","1","Kota MADANI Integrated Urban Development Project","the Kota MADANI in Putrajaya will be developed as a pioneer model for the future urban development, providing social amenities and economic opportunities within an integrated ecosystem.",""],[1,"149","7","Affordable Housing Construction Programme","This commitment is realised through the implementation of various strategies and initiatives, including the construction of affordable housing that fulfils humane needs, maintenance programmes, provision of funds and financing incentives as well as improvement of housing management.",""],[1,"149","7","Housing Maintenance Programme","This commitment is realised through the implementation of various strategies and initiatives, including the construction of affordable housing that fulfils humane needs, maintenance programmes, provision of funds and financing incentives as well as improvement of housing management.",""],[1,"149","7","Housing Finance Incentives and Funding Support","This commitment is realised through the implementation of various strategies and initiatives, including the construction of affordable housing that fulfils humane needs, maintenance programmes, provision of funds and financing incentives as well as improvement of housing management.",""],[1,"149","7","Housing Management Improvement Initiative","This commitment is realised through the implementation of various strategies and initiatives, including the construction of affordable housing that fulfils humane needs, maintenance programmes, provision of funds and financing incentives as well as improvement of housing management.",""],[1,"150","1","Housing Reform for Affordable Homeownership","During the Thirteenth Plan period, housing reform aims to enhance the sustainability of the housing ecosystem in providing liveable, quality and inclusive homes that are affordable for all segments of society.",""],[1,"150","1","Rent-to-Own Housing Finance and Ownership Model","A shift in focus towards a new financing and ownership model based on rent- to-own (RTO) will enhance the ability of the rakyat to own houses.",""],[1,"150","7","Housing Reform for Affordable and Inclusive Housing","This reform will focus on efforts in increasing the supply of quality, liveable and inclusive housing, enhancing access to financing as well as strengthening the housing regulatory and management effeciency.",""],[1,"150","8","Quality Housing Provision Improvement","The provision of quality housing for the rakyat will be increased through improvements in planning, restructuring of governance and enhancement of construction methods as well as the optimal use",""],[1,"151","1","National Affordable Housing Reform","This housing reform aims to provide one million affordable houses within 10 years.",""],[1,"151","4","Affordable Housing Provision and Urban Renewal Redevelopment","the provision of affordable housing.",""],[1,"151","5","Expansion of the Rent-to-Own Housing Scheme","Home ownership approach through the RTO scheme will be expanded to provide opportunities for households lacking initial deposit and ineligible to obtain commercial financing.",""],[1,"151","5","Flexible Rent-to-Own Housing Scheme Model","A new model of the RTO scheme will be introduced to establish a mechanism to provide a more flexible and affordable rental system.",""],[1,"151","6","Affordable Home Financing Scheme Improvement","Existing affordable home financing schemes will be improved, including in terms of setting interest rates at certain interval and financing periods which will enable more target groups to purchase a first home.",""],[1,"153","2","State Affordable Housing Price Control Policy","State governments will be encouraged to implement price control on affordable houses through the state housing policy to ensure that the selling prices are in line with household incomes and local needs.",""],[1,"153","2","Public Housing Project Empowerment and Bulk Procurement Mechanism","state governments will be empowered to implement public housing projects, including through the introduction of a bulk public housing procurement mechanism.",""],[1,"153","2","Public Housing Fund Enhancement","the existing housing fund, the Kumpulan Wang Amanah Program Perumahan Rakyat Dimiliki will be improved.",""]],"48":[[1,"92","4","Strengthening of the National TVET Council","The National TVET Council was strengthened to serve as the sole coordinator in the development of TVET talent, in line with the aspirations of the Ekonomi MADANI.",""],[1,"92","4","National TVET Policy 2030","The National TVET Policy 2030 was introduced in 2024 as an effort to strengthen the TVET ecosystem and ensure TVET institutions offer programmes that meet industry needs.",""],[1,"92","4","Malaysia Skills Management Integration System","the Sistem Pengurusan Integrasi Kemahiran Malaysia was developed to integrate TVET data across various ministries as well as enable streamlining of student admission applications through one channel and implementation of a single rating system for TVET programmes.",""],[1,"96","3","Establishment of the TVET Commission","TVET governance will be strengthened by establishing the TVET Commission as a dedicated entity to regulate TVET institutions and monitor strategies and initiatives under the National TVET Policy.",""],[1,"96","3","TVET Act Formulation Study","A study to formulate a TVET act will also be conducted to improve TVET governance.",""],[1,"96","3","Expansion of Malaysian Skills Certification Levels","The expansion of skill certification levels under the Malaysian Skills Certification System will be implemented by amending the National Skills Development Act 2006 [Act 652] in elevating TVET to be on par with the academic pathway in the national higher education system.",""],[1,"96","5","TVET Programme Strengthening and Expansion","TVET programmes will be strengthened in line with the industry needs.",""],[1,"96","5","Public-Industry TVET Collaboration and Instructor Upskilling","Thus, collaboration between public TVET institutions and the industry will be intensified through sharing of expertise and latest technologies, including AI and curriculum development as well as upskilling and reskilling programmes for TVET instructors.",""]],"49":[[1,"94","5","Compulsory Preschool Education Reform","Early childhood education or preschool will be made compulsory at the age of five to optimise early cognitive development.",""],[1,"94","5","Mandatory National Preschool Curriculum Adoption","The adoption of the national curriculum for preschool education, which emphasises the inculcation of karamah insaniah values, character building, critical thinking and life skills will be made compulsory to all institutions of early childhood education.",""],[1,"94","5","Strengthening of Education Act Enforcement","In this regard, the enforcement of the Education Act 1996 [Act 550] will be strengthened.",""],[1,"94","5","Primary School Entry Age Reform","Primary education will begin at the age of six, in line with international practices.",""],[1,"94","5","Expanded Language Learning in Primary Schools","the learning of an additional language will be expanded in primary schools to enhance language proficiency in early schooling years.",""],[1,"94","5","Enhanced School Curriculum Reform","The school curriculum will be enhanced with the emphasis on the aspects of nationhood, socioemotional, fundamental literacy skills and digital, in addition to entrepreneurship, finance and sustainability.",""],[1,"94","6","Nationwide Expansion of Special Educational Needs Education","The availability of education for students with special educational needs will be expanded nationwide, from preschool to secondary level.",""],[1,"94","6","School Hours and Specialised School Effectiveness Studies","Studies will be conducted to determine the optimal school hours, assess the effectiveness of specialised schools as well as improve the educational model for gifted and talented students in enhancing overall education outcomes.",""],[1,"109","2","Inclusive Compulsory Education Support","Efforts will be intensified to ensure that all children, including those with special needs are able to complete compulsory education in a fair and equitable manner.",""]],"50":[[1,"95","3","Teacher Recruitment Mechanism Enhancement","The mechanism for recruitment of teachers will be enhanced to secure the best teaching talent from various sources.",""],[1,"95","3","Continuous Professional Development Programme for Teachers","A continuous professional development programme for teachers, akin to practices in other professions will be introduced to ensure teachers are competent and equipped with the latest knowledge in line with current needs.",""],[1,"95","4","Primary School Teacher Multi-Subject Training","Primary school teachers will be trained to be capable of teaching all foundation subjects for level one students.",""],[1,"95","4","Cross-Placement and Mobility Feasibility Study for Educators","A study will be undertaken to assess the feasibility of cross-placement and -mobility of various professions to enhance competencies of educators and secure the best talent.",""],[1,"95","4","Teacher Promotion System Review","The promotion system for teachers will be reviewed to provide a more competitive career pathway, on par with other professions.",""]],"51":[[1,"94","7","Mandatory Paid Internship Scheme","A mandatory paid internship scheme will be introduced to improve graduate outcomes.",""],[1,"95","1","Demand-Driven Learning Model Expansion","The demand driven-based learning model will be expanded by increasing collaboration between public universities and the private sector through certification of skills and work experience.",""],[1,"95","2","Graduate Outcome Assessment","a new graduate outcome assessment will be introduced to address skills and competency mismatches, thereby curbing graduate underemployment issues.",""]],"52":[[1,"32","2","Future-Ready Talent Development Across the Learning Continuum","The development of future-ready talent across the learning continuum will be intensified to produce creative and innovative skilled talent in accelerating economic transformation.",""],[1,"32","2","STEM and Digital Skills Exposure in Primary Education","This talent will be nurtured as early as at the primary school level by giving exposure to Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics (STEM) -based activities as well as digital skills, including AI.",""],[1,"32","2","Industry-Aligned Higher Education Programme Strengthening","Academic programmes in higher education institutions will be strengthened in line with industrial needs, particularly for the HGHV industries and high-impact strategic sectors.",""],[1,"32","2","TVET Mainstreaming for Industrial Talent Needs","TVET programmes will also be mainstreamed to support industrial talent needs, including in strategic investment locations.",""],[1,"32","2","Academy in Industry Programme Intensification","The implementation of the Academy in Industry (ADI) programme will be intensified to increase local workforce participation and certification.",""],[1,"34","4","Education and TVET Investment for Settlement Communities","The competitiveness of communities in settlement areas of the Federal Land Development Authority (FELDA) and the Federal Land Consolidation and Rehabilitation Authority (FELCRA) as well as the regional development authorities (LKWs), will be increased through investment in education and TVET, particularly for the second and third generations.",""],[1,"36","6","Targeted Education Fee, Tuition and Scholarship Assistance","Access to education and skills development, including TVET, will continue to be strengthened through targeted assistance on fee, tuition and scholarship to ensure students from low-income groups remain in the learning continuum.",""],[1,"36","6","Education Loan Scheme Review","The education loan schemes will be reviewed to be more targeted, focused and sustainable.",""],[1,"37","4","Education Reform to Improve Learning Outcomes","Education reform will serve as the backbone in instilling humane aspects, encompassing insaniah and ethical values as well as social and societal relations.",""],[1,"37","4","Compulsory Preschool Education at Age Five","In this regard, preschool education will be made compulsory at the age of five, while primary education will begin at the age of six.",""],[1,"37","4","Mandatory National Preschool Curriculum","The adoption of the national preschool curriculum will be made mandatory for all early childhood education institutions.",""],[1,"37","4","Expanded English and Additional Language Instruction in Primary Schools","In addition, in primary schools, the English language will be part of the language of learning and communication for level one students and the learning of additional languages will be expanded.",""],[1,"37","4","STEM and TVET Learning Promotion","Focus will also be given to encourage learning in STEM and TVET streams as an alternative pathway for students.",""],[1,"39","1","Teacher Recruitment and Continuous Professional Development Programme","The competency and efficiency of educators will be enhanced through improvement in the mechanism for recruitment of teachers from various open sources as well as introduction of a continuous teaching professional development programme.",""],[1,"39","1","Teacher Promotion System Revision and Career Mobility Study","In addition, the revision of promotion system for teachers and a feasibility study on cross-placement and -mobility between various professions will be conducted to provide a more competitive career pathway.",""],[1,"39","1","Education Governance Restructuring","The restructuring of roles and functions of agencies will be implemented to centralise education governance of preschool to secondary school, as well as pre-university to higher education in improving effectiveness of education delivery.",""],[1,"39","1","Early Childhood Education Act and Alternative Education Regulation","Measures will be undertaken to enact a new act related to early childhood education, strengthen the regulatory mechanism for alternative education and implement a pilot project in granting autonomy to universities.",""],[1,"39","1","Education Facilities and Sponsorship Investment Increase","Investment in education will also be increased to improve educational facilities and sponsorship.",""],[1,"45","2","Education Reform for Social Mobility","Under this pillar, focus will be given on the efforts to reform education and labour market, strengthen inclusive development from multidimensional perspectives, improve the socioeconomic level of the target groups as well as balance economic progress between regions and strengthen rural development.",""],[1,"45","2","Labour Market Reform for High-Value Transition","Labour market reform aims to support the structural transition to a high-value economy and subsequently increase salaries and wages towards achieving a decent living.",""],[1,"74","1","Skilled and Future-Proof Talent Development","Measures will also be undertaken to enhance the development of skilled and future-proof talent as well as ensure better governance.",""]],"53":[[1,"96","2","Lifelong Learning Strengthening Initiative","Lifelong learning (LLL) will be strengthened in preparation towards Malaysia becoming an aged nation by 2043.",""],[1,"96","2","Third Age University Lifelong Learning Programme","Older persons in the third age will be offered LLL programmes through the Third Age University concept.",""],[1,"96","2","Public Facility-Based Lifelong Learning Initiatives","Public facilities such as sports centres and libraries will also be utilised for the implementation of LLL initiatives, including self-learning and peer-to-peer learning to optimise usage of resources.",""],[1,"96","2","Lifelong Learning Governance Mainstreaming Reform","the related governance will be improved to mainstream LLL as an integral part of the national education system.",""],[1,"144","2","Lifelong Learning Programmes for Older Persons","Efforts to enhance the wellbeing of older persons were expanded through lifelong learning programmes at health clinics, benefitting 41,400 older persons from 2021 to 2024.",""],[1,"145","5","Education System Modernization for an Aging Society","Education will be strengthened in preparation for an aged nation, which requires changes in content, method and learning processes.",""],[1,"145","5","Dynamic Curriculum Improvement","Educational syllabus will be improved to be more dynamic in considering the need for changes in the future.",""],[1,"145","5","Expanded TVET Curriculum for Ageing-Related Fields","Skills development will be intensified and the TVET curriculum will be expanded to include ageing-related fields.",""],[1,"145","5","Flexible Lifelong Learning and Upskilling Programme","In addition, lifelong learning will be enriched through wider access to and opportunities for flexible training programmes, such as micro-credentials, recognition of prior learning as well as upskilling and reskilling to increase career mobility.",""]],"54":[[1,"147","7","Health Digitalisation Improvement Initiative","Focus will also be given on efforts to improve health digitalisation",""],[1,"149","3","Digital Health Information Sharing Platform","A digital health information sharing platform will be developed to enable either public or private healthcare services providers across institutions and states to deliver quality services to the rakyat.",""],[1,"149","3","Outsourced Electronic Medical Record System for Government Health Facilities","In addition, outsourcing of the electronic medical record system by all government health facilities will further improve the management of health information of the rakyat through the usage of big data, artificial intelligence (AI) and emerging technologies.",""]],"55":[[1,"46","1","GovTech Mainstreaming Initiative","mainstream the GovTech and enhance good governance.",""],[1,"135","1","Public Service Digitalisation Reform","During the Thirteenth Plan period, the public service reform will be continued by mainstreaming digitalisation in ensuring the public sector is more dynamic, progressive and pragmatic towards a digital government to meet the needs of the rakyat and business community.",""],[1,"135","1","ILTIZAM-Based Service Delivery Improvement","In this regard, focus will be given on improving service delivery based on the ILTIZAM principles",""],[1,"135","1","GovTech and Advanced Technology Mainstreaming","strengthening the GovTech by mainstreaming advanced technologies, including Al.",""]],"56":[[1,"142","7","Inclusive Sports Participation Promotion","all segments of society, including children, youth, women, persons with disabilities (PWDs) and older persons will also be encouraged to participate in sports activities.",""],[1,"143","1","Community Sports and Fitness Participation Programme","NGOs and communities will be empowered with bigger roles in organising various sports and fitness activities.",""],[1,"143","1","Sports Facility Access Expansion Initiative","Access to sports facilities will also be expanded by ensuring the facilities are of quality and available to all segments of society, particularly in the rural areas.",""]],"57":[[1,"143","3","National Athlete Excellence Enhancement Measures","Measures to enhance the excellence of national athletes at the international level will continue to be intensified in boosting the image of the country and thus fostering a sense of pride among the rakyat.",""],[1,"143","3","Sports Training Centre Modernisation","More sports training centres will be equipped with modern facilities, enabling athletes to be trained in various disciplines and specialisations using training modules based on the latest sports science and technology.",""],[1,"143","3","High-Performance Athlete Training Management Reform","The training management of high-performing athletes will be improved by providing flexibility for athletes to personally choose coaches, training venues, competition types and sports science support modules.",""],[1,"143","3","2027 SEA Games Hosting Leveraging Initiative","The hosting of the 2027 Southeast Asian (SEA) Games in Malaysia will be leveraged to enhance the national excellence as well as expand involvement of society in sports and voluntary activities.",""]],"58":[[1,"63","2","Domestic Sports Industry Development Initiative","Efforts will be intensified to develop the domestic sports industry as a new source of economic growth.",""],[1,"63","2","Sports Industry Financing and Incentives Support","These initiatives include developing a supportive ecosystem for sports industry, such as access to better financing and incentives as well as introducing 'Made by Malaysia' sports products in the global market.",""],[1,"63","2","Sports Product and Service R&D Scaling","The R&D&C&I activities will be scaled up to increase the development of competitive and high-value sports products and services.",""]],"59":[[1,"40","2","Centralised Waste Management Coordination Agency","In addition, centralised coordination of waste management under a dedicated agency will be explored.",""]],"60":[[1,"69","1","Strengthened Fisheries Enforcement and Fisheries Act Amendment","The enforcement of the Fisheries Act 1985 [Act 317] will be tightened to curb illegal and excessive fishing activities, particularly in the South China Sea.",""],[1,"69","1","Expansion of the Tagal or Tagang Inland Fisheries System","The tagal or tagang system practiced in Sabah and Sarawak will be expanded to the Peninsular Malaysia to ensure sustainability of inland fisheries resources.",""],[1,"69","1","Island Waste Management and Coastal Cleaning Partnerships","Strategic collaborations with the private sector, non-governmental organisations (NGOs) and local communities will continue to be strengthened in the implementation of programmes on waste management and recycling on islands as well as coastal cleaning.",""],[1,"69","1","Sustainable Tourism Amenities Technology Adoption","Efforts will also be intensified to encourage providers of tourism amenities and facilities in adopting the latest technology to manage energy, water and waste sustainably.",""]],"61":[[1,"6","5","Environmental Sustainability Commitments","This development agenda will also uphold the environmental sustainability commitments, symbolising the bonding and pledge of the nation to protect the earth as entrusted by the God and the future generations.",""],[1,"40","2","Climate Change and Environmental Management Enhancement","Efforts will continue to be enhanced to safeguard the planetary health, among others by improving climate change and environmental management, strengthening flood mitigation and adaptation as well as preserving and conserving biodiversity.",""]],"62":[[1,"32","5","Circular Economy Compliance and Waste Management Improvement","In addition, the implementation mechanism of the circular economy will be improved by encouraging compliance to ESG principles, particularly through plastic sustainability as well as the management of scheduled and solid wastes.",""],[1,"40","2","Circular Economy and Waste Management Strengthening","The implementation of the circular economy will be invigorated and waste management will be strengthened through improvement in policy, enhancement of regulation and implementation mechanisms as well as provision of modern infrastructure.",""],[1,"40","2","Waste-to-Energy Plant Expansion through Public-Private Partnerships","The construction of waste-to-energy plants will be expanded through public-private partnerships to support the policy of prohibiting the opening of new landfill sites.",""],[1,"40","2","5R Waste Management Promotion","Alternative method for waste management using the refuse, reduce, reuse, recycle and recovery (5R) approach will also be promoted.",""],[1,"157","1","Circular Economy Implementation","enable the implementation of sustainable economic activities.",""],[1,"159","6","Circular Economy and Waste Management Strengthening","Efforts to enhance the circular economy and improve waste management will be intensified by strengthening policies, regulations and implementation mechanisms as well as providing modern infrastructure.",""],[1,"159","6","Circular Economy Legislation Across Sectors","Legislation related to the circular economy across sectors will be enacted to regulate activities along the value chain, from production to disposal.",""],[1,"159","6","Circular Economy Adoption Support Measures","In addition, mechanisms for the adoption of the circular economy will be improved, comprising sustainable plastics, management of biomass and scheduled waste, development of local sustainable aviation fuel and the expansion of extended producer responsibility.",""],[1,"159","6","Food Waste Treatment Financing and Tax Incentives","Blended financing and appropriate tax incentives to encourage food waste treatment at source will also be expanded to include commercial, industrial and institutional sectors.",""],[1,"177","3","Private Sector Sustainable Production and Consumption Practices","The private sector adopts sustainable production and consumption practices, including investing in low-carbon technologies, increasing the use of renewable energy as well as embracing the circular economy concept to protect planetary health.",""]],"63":[[1,"159","1","Environmental and Chemical Management Enforcement Strengthening","Measures to preserve environment will be enhanced by strengthening and enforcing legislation related to environment and chemical management.",""],[1,"159","1","Environmental Quality Act Regulatory Review","Regulations under the Environmental Quality Act 1974 [Act 127] will be reviewed to improve enforcement efficiency.",""],[1,"159","1","Greywater Management Legislation and Awareness Programme","Existing legislation and awareness programmes related to greywater management at premises of discharge will be strengthened.",""],[1,"159","1","Integrated Chemical Life-Cycle Monitoring System","An integrated management system will be developed to monitor the full life cycle of chemicals, starting from the point of entry into the country or local production to disposal.",""],[1,"159","1","Stockholm and Minamata Convention Ratification Basis","These initiatives will be the basis for Malaysia to ratify the Stockholm Convention and the Minamata Convention in reducing negative impacts on human health and the environment.",""]],"64":[[1,"33","2","Agricultural Sector Intensification for Food Supply Security","The development of the agriculture sector will be intensified to ensure food supply security and the production of high-value agricultural commodities.",""],[1,"33","2","Large-Scale Agrofood Production Expansion","Large-scale agrofood production, including paddy cultivation will be increased through improvement in irrigation and drainage system, implemented through PPP.",""],[1,"33","2","Livestock, Vegetable, and Fruit Productivity Enhancement","The production of livestock products, vegetables and fruits will be enhanced by developing quality crop varieties and breeds as well as animal feed.",""],[1,"33","2","Agricommody Competitiveness and Sustainability Certification Reform","In addition, the competitiveness of the agricommodity subsector will be strengthened by improving local sustainability certification standards for palm oil, rubber and timber as well as introducing standards for kenaf, cocoa and pepper.",""],[1,"33","2","Smallholder Rubber and Oil Palm Replanting Expansion","Rubber and oil palm replanting by smallholders will be expanded to increase productivity and income.",""],[1,"35","2","Import Substitution and Local Production Expansion","Efforts will be amplified to reduce reliance on imported goods by increasing local production.",""],[1,"35","3","Domestic Food Production Expansion","the production of paddy and other food crops, fisheries and livestock will be increased to improve the self-sufficiency ratio of the nation",""],[1,"39","5","Food Security Strengthening Measures","Food security will be fortified by boosting local food production, diversifying countries of import sources and strengthening the food supply chain.",""],[1,"39","5","Nutritious Food Access and Child Malnutrition Reduction","Efforts will also be focused on increasing access to nutritious and balanced food to improve the health of the rakyat and address malnutrition issues, particularly among children.",""],[1,"45","1","Food Security Strengthening Initiative","Priority will also be given to fortify food security, strengthen flood mitigation and adaptation, improve the availability of public transport infrastructure as well as empower MSMEs and the third sector.",""],[1,"50","1","Food Security Strengthening Measures","In raising the floor, efforts will also be focused, among others, on strengthening of food security.",""],[1,"58","1","Agrofood and Agricommodity Subsector Acceleration Programme","The development of agrofood and agricommodity subsectors will be accelerated by focusing on efforts to increase high-value production, productivity and technology adoption, intensify R&D&C&I as well as expand markets.",""],[1,"58","1","Large-Scale High-Value Farming Promotion","Large-scale farming of high-value products such as durian, pineapple, seaweed, bird's nest, floriculture and ornamental fish will be encouraged to meet market demand.",""],[1,"58","1","Agro-Based Product Diversification and Innovation Partnership","efforts to diversify agro-based products will be intensified through strategic collaboration with the private sector and universities to increase innovation in producing high-value products.",""],[1,"58","2","Integrated Infrastructure and Targeted Performance-Based Incentives","Focus will be given on providing integrated infrastructure and improving the provision of incentives to be more targeted and based on performance to enhance implementation effectiveness.",""],[1,"58","2","Smart Farming Technology Expansion","Efforts to enhance productivity through smart farming will be expanded by adopting modern technologies, such as internet of things, drones and big data analytics.",""],[1,"58","2","Food Processing Technology Adoption","The adoption of technologies, which include rapid freezing, retort sterilisation and high-pressure processing will be increased to produce safe and quality food products.",""],[1,"58","2","Robotic Technology Pilot in Oil Palm Plantations","the use of robotic technology in oil palm plantations to reduce dependency on foreign workers will be implemented on a pilot basis.",""],[1,"58","3","Agricultural R&D and Commercialisation Support","Investment in R&D&C&I to produce agricultural inputs that are resilient to diseases and weather conditions as well as high-yield will be increased through collaboration with industry.",""],[1,"58","4","Export Trial Initiatives and Targeted Promotion Programme","export trial initiatives and targeted promotions will be implemented to explore and expand international markets.",""],[1,"58","5","Agricommodity Replanting Programme Expansion","The agricommodity replanting programmes, particularly for oil palm and rubber smallholders, will be expanded to increase productivity and income of smallholders, as well as the export value of the nation.",""],[1,"58","5","Agricultural Waste Circular Economy Utilization","In addition, to strengthen the implementation of circular economy, focus will be given in leveraging the use of agricultural waste within the agricommodity subsector value chain such as oil palm fronds, empty fruit bunches, fallen rubber leaves and cocoa pods.",""],[1,"58","5","Biomass Value-Added Technology and Innovation Initiative","In this regard, the use of technology and innovation in producing high-value products from biomass such as bioenergy, biocomposites, biopellets and compost fertiliser will be intensified.",""],[1,"58","5","ESG Adoption Strengthening for Agricommodity Industry","The adoption of environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles among industry players will be strengthened to ensure sustainable, resilient, and ethical development of the sector in line with global requirements.",""],[1,"66","2","Greening the Agricommodity Supply Chain","Focus will be given to greening the agricommodity supply chain to increase the competitiveness of Malaysian products in the global market and safeguard the domestic market ecosystem.",""],[1,"66","2","Improved Sustainability Certification Standards for Agricommodities","Local standards for sustainability certification will be improved for palm oil, rubber and timber, and sustainability certification for other agricommodity products such as kenaf, cocoa and pepper will be introduced.",""],[1,"66","2","Agricommodity Supply Chain Traceability Initiative","Efforts to increase the traceability of agricommodity products along the supply chain will be implemented through the usage of advanced technology.",""],[1,"66","2","Environmental Sustainability Mechanism for Imported Agricommodities","a mechanism to set the environmental sustainability of imported agricommodity products will be developed to ensure resilience of downstream industries.",""],[1,"71","2","Food Security Strengthening Strategy","During the Thirteenth Plan period, focus will be given to strengthen food security in ensuring the nation is safeguarded against any supply shocks and disruptions.",""],[1,"71","2","Food Production Capacity Expansion","efforts will be intensified to ensure food production capacity is increased",""],[1,"71","2","Safe and Nutritious Food Supply Access Initiative","food supply accessible by the rakyat is safe and nutritious.",""],[1,"71","3","Large-Scale Food Production Hub Development","a stretch of corridor in the east coast states of the Peninsular Malaysia as well as in Sabah and Sarawak will be developed as food production hubs",""],[1,"71","3","Paddy Cultivation Intensification through Public-Private Partnerships","Efforts to increase paddy cultivation will continue to be intensified through the implementation of public- private partnership programmes, such as in the Muda area of Kedah and Perlis.",""],[1,"71","4","Irrigation and Drainage Infrastructure Improvement","comprehensive infrastructure development, including improvements to irrigation and drainage system as well as the application of smart farming.",""],[1,"71","4","Smart Farming Application","comprehensive infrastructure development, including improvements to irrigation and drainage system as well as the application of smart farming.",""],[1,"71","5","Agricultural R&D, Smart Farming, and Technology Transfer Initiative","The productivity and quality of production will be improved by intensifying R&D&C&I activities and smart farming through collaborations among farmers, research institutions and industries.",""],[1,"71","5","Alternative Food Crop R&D Promotion","The use of underutilised crops, such as tubers, legumes and high-protein plants, as alternative food sources will be explored by encouraging more R&D&C&I activities.",""],[1,"71","6","National Agri-Food Empowerment Programme","Efforts to increase the SSR of food commodities will continue to be intensified through the implementation of several main programmes such as the Program Pemerkasaan Agromakanan Negara, the Program Agropreneur Nextgen and the Program Pengganda30.",""],[1,"71","6","Targeted Incentives for Young Agropreneurs","In this regard, more young agropreneurs will be mobilised to participate in large-scale and modern agricultural activities through the provision of more targeted incentives.",""],[1,"71","7","Food Import Source Diversification Policy","The security of food supply will be enhanced through the diversification of import sources and the strengthening of risk management.",""],[1,"72","1","Food Safety Import Control Strengthening","which include import permits and certification as well as inspection at entry points, will be strengthened to address food safety risks.",""],[1,"72","1","Cross-Border Food Safety Cooperation","collaboration with the authorities of exporting countries will be intensified",""],[1,"72","1","Agricultural Supply Chain Efficiency and Post-Harvest Loss Reduction","Focus will also be given towards efforts in addressing post-harvest losses issues through efficiency enhancement along the supply chain, encompassing methods in harvesting, storing and transporting agricultural produce.",""],[1,"72","2","Strengthened Enforcement of Import Regulations","Enforcement of existing import regulations, including those under the Food Act 1983 [Act 281], the Malaysian Quarantine and Inspection Services Act 2011 [Act 728] as well as the Plant Quarantine Act 1976 [Act 167] will be increased.",""],[1,"72","2","Strengthening of Food Security Agency Roles","The roles of agencies involved in food security encompassing production, price control, logistics, marketing and safety will be strengthened to ensure the national food supply is sufficient.",""],[1,"72","2","Targeted Agricultural Disaster Protection Scheme","A targeted agricultural disaster protection scheme will be introduced to reduce losses due to disasters.",""],[1,"72","2","Agricultural Insurance Partnership Exploration","Strategic collaboration with private insurance providers will be explored to ensure operators of various agricultural activities are provided with maximum coverage.",""],[1,"72","3","Food Supply Chain Strengthening Programme","The food supply chain will be strengthened through improvements in infrastructure, enhancement of the retail sector, establishment of platforms for price transparency and comprehensive enforcement of regulation.",""],[1,"72","3","Agrofood Marketing Hubs Expansion","The availability of marketing infrastructure, encompassing collection, processing, packaging and distribution centres, as well as logistics facilities and digital services, will be increased through collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"72","3","Real-Time Price and Supply Repository System","In addition, a price and supply repository system will be developed to provide information in real-time to ensure price transparency along the supply chain.",""],[1,"72","4","Competition Law Enforcement Intensification Using Data Repository","Act 2011 [Act 723] and the Competition Act 2010 [Act 712] will be intensified by leveraging data from this repository to curb price manipulation activities.",""]],"65":[[1,"25","6","AI-Enabled Precision Agriculture and Weather Forecasting","AI can be applied for high-precision crop monitoring, real-time weather forecasting and planning for more sustainable resource utilisation.",""],[1,"25","6","Robotic Technology Deployment in Oil Palm Plantations","The deployment of robotic technology in oil palm plantations will improve productivity and reduce dependency on foreign workers.",""],[1,"33","2","Advanced Technology Adoption in Capture Fisheries and Aquaculture","The capture fisheries and aquaculture industries will also be enhanced through the adoption of advanced technologies, including AI.",""]],"66":[[1,"56","1","Creative Industries Strengthening","the development of high impact strategic sectors will emphasise efforts to expand the air transport industry as well as strengthen the tourism, halal and creative industries.",""],[1,"61","4","Local Creative Industry Ecosystem Strengthening","The local creative industry ecosystem will be strengthened to enhance competitiveness of the orange economy through the production of creative works with high commercial value.",""],[1,"61","5","Creative Talent Development and TVET Collaboration","the development of highly skilled and dynamic creative talent aligned with technological changes will be enhanced, including through collaboration with TVET institutions to meet market demand.",""],[1,"61","5","Private Sector-Driven Financing Support for Creative Industry Growth","Private sector-driven financing will also be improved to support the industry growth.",""],[1,"61","5","Integrated Creative Industry Value Chain Coordination","An integrated approach through collaboration with all stakeholders will be intensified to strengthen the entire creative industry value chain.",""]],"67":[[1,"56","4","Natural Gas Roadmap Implementation","The Natural Gas Roadmap will be implemented to ensure supply security, optimise the value of domestic natural gas resources as well as increase private investment.",""],[1,"56","4","ASEAN Gas Trade and Infrastructure Cooperation","among the initiatives that will be undertaken include strengthening cooperation in trade and infrastructure development with the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) member states to achieve the aim of positioning Malaysia as a leading regional gas trading hub.",""],[1,"56","4","Third Regasification Terminal Construction","Construction of the third regasification terminal will begin in 2026 and is expected to commence operation in 2027 to meet the increasing demand for natural gas in the Peninsular Malaysia.",""],[1,"56","4","National and Regional Natural Gas Governance Coordination","planning, development and governance of the natural gas industry at national and regional levels will be coordinated.",""]],"68":[[1,"36","7","Rural Basic Utilities Expansion","The provision of basic utilities, such as clean water supply, electricity and broadband coverage in rural areas will also be expanded.",""]],"69":[[1,"109","4","Youth Economic Empowerment and Wellbeing Enhancement","Youth development will be focused on the aspects of economic empowerment and wellbeing enhancement as well as shaping future youth to build capable and competitive successive generations in increasing social mobility.",""],[1,"109","4","Youth Participation in Strategic Economic Sectors","Efforts will be intensified to increase youth involvement in strategic economic sectors, including",""],[1,"109","5","Skills Development Programmes for Future-Ready Talent","skills development programmes will be enhanced to provide future-ready talent.",""],[1,"109","5","Micro-Credential Career Development Support","career development opportunities will be strengthened with the assurance of micro- credential programmes to enable youth to increase skills while working.",""],[1,"109","5","Youth Entrepreneurship and Business Participation Initiative","Youth participation in entrepreneurship and business will be enhanced to provide new job opportunities for the community.",""],[1,"109","7","Youth Tracer Initiative","A youth tracer initiative will be introduced as a focused intervention mechanism in identifying and providing comprehensive support to youth at transition phases4",""]],"70":[[1,"110","1","Youth Leadership Capacity Building and Advocacy Training Programme","Youth leadership will be strengthened through the implementation of capacity building and public policy programmes, advocacy training as well as involvement in community-based initiatives to produce credible, progressive and value-based successive leaders.",""],[1,"110","1","Rakan Muda Time Bank Initiative","The Rakan Muda time bank initiative will be explored as an innovative approach in fostering volunteerism, enhancing skills and expanding social networks among youth.",""]],"71":[[1,"110","2","Gender Impact Assessment and Gender Audit System","gender impact assessment in national development will be implemented, and gender audit evaluation of high impact programmes and projects will be introduced to mainstream equitable access and active participation, particularly for women.",""],[1,"110","2","National Action Plan on Women, Peace and Security","A national action plan on women, peace and security will be developed, particularly to protect women in the defence, security and public safety sectors.",""],[1,"110","2","Women Workforce Participation Recognition System","The star rating system will be expanded to recognise private companies that encourage and retain women participation in the workforce.",""],[1,"110","2","Women Leadership Academy and Support Hub","the leadership capacity and capability of women will be enhanced through the introduction of academy and hub for empowerment, mentoring, advancement and support for women.",""]],"72":[[1,"45","1","Public Transport Infrastructure Expansion","Priority will also be given to fortify food security, strengthen flood mitigation and adaptation, improve the availability of public transport infrastructure as well as empower MSMEs and the third sector.",""],[1,"80","5","Public Transport Infrastructure Improvement","Improved availability of transport infrastructure will enhance the efficiency, viability and reliability of public transport services.",""],[1,"80","5","Public Transport Fare and Cost Review","In addition, the review of fares and costs will improve the financial sustainability of public transport operators.",""],[1,"80","5","Modal Shift to Public Transport","The shift from usage of private vehicles to public transport will reduce the carbon footprint and fiscal burden of the Government.",""],[1,"80","6","Public Transport Service Improvement Measures","During the Twelfth Plan period, public transport services continued to show improvement, resulting from the implementation of various strategies and initiatives that focused on mobility of the rakyat.",""],[1,"80","6","Electric and Diesel Bus Procurement","Public transport services was further improved through the additional procurement of 250 electric buses and 310 diesel buses during the period from 2024 to 2025.",""],[1,"80","6","Demand-Responsive Transit Expansion","the Demand-Responsive Transit (DRT) services, which was introduced in 2022 was expanded to cover over 33 zones in the Klang Valley with 300 vans in 2025.",""],[1,"80","7","Public Transport Fare Support and Concession Passes","Efforts to encourage the usage of public transport services were continued through the sales of 2.7 million MY50 travel passes and introduction of special passes for students and persons with disabilities for the Shuttle Timuran as well as the KTM Komuter in the Klang Valley and northern sectors.",""],[1,"81","1","Stage Bus Service Transformation Scheme","continuation of the Stage Bus Service Transformation Scheme.",""],[1,"81","7","Public Transport Service Improvement and Rail Governance Reform","Focus will be given to efforts in reducing dependency of operators on the Government funding, accelerating transit oriented development (TOD), improving infrastructure and support facilities as well as enhancing efficiency of rail governance and operations.",""],[1,"81","8","Public Transport Fare Review Mechanism","a review mechanism to set appropriate public transport fares will be identified based on the study findings of the Pelan Strategik Pengangkutan Awam Lembah Klang.",""],[1,"81","8","Special Electricity Tariff for Public Transport","the introduction of special electricity tariffs for public transport will be explored to reduce operational costs.",""],[1,"81","9","Transit-Oriented Development Implementation Acceleration","The implementation of TOD will be accelerated through strategic collaboration between public transport operators and the private sector in potential areas.",""],[1,"82","1","Public Transport Infrastructure Expansion","Investment in public transport infrastructure and facilities will be increased to expand public transport network and improve comfort of users.",""],[1,"82","1","Klang Valley Rail Network Completion","The construction of public transport infrastructure to complete the rail network in high-density areas in the Klang Valley will be continued towards achieving the target of 40% modal share in 2030.",""],[1,"82","1","LRT3 Rail Project Completion","In this regard, the LRT3 project with 37 kilometres of rail network will be completed during the Thirteenth Plan period.",""],[1,"82","1","ECRL and RTS Link Operationalisation","the integration and expansion of the public transport network will be enhanced through the operationalisation of the ECRL and the Rapid Transit System (RTS) Link, expected to be completed during the Thirteenth Plan period.",""],[1,"82","1","Passenger Train Leasing Expansion","The number of passenger trains will be increased through leasing arrangements to optimise rail track capacity and improve mobility of the rakyat.",""],[1,"82","2","First- and Last-Mile Public Transport Connectivity Improvement","The first- and last-mile connectivity will also be improved to be more integrated to accelerate the shift to public transport.",""]],"73":[[1,"114","3","Underserved Areas Road Connectivity Improvement","Road development under the Thirteenth Plan will also be focused on connecting major roads to underserved areas to provide better road connectivity and support a more balanced regional development.",""],[1,"114","3","Central Spine Road Completion","The completion of the Central Spine Road, which covers the stretch from Bentong, Pahang to Kuala Krai, Kelantan will provide economic spillover benefits to the rakyat in the east",""],[1,"114","4","Sarawak-Sabah Link Road and Pan Borneo Highway Completion","the Sarawak- Sabah Link Road Project, the Trans Borneo Highway Project and the subsequent packages for the Pan Borneo Highway Project in Sabah will be completed",""],[1,"114","4","North-South Expressway Juru-Sg. Dua Upgrade","The project to upgrade the North-South Expressway (PLUS) Juru-Sg. Dua Section in Penang will be implemented to ease mobility and access to the northern region",""],[1,"114","4","Senai Utara-Machap Expressway Widening Project","The ongoing Senai Utara-Machap Section PLUS Expressway Widening Project will further boost economic and investment activities in the southern region",""]],"74":[[1,"40","6","Foreign Worker Dependence Reduction Measures","Measures will be undertaken to reduce reliance on foreign workers by setting the number of foreign workers to total workforce at an average of 10% in 2030 and up to 5% in 2035.",""],[1,"40","6","Multi-Tier Levy Mechanism","the Multi-Tier Levy Mechanism will be implemented in 2026.",""],[1,"41","1","Local Talent Employment and Skills Development Programme","This measure will create employment opportunities and enhance skills of local talent, leading to better salaries.",""],[1,"41","1","Industry-Linked Talent Development Programme Improvement","Talent development programmes will be improved with active industry involvement to match labour supply and demand.",""],[1,"41","1","Worker Protection and Welfare Enhancement Measures","Worker protection and welfare will also be enhanced through improvements in management of savings for retirement and strengthening of occupational hazard protection schemes.",""]],"75":[[1,"22","4","Progressive Wage Policy Implementation","the full implementation of the Progressive Wage Policy (DGP) was commenced in 2025 in the efforts to raise salaries and wages of workers",""],[1,"22","4","National Wage Reform Agenda Support by GLICs and GLCs","34 government-linked investment companies (GLICs) and government-linked companies (GLCs) had also committed to support the national wage reform agenda by implementing a decent minimum monthly salary of RM3,100 in 2025, benefiting 153,000 workers",""],[1,"37","1","Comprehensive Wage Adjustment and Decent Wage Measures","A comprehensive wage adjustment will be implemented, including periodic reviews of the minimum wage, determination of starting salaries for graduates, including TVET graduates as well as full implementation of the DGP.",""],[1,"37","1","Public Sector Salary System Implementation","As for the public sector, the Government remains committed to continue the implementation of the Sistem Saraan Perkhidmatan Awam, which began in 2024 to ensure that the salaries of the civil servants attain a decent wage level.",""],[1,"40","6","Accelerated Labour Market Reform","Labour market reform will also be accelerated to create a more dynamic, competitive and sustainable employment ecosystem to increase income.",""],[1,"40","6","Expanded National Wages Consultative Council Mandate","the role of the National Wages Consultative Council will be expanded to include all matters pertaining to salaries.",""],[1,"97","4","Progressive Wage Policy Implementation","The Progressive Wage Policy (DGP) White Paper was tabled in Parliament in 2023 and a pilot project involving 756 employers was implemented in 2024.",""],[1,"97","4","Minimum Wage Revision","The Minimum Wage Order (PGM) was revised twice during the Twelfth Plan period.",""],[1,"99","1","Holistic Wage Adjustment and Minimum Wage Revision","Efforts to accelerate wage adjustment holistically will be undertaken to reduce wage gap and improve compensation of employees.",""],[1,"99","1","National Wages Consultative Council Coordination Enhancement","The role of the National Wages Consultative Council will be enhanced to include coordination of all matters related to wage.",""],[1,"99","1","Enhanced Employment Information Portal","The e-MASCO portal will also be enhanced as a comprehensive employment information platform, including information on wages, which will be a source of reference for employees and stakeholders.",""],[1,"99","2","MSME Negotiation Platform for Wage Bargaining","A negotiation platform for micro, small and medium enterprises will be developed to increase bargaining power of employees, particularly related to wage increment.",""],[1,"104","2","DGP Expansion and PGM Review","The implementation of DGP will be expanded and periodic review of the PGM that takes into account changes in the cost of living will be continued in narrowing the salary and wage gaps.",""]],"76":[[1,"54","2","Malaysia International Islamic Finance Centre Leadership Council Collaboration","involvement of Malaysia as an international gateway for Islamic finance was strengthened through various collaborations under the Malaysia International Islamic Finance Centre (MIFC) Leadership Council.",""],[1,"62","2","Strengthen Malaysia's Islamic Finance Leadership Initiatives","Efforts will be strengthened to maintain the position of Malaysia as a global leader in Islamic finance through initiatives under the Financial Sector Blueprint, 2022-2026 and the new capital market masterplan.",""],[1,"62","2","Structured International Islamic Finance Collaboration","Collaboration in the international Islamic finance market will be strengthened with a more structured approach through the MIFC Leadership Council.",""],[1,"62","2","Expand Islamic Financial Solutions Along the Halal Supply Chain","the offering of Islamic financial solutions will be expanded into investment and trade activities along the halal supply chain.",""],[1,"62","2","Green Financing for the Halal Industry","Green financing for the halal industry will be expanded to encourage adoption of green practices in businesses.",""]],"77":[[1,"154","5","Crime Offender Management and Rehabilitation Programme","focus will be given on efforts to enhance public safety and security, uphold the national sovereignty, enhance the welfare of security personnel as well as improve the management and rehabilitation of crime offenders.",""],[1,"156","3","Prison Facilities Development and Modernisation","the capacity of basic infrastructure will be improved by developing, upgrading and modernising prison facilities.",""],[1,"156","3","Alternative Punishment and Community Rehabilitation Expansion","The implementation of alternative punishment through community works and community rehabilitation programmes will also be expanded.",""],[1,"156","3","Electronic Monitoring for Offender Surveillance","latest technologies, including electronic monitoring devices will be used to enable a more systematic surveillance and tracking.",""]],"78":[[1,"115","3","Urban Development Efficiency and Smart Cities Promotion","The efficiency of urban development and management will be given focus to address the challenges of urban sprawl, a dense population as a result of rural-urban migration and traffic congestion.",""],[1,"115","3","Smart City Standards Compliance Promotion","Development of smart cities will be promoted through compliance to smart city indicators under the Sustainable Cities and Communities standards.",""],[1,"115","4","Smart City Infrastructure Development","Infrastructure development characterised by smart and innovative as well as safe technologies will be prioritised to improve quality of life, resource efficiency and urban competitiveness.",""],[1,"115","4","Kota MADANI Urban Development Project","the Kota MADANI in Putrajaya will be developed as a pioneer of the future urban model through an urban development approach based on values, sustainability and wellbeing of the rakyat.",""]],"79":[[1,"108","3","Kampung Baru Socioeconomic Development Programme","the socioeconomic development of low-income residents in the Kampung Baru will be implemented based on the Kampung Baru Development Master Plan.",""],[1,"108","3","Improved Financing Schemes for Resident Entrepreneurship","Opportunities for residents to participate in business and entrepreneurial activities, including in the potential tourism industry, will be enhanced through the improvement of existing financing schemes.",""],[1,"108","3","Socioeconomic Support for Low-Income Chinese Households","Efforts to enhance the quality of life of the Chinese community, particularly the low-income households nationwide in facing the challenges of the cost of living will be strengthened.",""],[1,"108","4","Kampung Baru Infrastructure and Public Amenities Upgrade","Infrastructure and public amenities will be upgraded to improve the socioeconomic wellbeing of the residents, including older persons and youth in the Kampung Baru.",""],[1,"108","4","Hawker Site Provision and Upgrading","In addition, hawker sites will be made available and enhanced to support socioeconomic improvement.",""],[1,"108","4","Tourism Facilities Upgrading Programme","Furthermore, efforts to upgrade tourism facilities will be implemented to ensure the local tourism industry remains competitive and sustainable.",""]],"80":[[1,"66","1","Green Government Procurement Expansion","the GGP Works guideline will be enforced to complete the Government green procurement scopes, encompassing supplies, services and works.",""],[1,"66","1","Expansion of Green Government Procurement by State Governments and PBTs","State governments and PBTs will be encouraged to expand the implementation of the GGP.",""],[1,"66","1","Sustainable City Transformation Initiative","the transformation of cities to be more sustainable will be accelerated through increased usage of RE and energy efficiency, green mobility as well as smart landscapes.",""],[1,"66","1","Green Product Certification and Industry Capacity Building","Green products and services supply chains will be strengthened through improvement in green certification and capacity building of related industries to support green market initiatives.",""]],"81":[[1,"43","4","PPP Project Rationalisation and User-Pay Model","The implementation of PPP projects will be rationalised by focusing on user-pay model to provide options of services for the rakyat.",""],[1,"130","4","Privatisation Projects Based on User-Pay","Emphasis on the implementation of privatisation projects based on user-pay will provide alternative quality infrastructure and help in reducing the financial commitment of the Government.",""],[1,"131","7","Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","These efforts include improving effectiveness of project implementation and cost control as well as strengthening public-private partnership (PPP).",""],[1,"132","2","Strengthening of Public-Private Partnership Projects","The implementation of PPP projects will continue to be strengthened based on the PIKAS 2030, focusing on user-pay model in the provision of infrastructure facilities and services as alternatives for the rakyat.",""],[1,"132","2","PPP Governance Enhancement and PPP Legislation","In addition, PPP governance will be enhanced, including through the introduction of a specific legislation related to PPP.",""],[1,"132","2","PPP Viability Assessment and Screening Process","The VAE process as an initial screening of PPP project applications will also be undertaken to ensure only viable, strategic and implementation-ready projects are considered.",""]],"82":[[1,"36","7","Public Transport Service Expansion and Improvement","These initiatives include improving the quality and frequency of public transport services, such as expanding routes as well as increasing the number of buses and trains.",""],[1,"82","2","Urban Bus Service Enhancement","The availability of buses with better service frequency and consistency in major cities will be enhanced, particularly during peak hours.",""],[1,"82","2","Station and Park-and-Ride Facility Upgrading","Infrastructure and support facilities at the stations and park-and-ride areas will also be upgraded based on pedestrian-friendly and lifestyle hubs for the comfort of public transport passengers.",""]],"83":[[1,"155","5","National Border Control Enhancement","The national border control will be enhanced through the strengthening of security posts in the north of Peninsular Malaysia, Sabah and Sarawak, as well as through full-scale operation of the AKPS at all national entry points.",""],[1,"155","5","AI-Enabled Immigration Process Modernisation","existing assets and immigration processes will be improved through the application of AI, digitalisation and automation to reduce congestion and increase control at the national entry points.",""],[1,"155","5","Integrated Enforcement Coordination Against Smuggling and Human Trafficking","The role of all enforcement agencies will be streamlined by optimising resource utilisation to increase effectiveness of efforts in combating smuggling and human trafficking activities as well as maritime security threats.",""],[1,"155","7","Integrated Illegal Immigration Control and Enforcement","Control over illegal immigrants (PATI) will be strengthened in a comprehensive and integrated manner through collaboration among related agencies.",""],[1,"155","7","Illegal Immigration Enforcement Operations","Key approaches to be implemented include enhancing enforcement operations, deportation and border control, closing of illegal routes as well as adopting surveillance technologies extensively.",""],[1,"155","7","Integrated Immigration System Strengthening","the existing integrated immigration system will continue to be strengthened to enhance the efficiency in managing foreigners.",""]],"84":[[1,"26","4","AI-Enabled Disaster Preparedness and Response System","The use of AI can also enhance the efficiency, precision as well as effectiveness of disaster preparedness and response.",""],[1,"26","4","AI-Supported Disaster Logistics and Recovery Management","AI is utilised in forecasting disaster, assisting in the management of relief logistics, resource distribution and evacuation centres, detection of affected areas and assessments of infrastructure damages as well as optimising recovery plans.",""],[1,"28","23","Disaster Preparedness and Response Improvement","Improve efficiency, precision and effectiveness of disaster preparedness and response",""],[1,"40","3","Disaster Risk Reduction and Early Warning System Strengthening","Initiatives to reduce disaster risks will also be strengthened, including by improving the early warning system and accelerating the implementation of",""],[1,"138","1","Planetary Health and Disaster Management Initiative","preserve the planetary health and enhance disaster management will also be given focus",""],[1,"160","5","Disaster Management Strengthening Measures","Measures to further strengthen disaster management are able to increase the level of preparedness and accelerate response, thus ensuring the wellbeing of the rakyat is always safeguarded.",""],[1,"160","5","Inclusive and Integrated Disaster Management","An inclusive and integrated disaster management is able to reduce disaster risks and impacts as well as increase efficiency in resource use.",""],[1,"160","5","Disaster Governance Strengthening","Increased preparedness and fast response through strengthening of governance will elevate confidence of the rakyat and business communities that their safety and properties are always protected.",""],[1,"161","1","Meteorological Warning System Improvement","The meteorological warning system was improved in the effort to provide early information on weather warning to all stakeholders.",""],[1,"161","1","International Disaster Management Cooperation and Joint Training","Cooperation on disaster management at international level, including ASEAN through the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030 global platform was strengthened with the involvement of various agencies in joint training exercises.",""],[1,"161","7","Disaster Mitigation Governance and Coordination Strengthening","focus will be given to the efforts in increasing the efficiency of disaster mitigation governance, planning and coordination as well as the preparedness of security agencies in handling disasters.",""],[1,"161","8","Disaster Risk Management Governance Efficiency Measures","Measures to increase governance efficiency in disaster risk management will be implemented by strengthening policies, strategies and administration as well as adopting advanced technologies.",""],[1,"161","8","Expansion of Disaster Risk Reduction Policy to States and PBTs","The implementation of Disaster Risk Reduction Policy will be expanded to states and PBTs as a guide for disaster risk management.",""],[1,"161","8","Local Disaster Risk Management Action Plans","Action plans for disaster risk management will be incorporated as part of the Local Plan to increase the resilience of populated areas and municipalities.",""],[1,"161","8","Improvement of the National Disaster Relief Trust Fund Governance","The governance of Kumpulan Wang Amanah Bantuan Bencana Negara, including the guideline will be improved to expedite post-disaster response processes.",""],[1,"161","9","Nature-Based Disaster Risk Reduction","Nature-based solutions will be adopted to reduce impact of disasters due to climate change.",""],[1,"161","9","Geological and Underground Utility Mapping Enhancement","geological and underground utility mapping will be intensified to improve safety of the rakyat.",""],[1,"161","9","Meteorological Early Warning System for All Upgrade","The Meteorological Early Warning System for All will be improved to increase national disaster preparedness.",""],[1,"161","9","Climate Disaster Resilience Index Expansion","the adoption of Climate Disaster Resilience Index will be expanded to evaluate key components of urban resilience in enhancing the capability of cities in disaster management.",""],[1,"163","1","Disaster Management Improvement","Focus will also be given in health and housing reform, strengthening of security and defence, preservation of planetary health as well as improvement in disaster management to raise the floor and strengthen governance.",""]],"85":[[1,"56","1","Global Services, Finance, Distributive Trade, Logistics and Sports Industry Revitalisation","In addition, global services (GS), finance, distributive trade, logistics and sports industries will be invigorated.",""],[1,"62","5","Logistics Supply Chain Modernisation and Real-Time Monitoring","The logistics supply chain management will be modernised by strengthening the monitoring to increase efficiency in the movement of goods.",""],[1,"62","5","Cargo Shift from Road to Rail Transport","In addition, measures will be undertaken to ensure that majority of the cargo movements shift from utilising roads to rail transport system by increasing train capacity and services frequency.",""],[1,"62","5","National Warehouse Standards and Inventory Website Development","Standards and specifications for warehouses as well as a national warehouse inventory website will also be developed to facilitate business and enhance competitiveness towards achieving the goal of becoming a logistics hub in the Asian region.",""],[1,"62","6","Logistics Support Facility Development","Logistics support facility such as fulfilment centres offering warehousing, cold chain, order processing and online delivery services will be developed.",""],[1,"62","6","Gig Worker Skills Training Initiative","The industry will be encouraged to provide training for gig workers to enhance skills in meeting the industry demand.",""],[1,"62","6","Logistics Performance Benchmarking Study","a study will be conducted to identify structural issues and challenges as well as gaps in the achievement of Malaysia compared with the top five countries in the World Bank Logistics Performance Index report.",""],[1,"63","1","National Logistics Industry Action Plan and Monitoring Mechanism","The study will also provide action plans as well as monitoring and performance evaluation mechanism to increase the efficiency and competitiveness of the national logistics industry.",""]],"86":[[1,"59","6","Malaysia Aviation Decarbonisation Blueprint","the Malaysia Aviation Decarbonisation Blueprint will be implemented to reduce carbon footprint of the air transport industry.",""],[1,"59","6","Sustainable Aviation Fuel Readiness Assessment","The readiness of the industry ecosystem to shift towards sustainable transport, including the adoption of sustainable aviation fuel (SAF) and low-carbon aviation fuel as well as the development of SAF-related infrastructure will be assessed.",""],[1,"59","6","Green Ground Handling Decarbonisation Measures","efforts to decarbonise ground handling services will be enhanced, which include providing more electric vehicle charging stations and photovoltaic panels to generate RE as well as creating more green landscapes.",""]],"87":[[1,"41","2","Bumiputera Empowerment Agenda Intensification","Implementation of the Bumiputera empowerment agenda will be intensified through the whole-of-nation approach to increase Bumiputera participation, ownership and control.",""],[1,"41","2","Bumiputera Institutional Capacity and Financing Support","the Bumiputera empowerment units in all ministries as well as capacity building programmes and financing support of the Bumiputera-mandated agencies, state economic development corporations and LKWs will be strengthened.",""]],"88":[[1,"166","1","Thirteenth Malaysia Plan Monitoring Mechanism Improvement","the monitoring mechanism will be improved to enable a more transparent, systematic, comprehensive and effective monitoring of the Thirteenth Plan with the commitment from all levels of government, the private sector and civil society organisations.",""],[1,"167","1","Thirteenth Plan Monitoring Framework Enhancement","The Thirteenth Plan monitoring framework will be improved by establishing specific monitoring mechanism and governance structure.",""],[1,"167","2","PPD Monitoring Mechanism Enhancement","The improvement of the monitoring mechanism through PPD will involve preparation of a specific document based on the Thirteenth Plan framework, development of a monitoring system and strengthening of the roles as well as responsibilities of all ministries and agencies in preparing inputs as well as reports periodically.",""],[1,"167","2","Thirteenth Plan Strategy and Initiative Implementation Framework","The PPD document will prescribe the strategies and initiatives to be implemented by all ministries and agencies identified as lead or implementing entities.",""],[1,"167","3","MyRMK Reporting and Monitoring System","The MyRMK system, currently being developed internally by the Ministry of Economy will be accessible to all stakeholders to facilitate reporting and monitoring.","Ministry of Economy"],[1,"167","4","Thirteenth Plan PPD Reporting Through MyRMK System","The Thirteenth Plan PPD reporting through MyRMK system will be undertaken by all ministries, departments, agencies, state governments and local authorities based on lead or implementor roles on a quarterly basis.",""],[1,"167","4","Reporting Guideline for Ministries and Agencies","A reporting guideline will also be made available to facilitate the roles of ministries and agencies in preparing comprehensive reports based on specified timelines.",""],[1,"168","1","Thirteenth Plan Monitoring Governance Framework","The establishment of a comprehensive Thirteenth Plan monitoring governance framework based on existing committees will optimise resources, avoid duplication of functions and increase monitoring effectiveness.",""],[1,"168","2","Strengthening Ministry Coordination and Monitoring Units for PPD","The functions and roles of units or divisions in ministries responsible for coordination as well as monitoring will be strengthened to be the focal point in coordinating the preparation and reporting of the PPD.",""],[1,"169","1","Expanded Technical Monitoring and Coordination Committees for the Thirteenth Plan","The monitoring of the Thirteenth Plan at technical level will be implemented through the expanded roles of two existing committees established by the Ministry of Economy, namely TWGs and Inter-Agency Planning Groups (IAPGs).","Ministry of Economy"],[1,"169","2","Inter-Agency Planning Group Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","The IAPGs will also be assigned additional role in finalising the details of PPD by pillars, including setting clear output targets within specified timelines and coordinating strategies and initiatives across ministries.",""],[1,"169","2","Quarterly Thirteenth Plan Performance Reporting","In addition, the IAPGs will be responsible in reporting the Thirteenth Plan performance to the National Development Planning Committee (NDPC) on a quarterly basis.",""],[1,"169","2","Integrated Monitoring Issues Review Mechanism","The IAPGs meetings will also discuss issues raised through the monitoring mechanisms of the MyBelanjawan, the MyProjek and the SDGs as well as issues monitored under the PMU and the PACU.",""],[1,"170","1","High-Level Socioeconomic Policy Monitoring and Coordination by NDPC","Monitoring at the highest level of senior government officials will be undertaken by the NDPC, which is responsible in formulating and coordinating matters related to socioeconomic policy.",""],[1,"170","1","NDPC Policy Deliberation and Endorsement Platform","The NDPC serves as a platform to deliberate and endorse appropriate intervention before being escalated to the National Economic Action Council (NEAC).",""],[1,"170","2","NEAC Biannual Thirteenth Plan Monitoring Review","achievements of the Thirteenth Plan will be presented in the NEAC meetings biannually to finalise appropriate interventions.",""],[1,"170","2","Annual Thirteenth Plan Implementation Report to Cabinet","The Thirteenth Plan implementation report will also be tabled to the Cabinet annually, which comprises implementation progress, achievement of outcomes, issues and challenges as well as proposed solutions that require policy decisions.",""],[1,"171","1","Thirteenth Plan Monitoring Mechanism Enhancement","The monitoring of the Thirteenth Plan will be implemented comprehensively through enhancement of the monitoring mechanism and strengthening of governance at all levels.",""],[1,"171","1","PPD and MyRMK Monitoring System Development","The development of the PPD and MyRMK system will facilitate all stakeholders in assuming respective roles to monitor in a transparent, systematic, comprehensive and effective manner.",""],[1,"171","1","Whole-of-Government Governance Strengthening for Plan Delivery","Strengthening of governance through active involvement of ministries, departments, agencies and state governments will ensure the Thirteenth Plan achieves the aspirations of the 'Ekonomi MADANI: Memperkasa Rakyat'.",""]],"89":[[1,"102","8","Cost of Living Management Measures","Strategies will continue to focus on efforts to strengthen the management of the cost of living, address poverty, narrow inequalities as well as improve social protection.",""],[1,"102","8","Social Protection Improvement Measures","Strategies will continue to focus on efforts to strengthen the management of the cost of living, address poverty, narrow inequalities as well as improve social protection.",""],[1,"102","9","Integrated Cost of Living Relief Measures","The Thirteenth Plan focuses on efforts in addressing the rising cost of living as stipulated in strategies and initiatives across priority areas.",""],[1,"102","10","National Cost of Living Action Plan","a new national cost of living action plan will be introduced, among others, focusing on stabilising prices of goods and services as well as managing subsidy.",""],[1,"102","10","Integrated Supply Chain Enforcement Against Profiteering","A comprehensive enforcement will be implemented by integrating the scope of enforcement in the entire supply and distribution chains to curb profiteering and anti-competitive practices.",""],[1,"102","10","Program Jualan RAHMAH MADANI Expansion","initiatives to sell goods and services at reasonable prices, such as the Program Jualan RAHMAH MADANI will be expanded to other suitable localities, particularly in the rural areas.",""],[1,"102","11","Consumerism Action Plan 2030","Empowerment and advocacy of consumer rights will be further strengthened with the introduction of the Consumerism Action Plan 2030, which will detail out the National Consumer Policy 2.0.",""],[1,"102","11","Consumer Governance and Empowerment Measures","This action plan will cover aspects such as strengthening of governance, empowerment of consumer, sustainable consumption practices, fairer marketing as well as enhancement of technology adaptation through digitalisation and AI.",""],[1,"163","1","Cost of Living Relief Measures","During the Thirteenth Plan period, continuous efforts will be undertaken to address key issues and challenges that undermine the wellbeing of the rakyat, particularly the cost of living burden and environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"175","5","Needs-Based Resource Distribution","The government is also responsible in ensuring equitable distribution of resources based on the needs of the rakyat.",""],[1,"176","4","Inclusive Financing, Incentives and Targeted Support Programmes","In addition, government supports, such as financing, incentives and targeted programmes, are continuously improved to ensure inclusivity and address shortcomings that exist in the economy.",""],[1,"208","2","RAHMAH MADANI Sales Program","Program Jualan RAHMAH MADANI, 1-20, 3-14 Program Pemerkasaan Ekonomi Komuniti Bandar (PEKB), 1-21",""]],"90":[[1,"97","2","Labour Market Reform for a Dynamic Employment Ecosystem","Labour market reform aims to create a more dynamic, competitive and sustainable employment ecosystem, in line with the aspirations of the Ekonomi MADANI",""],[1,"98","8","Labour Market Reform Package","Six strategies will be implemented to reform the labour market during the Thirteenth Plan period, as follows:",""],[1,"100","6","Labour Law and Regulation Review","Labour laws and regulations will be reviewed to strengthen the implementation of policies related to labour and human capital development.",""],[1,"100","6","Labour Officer Capacity and Competency Enhancement","The capacity and competencies of labour officers will also be enhanced to support the enforcement of related laws and regulations.",""],[1,"100","6","AI and Digitalisation of Labour Systems","the adoption of AI in and digitalisation of the labour system and infrastructure will be expanded to enhance service delivery.",""]],"91":[[1,"99","7","Work-Life Balance and Flexible Work Arrangements Expansion","Initiatives that emphasise work-life balance will continue to be expanded in enhancing the wellbeing of employees.",""],[1,"100","1","Flexible Work Schedule Encouragement","to adjust work schedules in accommodating personal needs will continue to be encouraged.",""],[1,"100","2","Labour Market Participation Expansion Measures","measures to increase the participation of older persons, women and persons with disabilities (PWDs) will be intensified as part of the initiatives to improve the labour market.",""],[1,"100","2","Minimum Retirement Age and Re-employment Legislative Reform","Amendment to the Minimum Retirement Age Act 2012 [Act 753] and introduction of a legislation related to re-employment with more flexible terms will be implemented to provide productive older workers with options to remain in the labour market.",""],[1,"100","4","Flexible Work Arrangements Policy Strengthening","the implementation of policies related to flexible work arrangements ... will be strengthened",""],[1,"100","4","Career-Matching Programme Expansion","career-matching programmes will be strengthened",""],[1,"100","4","Workplace Childcare Facility Expansion","the provision of childcare facilities at the workplace will be expanded",""]],"92":[[1,"150","1","Multi-Stakeholder Housing Delivery Coordination","The aim to enable the rakyat to have a decent living will only be achieved through cooperation of all stakeholders, including state governments, the private sector, financial institutions and industry representatives.",""],[1,"151","1","Single National Housing Agency Establishment","a single national housing agency will be established through the rationalisation of all Federal housing agencies to plan, coordinate and manage the provision of affordable houses.",""],[1,"151","1","Integrated Housing Information Repository","An integrated housing information repository will be developed as a single reference in planning, implementing and monitoring of public housing programmes through the integration of all housing systems at the Federal and state levels.",""],[1,"151","4","Mandatory Build-and-Sell Housing Reform","The construction of houses based on the build and sell concept on a risk-sharing basis will be made mandatory through amendment to the Housing Development (Control and Licensing) Act 1966 [Act 118].",""],[1,"151","4","Housing Development Regulation and Tribunal Strengthening","The amendment to the Act 118 will also improve regulation on mixed housing development as well as strengthen the role of the housing tribunal.",""],[1,"151","5","Housing Consortium for Rent-to-Own Scheme Management","A proposal to establish a housing consortium to ensure a more efficient and sustainable management of the RTO scheme will be explored.",""],[1,"151","6","Residential Tenancy Act","An act related to residential tenancy will also be introduced to ensure fair protection for tenants and homeowners.",""],[1,"152","1","Public Housing Governance Legislation","legislation related to public housing governance will be enacted to improve efficiency and effectiveness of public housing management.",""],[1,"152","1","Subsidised Housing Resale Moratorium Mechanism","The establishment of moratorium period and mechanism in reselling of subsidised houses in the open market will be included in this legislation to ensure the provision of affordable housing is sustainable.",""],[1,"152","1","Cost-Based Tenancy and Maintenance Fee Mechanism","These measures will enable improvement of the mechanism in setting tenancy rate and maintenance fees based on actual costs.",""],[1,"152","1","Third-Party Housing Management Appointment","The appointment of third parties, such as accredited and licensed building management agencies or companies, will also be implemented to ensure effective and systematic housing management and maintenance.",""],[1,"152","2","Strata Ownership and Management Reform","Initiatives to resolve strata ownership issues will be explored in ensuring buyers of stratified housing unit are no longer entrapped with the difficulties in obtaining ownership and protected by the law.",""],[1,"152","2","Inter-Agency Coordination for Stratified Housing Management","Coordination among the relevant departments and agencies will be strengthened to enable the",""],[1,"153","2","Construction Cost Index for Housing","A construction cost index by type of houses will be developed as a guide to ensure house prices are more reasonable and transparent.",""]],"93":[[1,"42","3","Outcome-Based Ministry Performance Monitoring System","the monitoring and performance evaluation mechanism of ministries will be streamlined through the introduction of outcome-based indicators that are aligned with selected macroeconomic indicators and direct reporting to the Prime Minister.",""],[1,"42","3","MyRMK Plan Monitoring System Development","The comprehensive monitoring approach and governance structure of the Thirteenth Plan will be further improved through the development of a monitoring system for the Pelan Pelaksanaan Dasar RMK13, known as MyRMK.",""],[1,"42","3","Integrated Government Monitoring System Linkage","This system will be integrated with other monitoring systems, such as under the Ministry of Finance, Implementation Coordination Unit, Prime Minister's Department (ICU, JPM), Unit Pantau MADANI (PMU), Performance Acceleration Coordination Unit (PACU) and Pusat SDG Negara (PSN).","Ministry of Finance | Implementation Coordination Unit, Prime Minister's Department (ICU, JPM) | Unit Pantau MADANI (PMU) | Performance Acceleration Coordination Unit (PACU) | Pusat SDG Negara (PSN)"],[1,"42","3","Cabinet-Level Plan Performance Oversight","The performance of the Thirteenth Plan will also be monitored by the Cabinet as the highest level to ensure accountability and transparency in the implementation of development programmes and projects.",""],[1,"43","4","Project Management Reform for Fiscal Efficiency","Fiscal management efficiency will also be enhanced through a project management reform involving more systematic monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"43","4","Cost Control Improvement Mechanism","Cost control mechanism will be improved by incorporating key elements in cost calculation, including life cycle costs.",""]],"94":[[1,"23","2","Public Sector Digitalisation Strategic Plan 2021-2025","policies formulated during the Twelfth Plan period include the Public Sector Digitalisation Strategic Plan 2021-2025",""],[1,"26","6","GovTech-Based Digital Government Ecosystem","Digitalisation of government services, through empowerment of the GovTech based on principles of excellent governance will enable the establishment of a digital government ecosystem that connects not only government to government, but also government to the rakyat and the business community.",""],[1,"26","7","GovTech Digital Government Service System","The mainstreaming of the GovTech will create a comprehensive digital government service system across the lifespan of the rakyat, from cradle to grave in facilitating the matters concerning the rakyat and business community, regardless of location, including those in the rural and remote areas.",""],[1,"26","7","AI Adoption in Public Service Delivery","The widespread adoption of AI by all government agencies, including front line agencies, enforcement agencies, security agencies and research agencies will ensure transparent, timely and thorough services.",""],[1,"28","15","Digital Government Ecosystem","Establish a digital government ecosystem",""],[1,"42","6","GovTech Strengthening and Digital Government Transformation","The strengthening of GovTech which focuses on adoption of advanced technologies including AI, enhancement of digital governance as well as capacity building will be intensified to create a digital government ecosystem that is transparent, agile and holistic towards becoming an AI nation.",""],[1,"42","6","Enterprise Architecture and Secure Cloud Infrastructure Development","The enterprise architecture (EA), which also encompasses creation of a secure cloud infrastructure will be developed to enhance digitalisation of government services.",""],[1,"42","6","Single Government Service Gateway","A single gateway will also be developed to better facilitate the rakyat, business community and government in accessing various services provided, including through the usage of MyDigital ID.",""],[1,"42","6","Digitalisation Governance and Digital Talent Development","Governance of digitalisation and development of digital talent will also be strengthened in improving the efficiency and effectiveness of public service delivery.",""],[1,"42","6","Cybersecurity and Data Sharing Integration Enhancement","Aspects of cyber security as well as data sharing and integration will continue to be emphasised to ensure a secured and trusted public service digitalisation ecosystem.",""]],"95":[[1,"43","2","Electronic Invoicing Roll-out for Tax Collection","Government revenue collection will be enhanced through phased roll-out of the electronic invoicing system by 2026 to increase the digitalisation of tax collection.",""],[1,"43","2","Medium-Term Revenue Strategy Tax Base Expansion","In addition, the expansion of the tax base under the Medium-Term Revenue Strategy (MTRS), such as the implementation of the global minimum tax (GMT) and the periodic review of the sales and services tax (SST) will be undertaken to enable the provision of more facilities and assistance for the wellbeing of the rakyat.",""]],"96":[[1,"32","5","Renewable Energy, Storage, and Smart Grid Expansion","The competitiveness and flexibility of the energy market will be enhanced through the utilisation of renewable energy sources, such as energy storage and smart grids as well as hydro hybrid floating solar.",""],[1,"36","7","Time of Use Electricity Pricing Scheme","the Time of Use Scheme introduced in 2025 and energy efficiency incentives will be continued to encourage more efficient electricity usage and reduce the costs to consumers.",""],[1,"36","7","Energy Efficiency Incentives","the Time of Use Scheme introduced in 2025 and energy efficiency incentives will be continued to encourage more efficient electricity usage and reduce the costs to consumers.",""]],"97":[[1,"6","5","Digitalisation and Artificial Intelligence Value-Creation Shift","through the shift to value creation based on digitilisation and artificial intelligence.",""],[1,"18","2","Digitalisation and Advanced Technologies Transition","The national development for the upcoming five years will be based on a comprehensive transition towards digitalisation and advanced technologies, particularly artificial intelligence (AI),",""],[1,"24","2","Digital Transformation and AI Adoption for Plan Implementation","digital transformation and the use of AI technology will serve as the foundation in implementing priorities and strategies of the Thirteenth Plan towards positioning Malaysia as one of the main AI nations in the world.",""],[1,"25","2","Inclusive and Ethical AI Ecosystem Development","The transition towards an AI nation is a reform through systematic digitalisation and requires the development of an inclusive and ethical AI ecosystem based on advanced technologies.",""],[1,"25","2","AI Integration Across Key Sectors","AI-based solutions will be integrated into all key sectors, such as the manufacturing, agriculture, services, health, education, finance, security and defence, housing, urban as well as public service.",""],[1,"27","3","National AI Action Plan 2030","the Pelan Tindakan AI Kebangsaan 2030 will be introduced as the basis for AI planning, development, implementation and innovation.",""],[1,"31","3","Advanced Technology and Digitalisation Acceleration","Efforts to enhance the adoption of advanced technology and digitalisation will be intensified through the implementation of the National Science, Technology and Innovation Policy, the National Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR) Policy and the Malaysia Digital Economy Blueprint.",""],[1,"31","3","National AI Ecosystem Development","Measures to develop a comprehensive AI ecosystem based on cutting-edge technology will be implemented towards positioning Malaysia as an inclusive and sustainable AI nation.",""],[1,"31","3","National AI Action Plan 2030","In this regard, the Pelan Tindakan AI Kebangsaan 2030 will be introduced.",""]],"98":[[1,"18","2","Whole-of-Nation Social System Development","the development of a social system anchored on insan MADANI with a united society under the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[1,"18","3","Structural Transformation and Inclusive Growth Acceleration","Efforts to accelerate the economy will be intensified by accelerating structural change, propelling inclusive and sustainable growth, enhancing balanced development among regions and of rural areas as well as expanding economic integration at the global level.",""],[1,"18","3","Social Mobility and Cost-of-Living Support","In addition, living status of the rakyat or social mobility will be enhanced to empower the rakyat in addressing the burden of the cost of living, reengineer social system anchored on insan MADANI and improve quality of life.",""],[1,"36","1","Inclusive Social Development and Cost-of-Living Support Measures","Inclusive and responsive social development will continue to be prioritised in the efforts to uplift living status, akin to raising the floor.",""],[1,"36","1","Social System Reengineering Anchored on insan MADANI","Efforts will be intensified in addressing the burden of the cost of living, reengineering the social system anchored on insan MADANI, enhancing quality of life as well as empowering targeted groups towards achieving a decent life.",""],[1,"36","1","Targeted Group Empowerment for Decent Living Standards","Efforts will be intensified in addressing the burden of the cost of living, reengineering the social system anchored on insan MADANI, enhancing quality of life as well as empowering targeted groups towards achieving a decent life.",""],[1,"36","2","Cost of Living Reduction Initiatives","Focus will be given on initiatives to reduce the costs incurred in obtaining food supplies, healthcare services, housing, education, utilities and public transportation in reducing the financial burden of the rakyat.",""],[1,"36","2","Wage Increase and Targeted Social Assistance Measures","In addition, measures to increase income of the rakyat through wage increment and provision of targeted social assistance will be implemented.",""],[1,"37","1","Targeted Cost of Living Support Programmes","In addition, the Government is committed to continue implementing targeted programmes in addressing the cost of living pressures.",""],[1,"37","1","Cash Assistance and Targeted Subsidy Scheme","This commitment includes the provision of cash assistance and the implementation of targeted subsidies, such as the Sumbangan Tunai Rahmah (STR), the Sumbangan Asas Rahmah (SARA) as well as welfare assistance schemes for children, senior citizens and persons with disabilities (PWDs).",""]],"99":[[1,"6","5","High-Value Made by Malaysia Product Diversification","Culture of innovation will also be nurtured in diversifying the production of high-value \"Made by Malaysia\" products.",""],[1,"20","12","New Industrial Master Plan 2030","This performance was supported by the implementation of progressive industrial policies, particularly the New Industrial Master Plan (NIMP) 2030 and the National Semiconductor Strategy (NSS) that promote investment, automation and integration in the global supply chain.",""],[1,"20","12","National Semiconductor Strategy","This performance was supported by the implementation of progressive industrial policies, particularly the New Industrial Master Plan (NIMP) 2030 and the National Semiconductor Strategy (NSS) that promote investment, automation and integration in the global supply chain.",""],[1,"31","2","Economic Complexity and High-Value Product Development Initiative","efforts will be undertaken to strengthen the ecosystem that include the adoption of advanced technology and digitalisation, increase research, development, commercialisation and innovation (R&D&C&I) activities and productivity as well as strengthen competitiveness and global networks.",""],[1,"32","3","Intensified Implementation of Industrial and Energy Transition Strategies","The implementation of strategies and initiatives under the NIMP, NETR, NSS, Natural Gas Roadmap as well as the Hydrogen Economy and Technology Roadmap will be intensified to support efforts in creating more high-value 'Made by Malaysia' products and services.",""],[1,"32","6","Semiconductor Industry Reform and E&E Subsector Upgrading","The manufacturing sector will continue to be intensified through efforts in boosting the electrical and electronics (E&E) subsector, particularly by reforming the semiconductor industry to enhance the production of high value high technology (HVHT) products.",""],[1,"32","6","Technology- and IP-Centric Semiconductor Investment Collaboration","Strategic collaborations with global semiconductor companies will be strengthened through technology and IP centric investment model.",""],[1,"32","6","Integrated Circuit Design Champion Development","World-class local champions in creating integrated circuit design will be developed to increase production",""],[1,"33","1","Technology Creation and Domestic Production of High-Value Products","Emphasis will be given to accelerate technology creation and production of 'Made by Malaysia' products, such as chemical products, pharmaceuticals and medical devices, high-value halal and agro-based products, sports equipment as well as electric and aerial vehicles.",""]],"100":[[1,"25","7","AI-Based Predictive Analytics for Renewable Energy Planning","AI-based predictive analytics capabilities can be utilised to provide a more accurate projection of energy demand and supply, which in turn can optimise smart grid management as well as enhance operational efficiency and RE infrastructure provision.",""]],"101":[[1,"6","5","Cross-Sector Talent Development Initiatives","This aspiration will be supported through talent development initiatives across diverse fields, ranging from science and technology to arts and creative.",""],[1,"25","9","AI-Enabled Talent Planning and Development Systems","National labour market challenges related to demand and supply mismatch can be addressed through the integration of AI across various talent planning and development mechanisms.",""],[1,"27","4","Early AI Literacy Education Initiative","AI literacy will be nurtured at an early stage of education.",""],[1,"27","4","Talent Development and Specialisation Programme","Talent development and specialisation programmes, including certification, upskilling and reskilling will be strengthened.",""],[1,"27","4","Public-Private-Academia Collaboration for Advanced Technology Skills","Collaboration among the public sector, industry and academia will be intensified to equip local talent with skills in advanced technologies.",""]],"102":[[1,"26","3","National Health Digitalisation Agenda","The implementation of the national health digitalisation agenda can enhance the effectiveness of healthcare services.",""],[1,"26","3","AI-Enabled Early Diagnosis and Treatment Customisation","AI enables more accurate early diagnosis and treatment customisation based on the needs of the patients through big data analytics capabilities.",""],[1,"26","3","AI-Based Hospital Administration Optimisation","In hospital administration, AI can be leveraged for the management of treatment schedules, utilisation of facilities and medical equipment as well as patient flow, thus reducing waiting times and improving service quality as well as optimising resources.",""],[1,"39","6","Health Information Digitalisation and Data-Sharing Platform","The digitalisation of health information management will be enhanced through the development of a data-sharing platform between the public and private sectors as well as the outsourcing of electronic medical record systems that adopt AI technology.",""]],"103":[[1,"26","4","AI-Enabled Environmental Monitoring and Smart Waste Management","the adoption of AI enables more accurate and real-time monitoring of air and water quality as well as smart waste management.",""],[1,"26","4","AI for Green Technology Innovation and Low-Carbon Transition","AI technology can increase green technology innovation to accelerate the transition towards a low-carbon and more sustainable economy.",""]],"104":[[1,"26","5","AI-Enabled National Security and Defence Systems","AI technology plays an important role in the efforts to strengthen national security and defence.",""],[1,"26","5","AI-Based Digital Identity Verification System","AI is applied in facial recognition and biometric systems to enable fast and accurate digital identity verification.",""],[1,"26","5","AI-Based Border Surveillance and Early Warning System","AI-based monitoring systems also facilitate automated surveillance in physical border areas through the usage of drones, smart cameras and sensors, capable of providing early warnings to the authorities.",""],[1,"26","5","Real-Time AI Cyber Threat Detection System","AI is used to detect cyber threats in real time, allowing for immediate response to potential attacks.",""],[1,"28","24","National Security and Cyber Threat Detection Strengthening","Strengthen national security and defence as well as detect cyber threats in real time",""],[1,"40","4","Public Safety and National Defence Strengthening","the public safety and national defence will be strengthened by improving the readiness of security and defence assets, empowering capabilities and competencies of personnel as well as enhancing border control.",""],[1,"40","4","Management of Criminal Offenders and Undocumented Migrants","The management of criminal offenders and undocumented migrants will be improved and strategic cooperation among various enforcement agencies will be intensified to enhance public safety and security.",""],[1,"40","4","Cybercrime Prevention and Enforcement Enhancement","Efforts will be continued to combat cybercrime and the related threats by improving infostructure and infrastructure as well as strengthening enforcement and legislation.",""]],"105":[[1,"26","7","Safe and Trusted Digital Ecosystem for Online Transactions","Thus, application of AI in the public service will enable the rakyat to receive fast services and accurate information as well as enable daily activities and business transactions to be conducted online within a safe and trusted digital ecosystem.",""],[1,"27","6","National Digital Trust and Data Security Strategies","National digital trust and data security strategies will be launched with the aim to ensure the national digital ecosystem remains resilient, ethical and safe for the rakyat, businesses and government.",""],[1,"27","6","Digital Literacy and Cybersecurity for AI Trust","Digital trust will be enhanced to build public confidence in AI through literacy and cybersecurity.",""]],"106":[[1,"27","7","AI Ecosystem Strengthening and Strategic Investment Matching","Public-private partnerships will be intensified to increase strategic AI-related investment through project and investment matchings.",""],[1,"27","7","Quadruple Helix Innovation for Resource Management","the quadruple helix model will be leveraged to encourage innovation in resource management.",""],[1,"31","4","National Productivity Ecosystem Strengthening","the national productivity growth will continue to be increased by strengthening the ecosystem, which include aspects of policy and governance improvements, financing coordination and talent development.",""]],"107":[[1,"31","6","Public Investment and Development Programme Financing","A total of RM430 billion will be allocated in this plan period to finance the implementation of the Federal Government development programmes and projects.",""],[1,"31","6","Federal Government Development Programmes and Projects","The projects that will be implemented include infrastructure, infostructure, public transportation, construction of schools, hospitals and affordable housing projects as well as flood mitigation and capacity building programmes.",""],[1,"32","1","Public-Private Partnership Project Implementation Enhancement","the implementation of the development projects under the public-private partnership (PPP) will be enhanced, involving private sector financing projected at RM61 billion during the Thirteenth Plan period",""]],"108":[[1,"32","5","National Energy Transition Roadmap Green Economy Initiatives","The green economy development will be focused on implementing strategies and initiatives under the NETR, among others by exploring electricity generation using nuclear energy, expanding the use of hydrogen as fuel as well as implementing carbon capture, utilisation and storage (CCUS) initiatives and facilitating carbon trading.",""]],"109":[[1,"33","3","Non-Residential Building and Port Infrastructure Investment","Private sector investment in the non-residential building subsector, including the construction of the third terminal at Pulau Carey and Westports 2 container terminal as well as development of the Perlis Inland Port will support growth of the construction sector, which is expected to grow at 5% per annum during the Thirteenth Plan period.",""],[1,"33","3","Regasification Terminal and Major Transport Infrastructure Development","The development of the third regasification terminal and construction of high- impact public transport infrastructure, such as the Penang Mutiara Light Rail Transit, the Sabah Pan Borneo Highway and the Sarawak-Sabah Link Road project will also underpin the growth of the construction sector.",""],[1,"33","3","Construction Sector Modernisation through Advanced Technologies","In addition, the construction sector will be modernised by prioritising the usage of advanced technologies, such as the Industrialised Building System and the Building Information Modelling in residential building construction, including the development of affordable homes and housing in Kota MADANI.",""]],"110":[[1,"34","3","Rural Infrastructure and Services Expansion","focus will be given in expanding access to basic infrastructure and services to attract more investment in the rural areas and accelerate economic integration, including in Sabah and Sarawak.",""],[1,"34","3","Urban Development and Management Efficiency Improvement","the efficiency of urban development and management will be given focus to address the challenges of urban sprawl and accelerate urbanisation in land settlement areas.",""],[1,"34","3","Transit-Oriented Urban Development","Sustainable, smart and inclusive urban development based on the concept of transit-oriented development",""],[1,"34","5","Rural Investment Hub Development","Efforts will be undertaken to intensify economic activities through the development of rural investment hubs that leverage geospatial intelligence and big data analytics.",""],[1,"34","5","Corridor and Specialised Production Hub Development","the development of corridors and specialised production hubs will be explored to leverage the local economic potential, such as the Kerian Integrated Green Industrial Park (KIGIP), the Kulim Hi-Tech Park (KHTP), the Kota Kinabalu Industrial Park (KKIP) and halal industrial parks.",""],[1,"41","4","Kampung Baru Development Master Plan Implementation","the implementation of entrepreneurship and tourism activities based on the Kampung Baru Development Master Plan as well as the provision of support to upgrade public infrastructure and facilities.",""]],"111":[[1,"36","3","Food Cost Mitigation and Price Transparency Measures","Efforts to address the rise in food costs will be undertaken holistically by improving infrastructure, strengthening the food supply chain and retail sector as well as providing platforms to enhance price transparency.",""],[1,"36","3","Price Manipulation Enforcement and Legal Review","Enforcement measures will be intensified, while relevant acts will be reviewed to curb price manipulation activities.",""],[1,"36","4","Expansion of Program Jualan RAHMAH MADANI","the Program Jualan RAHMAH MADANI will be expanded to cover more suitable localities, especially in rural areas.",""]],"112":[[1,"34","2","Bumiputera Entrepreneurship Support Programme","Bumiputera entrepreneurship programmes will be enhanced by providing continuous support to enterprises according to business development stages based on a relay race concept.",""],[1,"37","2","Income-Generating Programme Streamlining","The design and implementation of income-generating programmes, such as the Inisiatif Pendapatan Rakyat, the Program Pemerkasaan Ekonomi Komuniti Bandar and the Skim Pembangunan Kesejahteraan Rakyat will be streamlined to enhance effectiveness in addressing poverty.",""],[1,"40","1","Youth and Rural Entrepreneur Capacity-Building Programmes","In addition, capacity and capability enhancement programmes for target groups, particularly youth and rural entrepreneurs as well as second and third generations in the FELDA, FELCRA and LKWs will be intensified.",""],[1,"41","5","Youth Skills, Talent and Entrepreneurship Development Initiative","youth development will be strengthened through the enhancement of skills, talent and entrepreneurship as well as the introduction of a focused intervention mechanism and a comprehensive support.",""]],"113":[[1,"37","3","Education System Reform and Nationalism Promotion","The development of insan MADANI will focus on reforming the education system and instilling the spirit of nationalism.",""],[1,"39","2","Patriotism and National Identity Strengthening Programme","Efforts to enhance the inculcation of adab, spiritual values and humane aspects, including based on the principles of Maqasid Syariah as well as reinforce the spirit of patriotism will be intensified to develop insan MADANI.",""],[1,"39","2","Rukun Negara and Federal Constitution Appreciation Initiative","In this regard, appreciation of the Rukun Negara and the Federal Constitution will be strengthened to ignite the spirit of nationalism.",""],[1,"39","2","Integrated Nationhood and Basic Military Training Modules","Integrated training modules that combine nationhood components and basic military training will be improved to foster strong self-identity.",""],[1,"39","2","Patriotic Creative Content Production Initiative","The production of creative works and content that showcase patriotism and national identity will also be intensified.",""]],"114":[[1,"39","4","National Athlete Excellence Enhancement","The excellence of national athletes at the international level will continue to be enhanced to uplift the image of the country and foster a sense of pride among the rakyat.",""],[1,"39","4","Diplomacy and International Relations Strengthening","effective diplomacy and international relations will be intensified to strengthen the position and positive image of Malaysia in the global arena.",""]],"115":[[1,"39","6","Domestic Medicine and Medical Device Security Strengthening","the security of domestic medicine and medical devices will be strengthened to ensure national preparedness in facing global health crises and reduce dependency on imported products.",""]],"116":[[1,"41","5","Child Wellbeing Support Programme","Child development will focus on improving access to education, health and social protection.",""],[1,"41","5","Gender Roles and Responsibilities Strengthening Initiative","The roles and responsibilities of men and women in the socioeconomic development of the nation will be strengthened to create a more inclusive, progressive and balanced society.",""],[1,"41","5","PWD Inclusion through Private Sector Partnership","The involvement of PWDs will be increased through collaboration with the private sector in providing equal opportunities for this group to lead a more meaningful life.",""],[1,"41","5","Family Institution Strengthening Initiative","The family institution will also be strengthened through the inculcation of familial values and responsibilities among family members, particularly of the child towards the parents.",""],[1,"41","5","Parenting Education and Reproductive Health Counselling Services","The provision of parenting education as well as counselling and support services related to reproductive health will also be emphasised.",""]],"117":[[1,"42","5","Legislative Review and New Acts Enactment","Efforts in improving legislation and enforcement will be implemented through the review of existing acts and enactment of new acts.",""],[1,"43","2","Public Finance Governance Reform","Good governance practices, based on accountability, transparency and efficiency under the Public Finance and Fiscal Responsibility Act 2023 [Act 850] will be adopted in public finance management.",""]],"118":[[1,"45","1","Advanced Technology and Digitalisation Adoption","Focus will also be given to increase the productivity and competitiveness of firms, industries and sectors through the adoption of advanced technologies and digitalisation as well as strengthening of the R&D&C&I ecosystem towards making Malaysia an inclusive and sustainable AI nation.",""],[1,"47","1","Digitalisation and Advanced Technologies Transition","The national development during the Thirteenth Plan period will be supported by a comprehensive transition towards digitalisation and advanced technologies, particularly AI as well as the development of a social system anchored on insan MADANI, with a society that is equitable, harmonious, respectful and united.",""],[1,"50","1","Artificial Intelligence and Advanced Technology Expansion","The development and adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) and other advanced technologies will be accelerated and expanded as a foundation in the efforts to advance economic complexity.",""],[1,"56","1","AI-Based Advanced Technology Adoption","development and adoption of advanced technologies based on AI will be emphasised.",""],[1,"56","1","Digital Economy Strengthening Initiative","Efforts for HGHV industries will focus on reforming the semiconductor industry, accelerating energy transition, developing the REE value chain, diversifying high-value agriculture products, strengthening development of the digital economy as well as leveraging science, technology and innovation (STI).",""],[1,"58","6","Digital Economy Ecosystem Strengthening Initiative","The development of the digital economy will be strengthened by focusing on enhancing the ecosystem, operational efficiency and policy implementation as well as infrastructure provision.",""],[1,"58","6","Digital Technology and AI Ecosystem Development Initiatives","The ecosystem to position Malaysia as a regional producer of digital technologies, particularly AI, will be improved through initiatives related to data, testing and matching platforms as well as cyber defence capabilities.",""],[1,"58","6","National Data Bank Establishment","A national data bank will be established as a centralised comprehensive information repository to facilitate a wider and safer sharing.",""],[1,"58","6","Digital Twin Innovation Sandbox Expansion","The usage of digital twin2 as virtual sandbox will be increased to support innovation simulation.",""],[1,"58","6","Hyper Personal Platform for Business Matching","In addition, a hyper personal platform will be developed to facilitate the matching of demand and supply between businesses and local technology solution providers.",""],[1,"59","1","Post-Quantum Cryptography Migration Plan","capabilities of the country will also be strengthened through a post-quantum cryptography migration plan to protect the national critical information infrastructure and ensure the continuity of business operations.",""],[1,"59","2","National AI Action Plan 2030","The Pelan Tindakan AI Kebangsaan 2030 will be introduced as a main reference to accelerate and expand adoption of AI in driving economic growth and enhancing national competitiveness.",""],[1,"59","2","AI Governance, Ethics, and Digital Trust Framework","the aspects of AI governance and ethics as well as digital trust will also be emphasised in ensuring that AI development and adoption are implemented responsibly and safely.",""],[1,"59","2","AI Talent Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","AI talent development will be strengthened through upskilling and reskilling programmes to meet the needs of the industry for the workforce.",""],[1,"59","3","Digital Infrastructure Improvement for High-Speed Internet Access","Digital infrastructure will be improved to enhance internet access, mainly high-speed connectivity.",""],[1,"59","3","Business Digital Identity System","Business digital identity will also be introduced to accelerate secured access to financing services and international markets.",""],[1,"63","3","Targeted CEPA for STI and AI Adoption","Awareness and understanding on the application of STI, including the adoption of AI technology, among industry players will also be increased through targeted CEPA implementation.",""],[1,"63","3","AI-Based Interactive Learning Tools for STEM Talent","This pilot project will also provide AI-based interactive learning tools for STEM talent.",""],[1,"77","3","AI-Enabled Productivity Enhancement for Firms","Firms will be encouraged to enhance productivity through the wide adoption of AI, such as smart systems, predictive analytics, and strategic automation to drive operational and production efficiency.",""],[1,"77","3","Work Process Redesign and Human-Machine Collaboration Initiative","Emphasis will be given on efforts to redesign work processes, optimise information flow, and intensify smart collaboration between humans and technology.",""]],"119":[[1,"45","1","R&D&C&I Ecosystem Strengthening","Focus will also be given to increase the productivity and competitiveness of firms, industries and sectors through the adoption of advanced technologies and digitalisation as well as strengthening of the R&D&C&I ecosystem towards making Malaysia an inclusive and sustainable AI nation.",""],[1,"56","1","Science, Technology and Innovation Leveraging Initiative","Efforts for HGHV industries will focus on reforming the semiconductor industry, accelerating energy transition, developing the REE value chain, diversifying high-value agriculture products, strengthening development of the digital economy as well as leveraging science, technology and innovation (STI).",""],[1,"58","3","Commercialisation of Public Research Outputs","The commercialisation of R&D outputs by public research agencies will be increased to provide greater benefits to target groups.",""],[1,"63","3","STI Mainstreaming and Innovation Promotion Initiative","Efforts to mainstream STI in socioeconomic development will be intensified to ensure a competitive and sustainable economy.",""],[1,"63","3","Collaborative Technology Transfer and Investment Attraction Model","A more flexible collaborative model with various local and international counterparts will be explored to attract investment in accelerating technology transfer and promoting innovation.",""],[1,"63","3","Industry-Blueprint STEM Talent Pilot Project","A pilot project based on the blueprint developed by the industry will be implemented to ensure the science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) talent meet the industry need.",""],[1,"72","6","R&D&C&I Ecosystem Enhancement and Strengthening","Enhancement and strengthening of R&D&C&I ecosystem will advance economic complexity, ensure environmental sustainability and improve the wellbeing of the rakyat, in line with efforts to raise the ceiling and strengthen governance.",""],[1,"72","6","Whole-of-Nation Stakeholder Collaboration for Innovation","Thus, collaboration among all stakeholders, including public agencies, the private sector and research institutions at various levels based on the whole-of- nation approach needs to be intensified to achieve this goal.",""],[1,"74","1","R&D&C&I Investment and Incentive Model Reform","Strengthening of the R&D&C&I ecosystem will focus on efforts to establish a more efficient as well as progressive investment and incentive model, in addition to reforming IP policies.",""],[1,"74","1","Intellectual Property Policy Reform","Strengthening of the R&D&C&I ecosystem will focus on efforts to establish a more efficient as well as progressive investment and incentive model, in addition to reforming IP policies.",""],[1,"74","1","R&D&C&I Governance Improvement","Measures will also be undertaken to enhance the development of skilled and future-proof talent as well as ensure better governance.",""],[1,"74","2","R&D&C&I Investment Model Improvement","The R&D&C&I investment model will be improved by providing research facilities and targeted incentives to increase investment and high-value researches.",""],[1,"74","3","Intellectual Property Commercialisation and Management Strengthening","The role of IP as a foundation in value creation to advance economic complexity will be strengthened by increasing commercialisation, leveraging IP as an asset and improving management efficiency.",""],[1,"74","4","Public Higher-Education and Research IP Commercialisation Support","commercialisation of high-value IP owned by public HEIs and GRIs will be increased.",""],[1,"74","4","IP Return Generation Business Model Enhancement","the business model for generating returns from IP will be enhanced as a guidance for these institutions.",""],[1,"74","4","Government-Backed IP Collateralisation Pilot Project","A pilot project on collateralisation of IP, backed by government, will be implemented to increase access to commercialisation financing.",""],[1,"74","4","Online IP Bidding and Trading Mechanism","online IP bidding and trading mechanism will be introduced to increase commercialisation and link researchers to potential investors.",""],[1,"74","5","Investor Incentive Conditions for New Intellectual Property Creation and Registration","The conditions for granting of incentives to investors will be improved by incorporating elements of creation and registration of new IP in Malaysia.",""],[1,"74","5","Patent Registration and Approval Cooperation Expansion","The management of IP registration and approval will be strengthened through more international collaborations under the Patent Prosecution Highway and the ASEAN Patent Examination Cooperation programme.",""],[1,"74","5","Intellectual Property Valuation Regulation Review","Policies and legislation related to regulation of IP valuation profession will be explored to ensure the credibility of valuation reports.",""],[1,"74","5","Technology Transfer Officer Recruitment and Career Guidelines","Guidelines on the recruitment and career prospects of technology transfer officers at public HEIs and GRIs will also be developed.",""],[1,"74","6","STEM Research and Technology Exposure in Primary School","Talent in R&D&C&I will be nurtured since primary school through exposure to scientific research and technology development activities by leveraging AI and AR in STEM- based co-curricular activities.",""],[1,"74","6","Problem-Based R&D Skills Learning Programme","The development of R&D skills among students will be enhanced through the implementation of specific learning programme based on local problems involving researchers in collaboration with state governments and the private sector.",""],[1,"74","6","Human Resources Development Fund for R&D Training","In addition, the Human Resources Development Fund will be utilised to develop specific training programmes related to R&D to be implemented by HEIs together with industry players, including for placement of researchers in the industry.",""],[1,"74","6","Research Manager Capacity-Building Programme","Structured training related to management of fund, finance and project will also be strengthened to enhance the capability of research managers in the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"75","1","R&D&C&I Governance Enhancement and Monitoring Reform","The governance of R&D&C&I will be enhanced by improving planning and monitoring mechanisms, refining programme approaches as well as restructuring GRI functions and roles.",""],[1,"75","1","R&D&C&I Satellite Account Development","A specific satellite account will be developed to strengthen evidence-based planning, monitoring and impact assessment of R&D&C&I investment.",""],[1,"75","1","Periodic Megatrend Analysis Report","A periodic megatrend analysis report using the foresight approach will also be produced as guidance and reference for the implementation of R&D&C&I activities.",""],[1,"75","2","National Mission-Based Research Programmes","The R&D&C&I programme approach will be strengthened through the introduction of the national mission-based research programmes that emphasise on applied and experimental development research.",""],[1,"75","2","Cross-Ministry R&D Moonshot Programmes","The R&D moonshot programmes involving selected projects will be implemented across ministries to explore creation of disruptive technologies, including those related to AI.",""],[1,"75","2","GRI Rationalisation and Performance Reform","The rationalisation of the roles and functions of all GRIs will also be carried out to ensure a more lean and efficient structure.",""],[1,"75","2","GRI Effectiveness Rating and Performance-Based Budgeting","This measure will be supported by introducing a rating system to assess the effectiveness of GRIs and implementing performance-based budgeting.",""],[1,"75","2","National Action Plan for R&D Infrastructure Management","A national action plan on the enhancement of R&D&C&I infrastructure management will be formulated to increase efficiency of R&D assets utilisation.",""]],"120":[[1,"46","2","Nation-Building and Social Wellbeing Pillar","Focus will be given to efforts in building a nation-state, enhancing preparation towards an aged nation, reforming health and housing sectors, strengthening security and defence, preserving planetary health as well as improving disaster management.",""]],"121":[[1,"52","4","National Energy Transition Roadmap Implementation","A total of 10 flagship projects and 50 NETR initiatives are being implemented, with projected outcomes exceeding the targets in the aspects of job opportunities, investment commitments and reduction in greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions.",""],[1,"52","4","Hydro Hybrid Floating Solar Project","Among the flagship projects currently being implemented are the Hydro Hybrid Floating Solar in Kenyir, Terengganu, the Biofuel Hub in Pengerang, Johor and the Community Solar in Bandar Elmina, Selangor.",""],[1,"52","4","Biofuel Hub Development","Among the flagship projects currently being implemented are the Hydro Hybrid Floating Solar in Kenyir, Terengganu, the Biofuel Hub in Pengerang, Johor and the Community Solar in Bandar Elmina, Selangor.",""],[1,"52","4","Community Solar Project","Among the flagship projects currently being implemented are the Hydro Hybrid Floating Solar in Kenyir, Terengganu, the Biofuel Hub in Pengerang, Johor and the Community Solar in Bandar Elmina, Selangor.",""],[1,"52","4","Hydrogen-Based Autonomous Rail Transit Project","In line with the initiatives to enhance green mobility, an autonomous rail transit project based on hydrogen technology was introduced in Sarawak, and mobile hydrogen refuelling station in",""],[1,"53","1","National Energy Transition Facility","the National Energy Transition Facility (NETF), a financing facility amounting to RM2 billion was launched to support energy transition-based initiatives.",""],[1,"56","1","Energy Transition Acceleration","Efforts for HGHV industries will focus on reforming the semiconductor industry, accelerating energy transition, developing the REE value chain, diversifying high-value agriculture products, strengthening development of the digital economy as well as leveraging science, technology and innovation (STI).",""],[1,"63","6","Green Economy Investment and Export Expansion","Strengthening of the green economy will increase investment in the development of new low carbon industries as well as expand the exports of high value green products and services.",""],[1,"65","1","Green Economy Strengthening Agenda","During the Thirteenth Plan period, the implementation of the agenda to strengthen the green economy will be intensified in ensuring economic resilience and environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"65","6","Blended Finance for Energy Transition Projects","Blended financing under NETF will be increased through collaboration between implementing agencies and private financing partners to accelerate energy transition projects.",""]],"122":[[1,"53","7","Capital Market Masterplan 2021-2025 Implementation","Under the implementation of the Capital Market Masterplan 2021-2025, various initiatives were introduced, including the Catalysing Access for MSMEs and MTCs to the Capital Market: 5-Year Roadmap (2024-2028), the National Sustainability Reporting Framework, the Practical Guide on Venture Capital and Equity as well as the VC Golden Pass.",""],[1,"61","7","Fourth Capital Market Masterplan","The fourth capital market masterplan will be developed to drive a more inclusive and resilient capital market transformation, as well as to enhance innovation and",""],[1,"62","1","Islamic Capital Market Strengthening","The Islamic capital market will continue to be strengthened through the application of Magasid Shariah concept to create a sustainable, inclusive and ethical investment ecosystem in line with the principles of the Ekonomi MADANI.",""],[1,"62","1","Venture Capital and Private Equity Ecosystem Development","Focus will also be given on efforts to strengthen the VC and PE market ecosystem through activities such as facilitating fund establishment and enhancing fund raising capability.",""]],"123":[[1,"56","1","Semiconductor Industry Reform","Efforts for HGHV industries will focus on reforming the semiconductor industry, accelerating energy transition, developing the REE value chain, diversifying high-value agriculture products, strengthening development of the digital economy as well as leveraging science, technology and innovation (STI).",""],[1,"56","2","National Semiconductor Industry Reform and Strategic Collaboration Programme","various strategic collaborations under the NSS will be implemented with global and local semiconductor companies along the value chain to accelerate the industry transition to produce more complex and high-value products.",""]],"124":[[1,"56","3","Circular Economy and AI-Based Supply Chain Digitalisation","The investment ecosystem will be strengthened by integrating the circular economy and AI-based digitalisation in domestic supply chains.",""],[1,"56","3","Investment Incentives and Alternative Financing for Knowledge-Based Investment","Investment incentives and financing will prioritise IP-based investment as well as alternative financing, such as credit guarantee and venture capital to accelerate the transition to more targeted and competitive knowledge-based investment.",""],[1,"56","3","Industry-Based Skills Training Expansion","Skills training programmes conducted fully in industry will be further expanded to increase invention capacity, driven by quality talent.",""]],"125":[[1,"56","5","Innovative Electricity Market System","An electricity market system based on a more innovative mechanism will be established to ensure quality and reliable electricity supply services.",""],[1,"57","1","Electricity Market Liberalisation Mechanism","of this new mechanism will focus on transparent and viable generation procurement, the development of an independent grid system and the establishment of a market operator towards liberalising the electricity supply industry.",""],[1,"57","1","Smart Meter Deployment Expansion","The deployment of smart meters will be expanded to enable consumers to fully leverage the Time of Use electricity tariffs scheme, which was introduced in July 2025 to promote more cost-efficient electricity consumption.",""],[1,"57","1","Renewable Energy Market Competitiveness Measures","The competitiveness of the energy market will be enhanced through the utilisation of various renewable energy (RE) sources and new technologies, such as participation of self-consumption generators.",""],[1,"57","1","Grid Flexibility and Electricity Infrastructure Upgrade","The grid flexibility will be strengthened through the implementation of battery energy storage systems and smart grid as well as the development of electricity supply infrastructure.",""],[1,"57","1","National Energy Efficiency Action Plan and Labelling Expansion","energy demand management will be strengthened through the introduction of the second national energy efficiency action plan and thermal energy efficiency guidelines as well as the expansion of energy efficiency labelling for industrial sector equipment.",""],[1,"57","2","Corporate Renewable Energy Supply Scheme Enhancement","Supply initiatives based on third-party access, such as the Corporate Renewable Energy Supply Scheme, will be enhanced as among the methods in obtaining new RE-based resources regardless of locality.",""],[1,"57","2","Community Renewable Energy Aggregation Mechanism","The implementation of the Community Renewable Energy Aggregation Mechanism will enable RE generation under the open grid access concept through the collective installation of solar photovoltaic systems on rooftops of residential premises.",""],[1,"57","2","Vietnam-Malaysia-Singapore Green Electricity Interconnection Project","In addition, green electricity interconnection project between Vietnam, Malaysia and Singapore to transmit RE will be implemented, supporting the ASEAN Power Grid vision in establishing a resilient, sustainable and interconnected energy market between countries.",""],[1,"57","2","Sarawak-Peninsular Malaysia Grid Interconnection Project","In line with the aspiration of Sarawak as the RE hub based on hydropower, grid interconnection project from Sarawak to Peninsular Malaysia will be implemented.",""]],"126":[[1,"57","3","Nuclear Energy Development Programme for Electricity Generation","The nuclear energy development programme for electricity generation as a clean energy source in the national energy mix will be implemented and is expected to begin operation in 2031.",""],[1,"57","3","National Nuclear Programme Governance and Implementation Coordination","MyPOWER Corporation will serve as the Nuclear Energy Programme Implementing Organization, responsible for the governance of the national nuclear programme, in accordance with the International Atomic Energy Agency.",""],[1,"57","3","Nuclear Energy Communication, Education, and Public Awareness Programme","This entity will coordinate the implementation of communication, education and public awareness (CEPA) programmes, investment in new infrastructure, strengthening of research and development (R&D) and expert training as well as international cooperation on nuclear energy.",""]],"127":[[1,"59","4","Air Mobility Expansion and Roadmap Development","The air mobility3, as one of the high-impact strategic sectors will be expanded by adopting advanced technologies in the creation and production of aerial vehicles as well as by integrating the usage within the national transportation network.",""],[1,"59","5","Unmanned Valley Controlled Airspace Ecosystem","The ecosystem for 'Unmanned Valley' or a controlled airspace zone will be established through collaboration with industry players to accelerate the adaptation to UAS and AAM technologies.",""]],"128":[[1,"56","1","Air Transport Industry Expansion","the development of high impact strategic sectors will emphasise efforts to expand the air transport industry as well as strengthen the tourism, halal and creative industries.",""],[1,"59","7","Air Transport Fleet Expansion and Route Development","The expansion of the air transport industry will be strengthened through strategic investment by local airline companies to increase flight operations within Malaysia and to international destinations.",""]],"129":[[1,"56","1","Tourism Industry Strengthening","the development of high impact strategic sectors will emphasise efforts to expand the air transport industry as well as strengthen the tourism, halal and creative industries.",""],[1,"60","1","Tourism Zone Development Initiative","The development of a high-income and sustainable tourism industry will focus on efforts in establishing specific tourism zones, maintaining the sustainability of tourism products as well as leveraging art, cultural and heritage assets.",""],[1,"60","1","Potential Tourism Investment Zones Development","Potential tourism investment zones will be developed as a strategic measure to provide new tourism products that can attract more domestic and international investors.",""],[1,"60","1","Tourism Connectivity Enhancement","Physical connectivity through land, sea and air as well as digital connectivity will be enhanced to support the development of the zones.",""],[1,"60","1","Homestay Tourism Programme Strengthening","In addition, tourism initiatives based on homestay programmes will be strengthened to increase income-generating opportunities, particularly for rural population.",""],[1,"60","2","Sustainable Tourism Area Monitoring and Impact Assessment Mechanism","Measurement and monitoring of sustainability of tourism areas will be introduced in the effort to ensure selected national tourism destinations meet international standards.",""]],"130":[[1,"60","3","Arts, Cultural and Heritage Asset Revitalisation","The art, cultural and heritage assets will be revitalised with new innovations to catalyse the tourism industry development and promote the development of the orange economy.",""],[1,"60","3","Digital Creative Content Development for Tourism","Latest technologies, such as augmented reality (AR) and virtual reality will be leveraged in developing creative content to enrich and enhance tourist experience.",""],[1,"60","3","Historic and Heritage Site Upgrading Partnership","In this regard, collaboration with state governments will be intensified to upgrade key historic and heritage sites, including the Archaeological Heritage of Lenggong Valley in Perak, the Sungai Batu and the Lembah Bujang archaeological sites in Kedah, the Gua Bewah in Terengganu as well as the Warisan KL4.",""],[1,"60","3","Heritage-Based Tourism Package and Trail Promotion","Collaboration with various stakeholders will also be implemented to promote heritage-based tourism packages and trails.",""],[1,"60","5","Heritage-Based Urban Regeneration and Tourism Revitalization Initiative","a strategic initiative based on the Kuala Lumpur Local Plan 2040, that leverages arts, culture and heritage as the thrust of urban regeneration and national identity, to revitalise heritage-based tourism in Kuala Lumpur.",""]],"131":[[1,"61","3","Global Technology Centre and Single Family Office Investment Promotion","The development of the GS industry will focus on attracting quality investment with high spillover effects, such as in the development of global technology centres and the Single Family Office Management Company5 as well as R&D and exploration of sophisticated products.",""],[1,"61","3","Foreign Investor Collaboration for Services Value Chain Upgrading","Local professional service providers will be encouraged to collaborate with foreign investors in enhancing competitiveness and penetrating the services value chain at the global level.",""],[1,"61","3","Green and Sustainable Practices Enforcement","Enforcement of green and sustainable practices will also be strengthened to ensure the GS industry players comply with existing legislation and guidelines.",""]],"132":[[1,"61","6","Financial Data Sharing Enhancement","Financial data sharing will be augmented, particularly through the use of a more supportive and innovative alternative data6.",""],[1,"61","6","Digital Financial Innovation Sandbox Expansion","The potential of new technologies, such as digital asset, blockchain, asset tokenisation and central bank digital currencies as well as expansion of sandbox will be explored to drive digital innovation.",""],[1,"61","6","Digital Financial Literacy and Banking Adoption Programme","Efforts will continue to be intensified to improve digital financial literacy as well as encourage the adoption of digital banking services among the rakyat.",""],[1,"61","6","Inclusive Financial Products Expansion","The offering of financial products specifically tailored for vulnerable groups, such as the B40 group, older persons and persons with disabilities will be expanded to ensure all segments of the rakyat have equitable access to financial services.",""],[1,"61","6","Blended Financing Mechanism Enhancement","In addition, the blended financing mechanism will be enhanced to enable businesses to access various sources of capital in mitigating investment risks.",""],[1,"65","6","Green Financing Expansion and Blended Finance Platform","Access to green financing will be enhanced through the strengthening of SMEs project viability, participation of more private financing providers and introduction of new financing programmes.",""],[1,"65","6","SME Green Project Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building programmes for SMEs in designing viable green projects in order to access existing financing, such as the Low Carbon Transition Facility, Green Technology Financing Scheme 5.0 and Sustainable Green Biz Financing will be intensified.",""],[1,"65","6","Green Decarbonisation Financing Programmes","In addition, new green financing programmes that support decarbonisation efforts through energy efficiency, RE generation, waste management and low-carbon technologies adoption, particularly in the manufacturing sector, will be explored.",""]],"133":[[1,"62","3","Retail Internationalisation and Capacity Building Support","Capacity building initiatives and assistance to participate in trade missions and establish businesses abroad will be improved.",""],[1,"62","3","Franchise Act Review and Self-Regulation Study","A study will be undertaken to improve the Franchise Act 1998 [Act 590] and assess the feasibility of implementing a self- regulatory system.",""],[1,"62","3","Retail Digitalisation Acceleration Initiative","efforts will be intensified to accelerate digitalisation among small and medium retailers to enhance competitiveness and resilience as well as scale up businesses.",""],[1,"62","3","Targeted Retail Support Programmes","Retailers will also be supported through the implementation of targeted programmes to enhance capacity and capability, strengthening of supply chain and improvement in access to need-based financing.",""],[1,"62","4","Unit Pricing Disclosure Amendment","The Price Control Order Regulations 1980 will be amended in mandating traders to display unit pricing in addition to the retail price.",""],[1,"62","4","Consumer Price Awareness Advocacy Programme","Advocacy programmes will be intensified to raise awareness and assist consumers to make smarter decisions as well as prevent price manipulation by traders.",""]],"134":[[1,"63","4","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Intensity Reduction Target","Malaysia is committed to achieve the target of 45% reduction in GHG emissions intensity to GDP in 2030 based on the emissions intensity in 2005.",""],[1,"65","2","National Carbon Market Policy and Carbon Trading Scheme","Carbon trading in compliance with the carbon reduction commitment under the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change will be intensified through the implementation of a national carbon market policy and enactment of a legislation related to climate change.",""],[1,"65","2","Carbon Emission Trading Scheme","A carbon emission trading scheme will be established as a mechanism to facilitate carbon trading.",""],[1,"65","2","Carbon Credit Project Incentives and Regulatory Compliance Streamlining","In addition, provision of incentives and regulatory compliance for the implementation of carbon credit projects will be streamlined at the Federal and state levels.",""],[1,"65","2","Carbon Emission Measurement and GHG Monitoring System","Carbon emission measurement and progress monitoring of the GHG reduction targets in the energy sector will be strengthened to ensure more effective planning and mitigation action plan.",""],[1,"65","2","National Energy Outlook Report","In this regard, a comprehensive national energy outlook report will be produced as a main reference on future carbon emission trend.",""],[1,"65","3","CCUS Initiative Intensification and Regulatory Framework Enhancement","The implementation of CCUS initiatives as a new source of economic growth which began in the Twelfth Plan period will be intensified to support the development of the green economy and the low-carbon economy.",""],[1,"65","4","Carbon Capture, Utilization and Storage Taxonomy Inclusion","CCUS activities will be included as part of the green investment and financing taxonomy to facilitate industry participation.",""],[1,"65","4","R&D&C&I Technology Collaboration Strengthening","The R&D&C&I activities will be strengthened, particularly to identify appropriate and cost-effective technologies through strategic collaborations between research institutions and industry players.",""],[1,"65","5","Bilateral CO2 Cross-Border Transportation Agreements","Bilateral agreements on CO2 cross-border transportation activities with Japan, the Republic of Korea and Singapore will be signed",""],[1,"65","5","Pilot CO2 Capture Project in the Iron and Steel Industry","a pilot CO2 capture project in the iron and steel industry will be implemented in Kemaman, Terengganu",""],[1,"65","5","CO2 Utilisation Exploration Initiative","the utilisation of CO2 sourced from the capture activities will be explored",""],[1,"65","5","SME Participation in CCUS Value Chain","The participation of SMEs, including oil and gas services and equipment (OGSE) companies across the CCUS value chain will be encouraged",""],[1,"65","5","CCUS Talent Development and Technology Transfer Collaboration","The development of local talent and expertise will be enhanced through technology transfer by undertaking strategic collaborations with foreign countries",""]],"135":[[1,"66","6","Blue Economy Blueprint","The Malaysia Blue Economy Blueprint was introduced in 2025 to holistically drive the development of the blue economy strategic sectors for the period from 2025 to 2030.",""],[1,"66","6","ASEAN Blue Economy Coordination and Forum Engagement","Malaysia also chaired the ASEAN Coordinating Task Force on Blue Economy (ACTF-BE) Meeting and organised the ASEAN Blue Economy Forum, in 2025 in conjunction with the ASEAN chairmanship.",""],[1,"68","1","Blue Economy Accounting System","Data and information on the blue economy will be integrated through the development of blue accounting to facilitate comprehensive and coordinated planning, development and monitoring.",""],[1,"68","1","Marine Bioprospecting Profile Bank","A marine bioprospecting profile bank will also be established to encourage R&D&C&I in boosting the blue economy activities.",""],[1,"68","6","Blue Economy Financing and Incentives Support","Existing financial incentives will be strengthened, and sustainable blue economy funding and financing, such as blended financing mechanisms will be explored to support the growth of strategic blue economy industries.",""],[1,"68","6","Marine Industry Technology Modernisation and Automation","The adoption of advanced technology in the marine industry will be expanded, particularly for the modernisation and automation of fishing, shipping and port activities as well as marine bioprospecting screening.",""],[1,"68","6","Regional Blue Economy Collaboration and Capacity Development","In addition, collaboration at the regional level in various fields will be intensified, encompassing R&D&C&I activities, technology transfer, expertise sharing and talent development.",""],[1,"68","6","Blue Economy Hub Development in Selected States","Blue economy hub will be developed in potential states such as Kelantan, Perak, Sabah and Terengganu to attract investment in strategic blue economy industries.",""],[1,"68","6","Youth Participation in High-Income Blue Economy Activities","Local experience and expertise in strategic industries will be recognised and leveraged to attract youth participation in blue economy activities that offer high income.",""]],"136":[[1,"67","7","Comprehensive Ocean Policy Development","A comprehensive ocean policy will be developed to manage and govern national maritime activities in a unified manner.",""],[1,"67","7","Marine Spatial Planning Support","The implementation of this policy will be supported by developing a marine spatial plan.",""],[1,"67","7","Seabed Mineral Extraction Policy and Legislation","The formulation of a policy and legislation on the extraction of minerals with great economic potential in the seabed will also be explored.",""],[1,"67","7","Federal Ports Governance Review","the management of the Federal ports will be enhanced through a comprehensive review of existing acts to avoid duplication of roles and responsibilities of the port authorities.",""]],"137":[[1,"67","7","National Shipping Industry Strengthening Policy","A policy to strengthen the national shipping industry, including by increasing the ship operations of local companies will be formulated to reduce dependency on foreign ships.",""],[1,"67","7","Local Company Ship Acquisition Programme","136 new ships will be acquired by local companies of which are expected to generate more than 840,000 gross tonnage in 2030.",""],[1,"68","2","Green Shipping and Bunkering Industry Upgrade","The strengthening of the national SBSR industry will prioritise efforts in attracting investment to improve capacity in green shipping and local bunkering activities.",""],[1,"68","2","Blue Economy Governance and Green Fuels Regulatory Framework","This improvement will involve the formulation of a regulatory framework to coordinate governance and expand the use of green fuels, as well as the upgrading of bunkering infrastructure at major ports by the private sector.",""],[1,"68","2","Port Infrastructure Expansion and Terminal Development","In addition, port infrastructure will be strengthened to support the growth of the blue economy through the development of more advanced, efficient and sustainable terminals.",""],[1,"68","2","Sustainable Port Capacity Expansion in Sabah and Sarawak","Port capacities in Sabah and Sarawak will also be increased to support economic growth.",""]],"138":[[1,"67","8","Pollution Management and Prevention Governance Strengthening","Legislation and governance related to pollution management and prevention will be strengthened to improve coordination, efficiency and effectiveness of measures in protecting the marine and coastal ecosystems.",""],[1,"67","8","Blue Carbon Policy and Trading Platform Development","policies and guidelines related to blue carbon will be developed, and a trading platform will be explored to enable the implementation of blue carbon credits as a new source of economic growth.",""],[1,"68","1","Blue Carbon Credits Assessment Mechanism","developing a blue carbon credits assessment mechanism will be explored.",""],[1,"68","6","Ocean Waste Management and Blue Carbon Innovation Initiative","The use of technology and innovation will also be given focus in ocean waste management, environmental conservation and blue carbon initiatives.",""]],"139":[[1,"67","5","Fishing Vessel Shipyard Upgrade Programme","Fishing vessel shipyards built or upgraded with facilities for shipbuilding as well as maintenance, repair and overhaul",""],[1,"68","3","Integrated Fisheries Hubs Development","Sustainable capture fisheries and aquaculture industries will be revitalised through the establishment of integrated fisheries hubs equipped with ports and logistics facilities that support activities along the value chain.",""],[1,"68","3","Integrated Fishing Vessel Shipyard Upgrading","The construction and upgrading of integrated fishing vessel shipyards, that include facilities for shipbuilding as well as maintenance, repair and overhaul, will be encouraged at these hubs.",""],[1,"68","3","Fisheries Hub Incentives and Support Measures","In this regard, incentives and supports will be provided to increase the capacity and contribution",""],[1,"68","4","Aquaculture Industry Strengthening Programme","the aquaculture industry will be strengthened through the development of quality brood stocks and seedlings, adoption of innovation and advanced technology as well as increased investment opportunities to produce high-value outputs.",""]],"140":[[1,"68","5","Coastal and Island Sustainable Tourism Product Enhancement","Coastal and island tourism products will be strengthened to improve sustainable tourism destinations.",""],[1,"68","5","Sustainable Tourism Standards Compliance Improvement","Tourism products that do not comply with international sustainable standards based on the International Network of Sustainable Tourism Observatories will be improved to support the development of the blue economy.",""],[1,"68","5","Blue Renewable Energy Technology and Investment Assessment","The potential of the blue RE industry will be assessed through the exploration of technology viability, project feasibility and required investment.",""],[1,"68","5","OGSE and Blue Renewable Energy Collaboration Network","OGSE activities will be diversified, particularly through the collaborative networks between OGSE and blue RE industry players at the domestic and international levels in increasing expertise and workforce.",""]],"141":[[1,"78","5","Dana Ihsan MADANI Flood Relief Contributions","Contributions amounting to RM35.8 million from 23 private companies were received in 2024 through the Dana Ihsan MADANI for flood victims nationwide, reflecting the commitment of all stakeholders in the efforts to strengthen flood mitigation and adaptation through the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[1,"80","1","Immediate Financial Assistance and Microcredit for MSME Recovery","Immediate interventions in the form of financial assistance and microcredit will be provided to accelerate the recovery process and reduce the financial burden of MSMEs.",""],[1,"80","1","Post-Flood Financing Scheme and Insurance Coverage","financial institutions and non- bank financial institutions will be encouraged to provide post-flood financing scheme and insurance coverage.",""],[1,"80","1","Affordable Insurance Schemes for Post-Flood Financial Protection","The introduction of affordable insurance schemes will be explored in increasing access of vulnerable groups to post-flood financial protection.",""],[1,"80","2","Central Disaster Management Committee Strengthening","The role of the Central Disaster Management Committee will also be strengthened to ensure an integrated, efficient, fast, and effective coordination.",""],[1,"80","2","Community-Based Disaster Risk Management Programme","Strategic collaborations among all stakeholders will be strengthened to ensure more integrated and effective flood management, including through the implementation of the Community-Based Disaster Risk Management Programme.",""]],"142":[[1,"77","1","Productivity Growth and Competition Ecosystem Strengthening","Focus will be given on efforts to spur productivity growth and strengthen the competition ecosystem.",""],[1,"77","2","National Productivity Framework and Roadmap","A comprehensive productivity framework and roadmap will be developed to improve competitiveness at the firm, industry and sectoral levels.",""],[1,"77","2","Productivity Institution Rationalisation and Oversight Reform","the functions and roles of productivity related institutions will be rationalised to strengthen planning, monitoring and regulatory oversight of productivity enhancement interventions.",""],[1,"77","2","Productivity Enhancement Legislation and Regulatory Mechanism Reform","a new legislation will be enacted, and the existing regulatory mechanism will be improved.",""],[1,"77","2","Firm-Level Productivity Screening Programme","A firm-level productivity screening programme, which evaluates the capability and efficiency of business processes will be introduced to facilitate policy interventions and provision of targeted support.",""],[1,"77","2","Locality-Based Productivity Collaboration Programmes","The roles of the productivity nexus will also be strengthened through the implementation of specific locality-based programmes, which involve collaboration with research institutions and subject matter experts.",""],[1,"77","3","MSME Financing Criteria for Productivity and Competitiveness","In addition, strengthening of productivity and competitiveness will be made as an important criteria in the provision of financing for MSMEs.",""],[1,"77","3","Streamlining of Grants and Funds","Various grants and funds will also be streamlined to avoid overlapping.",""],[1,"77","4","Progressive Wage Policy Implementation","Emphasis will be given on improving labour productivity through the full implementation of the Progressive Wage Policy which commenced in 2025.",""],[1,"77","4","Productivity Mindset Communication and Awareness Programme","The communication, education and awareness programme on productivity mindset as well as changes in work culture among firms will be implemented.",""],[1,"77","5","Comprehensive Competition Legislation Reform","The competition ecosystem will be strengthened through the provision of a more comprehensive and effective competition legislation.",""],[1,"77","5","Single Competition Regime for Multiple Industries","all industries including communications and multimedia, civil aviation as well as energy will be regulated under a single competition legislation.",""],[1,"77","6","Rent-Seeking Legislation","A comprehensive and integrated legislation related to rent-seeking will be introduced.",""]],"143":[[1,"82","3","Rail Public Transport Governance Restructuring","The governance of rail-based public transport will be restructured to improve the efficiency of agencies responsible for regulation, asset ownership and operations.",""],[1,"82","3","Separation of Rail Asset Ownership and Operations","Efforts will be continued to fully implement the separation of functions and responsibilities between asset owners and rail operators.",""],[1,"82","4","Rail Track Charges Reform","track charges will be explored to enable more services to be offered to passengers and encourage more freight transportation via rail.",""]],"144":[[1,"84","4","SME ESG Training and Mentoring Programme","The phased transition of SMEs in adopting the ESG principles based on the NESP will be accelerated through the implementation of more training and mentoring programmes, driven by anchor companies in the supply chain.",""],[1,"84","5","Comprehensive MSME Development Legislation","The MSME ecosystem will be improved with a provision of a comprehensive legislation to regulate MSME development.",""],[1,"84","5","Standardisation of MSME Definitions","The various definitions of MSMEs will be standardised to ensure support programmes designs are more targeted based on the potential and size of enterprises.",""],[1,"84","5","MSME Sustainable Financing Reform","The financing mechanisms of MSMEs will be streamlined, shifting from grant-based approach to sustainable financing, such as tiered and targeted financing.",""],[1,"84","5","Tiered MSME Loan Financing Model","Eligible MSMEs will be offered loans based on a tiered financing model, which sets varying interest rates or conditions depending on loan amount.",""],[1,"84","5","Targeted Financing for Innovative MSMEs","Targeted financing facilities will be provided to support innovative businesses and high value-added activities in priority and potential industries.",""],[1,"84","5","MSME Insurance, Takaful, and Guarantee Financing Expansion","Funding from insurance and takaful companies will be explored and guarantee schemes under the Syarikat Jaminan Pembiayaan Perniagaan will be fully leveraged.",""],[1,"84","5","ESG Financing Support for SMEs","In addition, anchor companies in business supply chains will be encouraged to facilitate SMEs access to financing for the adoption of ESG principles.",""]],"145":[[1,"87","1","AI-Nation Economic Transformation","Thus, the Thirteenth Plan will focus on pivoting towards a value creation-based economy anchored on AI nation by advancing economic complexity.",""],[1,"87","1","Innovation and Advanced Technology Adoption Initiative","Challenges and opportunities arising from megatrends pave the way for the nation to strengthen capabilities and competitiveness by focusing on accelerating innovation and adopting advanced technology as well as developing future-ready talent.",""],[1,"87","1","Future-Ready Talent Development Programme","Challenges and opportunities arising from megatrends pave the way for the nation to strengthen capabilities and competitiveness by focusing on accelerating innovation and adopting advanced technology as well as developing future-ready talent.",""]],"146":[[1,"90","1","Education and Labour Market Reform for Social Mobility","Priority will be given to the implementation of major transformations, particularly by reforming education and labour market, strengthening inclusive development as well as elevating the socioeconomic status of target groups in the efforts to raise the floor.",""],[1,"90","1","Inclusive Development and Target Group Upgrading Measures","Priority will be given to the implementation of major transformations, particularly by reforming education and labour market, strengthening inclusive development as well as elevating the socioeconomic status of target groups in the efforts to raise the floor.",""],[1,"90","1","TVET Ecosystem Strengthening","Measures to strengthen the Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) ecosystem and to balance regional economic development will be intensified to raise the ceiling.",""],[1,"90","1","Regional Economic Development Balancing Measures","Measures to strengthen the Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) ecosystem and to balance regional economic development will be intensified to raise the ceiling.",""],[1,"90","1","Governance Strengthening Measures","These major transformations will be complemented by efforts to strengthen governance.",""],[1,"92","2","Holistic Education Reform","A holistic education reform requires the commitment of all stakeholders, including parents, students, educators, society and the private sector, to be with the Government via the whole-of-nation approach in strengthening the national education system across the learning continuum.",""],[1,"94","1","National Education Reform Strategies","Eight strategies will be implemented to reform the national education during the Thirteenth Plan period, as follows:",""]],"147":[[1,"94","2","Education Governance Realignment and Service Delivery Reform","The education governance at all levels, from preschool to secondary as well as pre-university and higher education, will be realigned to enhance the effectiveness of education service delivery.",""],[1,"94","2","Early Childhood Education Regulatory Act","A new act will be enacted to regulate early childhood education, and measures will be undertaken to strengthen the regulatory mechanism for alternative education.",""],[1,"94","2","Alternative Education Regulatory Strengthening","A new act will be enacted to regulate early childhood education, and measures will be undertaken to strengthen the regulatory mechanism for alternative education.",""],[1,"94","2","National Education Council Establishment","A national education council, responsible for coordinating, monitoring and identifying interventions, will be established to ensure a progressive and world-class national education system.",""],[1,"94","2","University Autonomy Pilot Project","A pilot project to give autonomy to universities will also be implemented to improve financial sustainability and competitiveness of higher education institutions.",""],[1,"94","2","Internationalisation of Public Higher Education Institutions","Internationalisation of public higher education institutions will also be strengthened by amplifying international collaboration, improving academic programmes and expanding the implementation of twinning programmes to increase the institution competitiveness at the global level.",""],[1,"94","3","Education Institution Function Rationalisation and Restructuring","The functions and roles of education institutions will be rationalised to optimise resources and enhance the quality of national education.",""],[1,"94","4","Collaborative Networks for Professional Development, Research, and Innovation","rationalisation will involve strengthening of collaborative networks among institutions in undertaking continuous professional development training as well as research and innovation.",""]],"148":[[1,"95","5","Education Investment Efficiency Improvement","Investment in education will be improved to optimise the Government spending.",""],[1,"95","5","Expansion of Educational Facilities","The provision of educational facilities, including preschools, will be strengthened in accordance with learning needs.",""],[1,"95","5","School Construction Requirement for Large Housing Projects","Construction of schools will be instituted as one of the requirements under the Development Order for large scale housing projects in expediting the provision of educational facilities based on local needs.",""],[1,"95","5","Vertical School Construction Programme","The construction of vertical school will be increased to address the issues of overcrowded school and lack of suitable sites.",""],[1,"95","5","Community-Based School Expansion","Furthermore, community-based schools will be expanded for the Orang Asli community, residents of longhouses and population in remote areas.",""]],"149":[[1,"96","1","Education Sponsorship Alignment and Targeting Reform","Education sponsorships by the Government and government-linked companies (GLCs) will be improved to ascertain that fields of sponsorship are aligned with the actual needs of the nation and address the issue of talent migration.",""],[1,"96","1","Priority Support for Local Postgraduate Study","priority will be given to Malaysians pursuing postgraduate studies at local higher education institutions.",""],[1,"96","1","National Education Loan Scheme Review","The education loan scheme under the Perbadanan Tabung Pendidikan Tinggi Nasional will be reviewed to be more targeted, focused and sustainable.",""],[1,"96","1","Single National Education Sponsorship Platform","A single national platform for education sponsorships and contributions will also be established to enhance the efficiency and transparency in managing education financing.",""]],"150":[[1,"97","5","Academy in Industry Programme","the Academy in Industry (ADI), a programme based on industry demand, was implemented since 2023 to increase the participation of the local workforce.",""],[1,"97","5","Upskilling and Reskilling Programmes","The upskilling and reskilling programmes under the Human Resource Development Corporation succeeded in training a total of 3,886,470 workers from 2021 to 2024.",""],[1,"99","3","Expansion of the Dual-System Workforce Matching Mechanism","The dual-system mechanism based on the supply and demand of workforce will be expanded to ensure the provision of workforce is aligned with the skills required by industry.",""],[1,"99","3","Enhancement of ADI Based on Industry Demand","The implementation of the ADI based on industry demand will be enhanced in enabling workers to obtain the highest academic qualification instead of only the Malaysian Skills Certificate and Professional Diploma.",""],[1,"100","3","ADI Programme Expansion for Inclusive Participation","The ADI programme will be expanded to also focus on the participation of older persons, women and PWDs.",""],[1,"100","3","Inclusive Hiring Recognition Programme","initiatives related to equitability and inclusivity in the labour market will be improved by introducing a programme to recognise companies that hire older persons, women and PWDs.",""],[1,"100","3","Digital Economy Participation Expansion for Vulnerable Groups","Existing programmes, including those organised by social enterprises (SEs), will be expanded to encourage participation of older persons, women and PWDs in the digital economy.",""],[1,"100","4","Women’s Upskilling and Reskilling Programme","upskilling and reskilling programmes, specifically for women",""],[1,"100","5","Re-employment Support Measure","seeking re-employment will be introduced in building a more inclusive and responsive labour market.",""],[1,"104","2","Quality Education and Skills Training Enhancement","Access to quality and lifelong education and skills training, including TVET will be enhanced to improve the employability of household members, particularly of the low-income group.",""],[1,"104","2","Targeted Active Labour Market Support Expansion","job matching policy will be strengthened through the expansion of targeted active labour market support system.",""]],"151":[[1,"99","4","Integrated National Workforce Planning Platform","The national workforce planning will be enhanced through rationalisation of various workforce platforms into a single platform.",""],[1,"99","4","Integrated Coordination of Training and Skills Programmes","This effort will enable coordination of all training and skills programmes to be implemented in an integrated and comprehensive manner.",""],[1,"99","4","Skills Training Effectiveness Measurement Mechanism","In addition, a specific mechanism will be introduced to measure the effectiveness of skills training.",""]],"152":[[1,"103","3","Life-Cycle Healthcare Services for Poor Households","healthcare services for poor households will be improved through the life cycle approach, starting from prenatal stage to end of life.",""],[1,"103","3","First 1,000 Days of Life Initiative Expansion","health protection and care programmes, such as the First 1,000 Days of Life initiative, ... will be enhanced and expanded.",""],[1,"103","3","Rehabilitation Programme for Malnourished Children Expansion","health protection and care programmes, such as the ... Rehabilitation Programme for Malnourished Children ... will be enhanced and expanded.",""],[1,"103","3","MADANI Medical Scheme Expansion","health protection and care programmes, such as the ... MADANI Medical Scheme will be enhanced and expanded.",""],[1,"109","1","First 1,000 Days of Life Initiative","the First 1,000 Days of Life initiative will be strengthened to ensure physical and cognitive development of children is emphasised since conception.",""],[1,"109","1","National Strategic Plan to Combat the Double Burden of Malnutrition","implementation of the planning work for the National Strategic Plan to Combat the Double Burden of Malnutrition Among Malaysian Children, 2023-2030 will be intensified through the whole-of-nation approach.",""]],"153":[[1,"103","4","Housing Assistance Programme for Hardcore Poor Households","housing assistance programmes will be continued based on needs, including the construction of new and repair of dilapidated houses, particularly for hardcore poor households.",""],[1,"103","4","Rural Basic Services Infrastructure Expansion","the provision of infrastructure such as supply of clean water and electricity as well as broadband coverage will be enhanced in rural areas to enable access to necessary basic services and facilities.",""]],"154":[[1,"108","2","State-Level Integrated Economic Framework and Action Plan","An integrated economic framework and action plan at the state level will be introduced to guide the socioeconomic development of these target groups.",""],[1,"108","2","Federal-State Coordination Improvement Mechanism","Efforts will also be undertaken to improve coordination between the Federal and state agencies.",""]],"155":[[1,"108","5","Indian Community Social Mobility and Quality of Life Programmes","Initiatives and programmes to improve the social mobility of this community will be implemented based on the Malaysian Indian Blueprint and the Indian Community Action Plan.",""],[1,"108","5","Targeted Infrastructure, Amenities, and Housing Upgrading for Indian Households","Focus will be given to improve the quality of life through the provision of targeted programmes, including upgrading infrastructure and basic amenities as well as repairing of houses.",""],[1,"108","6","Indian Community Development and Governance Support Initiatives","Measures will also be undertaken to strengthen the economic, entrepreneurial and social development aspects, increase housing opportunities as well as improve the governance of the Indian community, including at the community level.",""],[1,"108","6","Micro-financing and Entrepreneurship Support Facilities","The implementation of these initiatives and programmes will be based on existing mechanisms, such as micro-financing facilities and entrepreneurship support, which will be further strengthened for greater inclusivity.",""],[1,"108","6","AI and Digitalisation Expansion for Targeting and Outcomes","The use of AI technology and digitalisation will be expanded to ensure accurate targets and maximum outcomes.",""]],"156":[[1,"108","7","Holistic Child Development Framework","A holistic framework for the development of children and the management of children wellbeing as well as a guideline on safety and disaster risk reduction for children will be developed.",""],[1,"109","2","Children's Participation in Decision-Making","the opinions of children will be considered in decision-making process at various levels, including in the Children Representative Council, as a measure to build a responsive and competitive future generation.",""]],"157":[[1,"109","6","Youth Long-Term Savings Investment Scheme","the introduction of amanah saham belia will be explored to encourage long-term investment and savings culture among the younger generation",""],[1,"109","6","Integrated Youth Housing Finance Support","integrated financing will be explored, including loan facilities for first home ownership with more flexible interest rates",""],[1,"109","6","Youth Financial Management Education Programme","Financial management education will be strengthened comprehensively to increase the level of financial literacy among youth",""]],"158":[[1,"110","3","Comprehensive Domestic Violence Response Partnership","Efforts will be implemented to address domestic violence comprehensively through a public-private partnership mechanism.",""],[1,"110","3","Women’s Information and Support Portal and Mobile Application","a one-stop portal and mobile application related to women will be developed as platforms to facilitate access to information, support and assistance on various issues, such as health, employment, rights of women and domestic violence.",""]],"159":[[1,"114","2","Rural Investment Hub Development","rural investment hubs will be developed by utilising geospatial AI and big data.",""],[1,"114","2","Specialised Industry Investment Promotion","Large- scale investment in specialised industries, including rare earth elements (REE), will be encouraged based on resource advantages of the regions.",""],[1,"114","2","Rural Workforce Skills Collaboration","local talent will be empowered through collaboration between training institutions, including TVET institutions and industry in ensuring rural workforce is equipped with skills that can support industrial growth.",""],[1,"114","2","Border Area Development and Connectivity Upgrade","Development in the border areas will be further intensified by improving basic infrastructure, enhancing security facilities and diversifying local economic activities.",""],[1,"114","2","Malaysia-Thailand Border Crossing Upgrade","access to the border areas will be improved through bilateral cooperations, among others, between Malaysia and Thailand with the upgrading of Rantau Panjang, Kelantan-Sg. Kolok, Narathiwat, Thailand Bridge",""],[1,"114","2","Kalabakan-Simanggaris Road Project Planning","as well as Malaysia and Indonesia with the planning of the Kalabakan to Simanggaris road project.",""]],"160":[[1,"114","4","Road Safety Infrastructure and Speed Monitoring Upgrade","Focus will also be given to road safety aspects by upgrading infrastructure, including the installation of street lights and traffic lights, in addition to the expansion of speed limit monitoring",""]],"161":[[1,"114","5","Planned Settlement Area Upgrading Programme","Efforts to empower the community in planned settlement areas, particularly the second and third generations will be implemented, including in the aspects of improvement in basic infrastructure, social amenities and housing as well as capacity building.",""],[1,"114","5","Village Infrastructure Upgrading Projects","the projects to be implemented include upgrading of village roads, drainage and irrigation systems as well as water supply, particularly in the settlements of the Federal Land Development Authority (FELDA), Federal Land Consolidation and Rehabilitation Authority (FELCRA) and regional development authorities (LKWs).",""],[1,"114","5","Education, TVET and Youth Entrepreneurship Support","investment in education and TVET as well as support for young entrepreneurs and in addressing social issues will be given focus to nurture a new generation that is competitive and progressive.",""],[1,"114","5","International Collaboration and Market Access Initiative","The FELDA and FELCRA communities will also be encouraged to participate in international collaborations such as the IMT-GT and the BIMP-EAGA to open up new market opportunities.",""]],"162":[[1,"114","5","Biodiversity, Renewable Energy and Solid Waste Initiatives","Biodiversity conservation, renewable energy initiatives and effective solid waste management will be explored in those areas to support the zero carbon agenda of the nation.",""]],"163":[[1,"114","6","Rural Digital Ecosystem Strengthening","The digital ecosystem in the rural areas will be strengthened to provide access and opportunities for rural communities to participate in the digital economy.",""],[1,"114","6","Entrepreneur Digital Skills Enhancement","Digital skills of entrepreneurs in managing operations and marketing of local products will be enhanced through strategic collaboration with various",""],[1,"115","1","E-commerce Tax Exemption Incentive for Rural Entrepreneurs","Tax exemption incentive on e-commerce transactions of products by rural entrepreneurs will also be explored.",""],[1,"115","1","Community Resource Centre Digital Hub Upgrade","Jabatan Kemajuan Masyarakat resource centres in areas without community digital centre facility will be upgraded to be digital hubs.",""]],"164":[[1,"115","5","Transit-Oriented Development Zone Expansion","Sustainable and inclusive urban development will be enhanced through the expansion of transit-oriented development (TOD) zones, which integrate housing, commercial and recreational components with the public transportation system.",""],[1,"115","5","Pedestrian and Micromobility Access Infrastructure","The implementation of TOD will be complemented with the provision of safe and easily accessible pedestrian and micromobility pathways as well as support facilities at terminals and stations.",""],[1,"115","5","Federal-State TOD Land Use Coordination Mechanism","In addition, cooperation between the Federal and state governments will be strengthened to coordinate land use planning in TOD zones and set a residential quota that comprises of 30% affordable houses, of which 20% priced below RM300,000 and 10% priced below RM150,000.",""]],"165":[[1,"115","6","Urban Growth Boundary Demarcation and Sprawl Control","Focused development in urban areas will be implemented through demarcation of urban growth boundaries to control urban sprawl and optimise land use.",""],[1,"115","6","Urban Management and Green Area Enhancement","In addition, measures to enhance the efficiency of urban management and services as well as the preservation of green areas, including the development of sustainable landscape and tree planting to address the issue of rising temperature will be emphasised.",""],[1,"115","6","Strategic Urban Revitalisation Projects","efforts will also be undertaken to revive the socioeconomic activities in selected cities, including in the Federal Territory of Labuan through the implementation of strategic projects.",""],[1,"115","6","Urban Consolidation of Adjacent Small and Medium Towns","The competitiveness and functionality of cities will be improved by merging adjacent small- and medium-sized towns to increase urban hierarchy.",""],[1,"115","6","Planned Settlement Urbanisation Acceleration","In addition, the focus of development will include measures to accelerate urbanisation in the planned settlement areas, particularly the FELDA, FELCRA and LKW areas.",""]],"166":[[1,"116","1","Malaysia Development Composite Index for Regional Gap Analysis","The Malaysia Development Composite Index (IKPM), as a comprehensive measurement tool, will be leveraged to identify development gaps at the regional, state and district levels.",""],[1,"116","4","Consolidated Rural Information Database","A consolidated rural information will be developed by integrating database of ministries and agencies, in line with the whole-of-government approach.",""],[1,"116","5","Integrated Spatial Database for Rural Development Planning","the Spatial Characteristics of Rural Malaysia System will be comprehensively used as an integrated spatial database for rural development planning.",""]],"167":[[1,"129","2","Syariah and Civil Court Jurisdiction Harmonisation Review","Focus will be given in reviewing legislation to ensure the harmonisation of jurisdiction between the Syariah and Civil Courts.",""],[1,"129","2","Syariah Judicial Remuneration and Appointment Reform Study","A study will be conducted in assessing the needs to enact a remuneration act for the Syarie Judge and establish a special commission for syariah judicial appointment in uplifting the dignity and independence of the Syariah judiciary.",""]],"168":[[1,"129","3","Extension of the Town and Country Planning Act to Sabah and Sarawak","The adoption of the Town and Country Planning Act 1976 [Act 172] will be extended to Sabah and Sarawak to strengthen the national spatial planning through the National Physical Plan, which comprises physical, economic, social and environmental development aspects.",""],[1,"129","3","National Land Use Planning Standardisation","This measure aims to ensure land use development planning is standardised across the country.",""],[1,"129","3","Land Use and Coastal Area Management Improvement","Planning and management of land use and coastal area will be improved to ensure sustainability of environment, balanced ecosystem as well as safety and wellbeing of communities.",""],[1,"129","3","Planning Permission Guideline and Coastal Inventory Development","In this regard, a guideline on planning and management as well as a coastal inventory will be developed to ensure Planning Permission process is regulated more effectively.",""]],"169":[[1,"129","7","Review of Retirement Benefits and Privileges","Policies related to retirement benefits and privileges of Members of the Administration and civil servants will also be reviewed to determine the best value for money.",""],[1,"129","7","Royal Commission of Inquiry on Public Sector Remuneration Reform","The assessment on the need to shift from a pension-based to a contribution-based remuneration schemes for all Members of the Administration and civil servants will be implemented through the establishment of the Royal Commission of Inquiry.",""],[1,"145","4","Mandatory Retirement Age Review for Civil Servants","The proposal to increase the mandatory retirement age of civil servants based on service schemes will be studied to enable the revision of the Pensions Act 1980 [Act 227].",""]],"170":[[1,"130","1","Civil Servant Support Services Improvement","The management of support services for civil servants, including in the aspects of psychology and counselling will be improved in ensuring civil servants are able to perform the duties with healthy mind and body.",""],[1,"130","1","Psychology Services Expansion at Urban Transformation Centres","the psychology services will be expanded and made available at the Urban Transformation Centres in facilitating civil servants to access counselling services.",""],[1,"130","1","Public Sector Mental Health Policy Implementation","the mental health policy will be implemented in the public sector to provide support services required by civil servants.",""],[1,"130","1","Civil Servant Job Satisfaction Study and Happiness Index","A study to assess job satisfaction levels will be conducted and a civil servant happiness index will be introduced as a guidance to identify initiatives in strengthening the public sector human resource development.",""]],"171":[[1,"130","4","Quality Infrastructure and Public Facilities Provision","The provision of quality infrastructure and services that are transparent, timely and thorough will also attract investors to start businesses, thus supporting economic growth.",""],[1,"130","6","Inisiatif Kemudahan Rakyat Small Projects Delivery Programme","The introduction of the Inisiatif Kemudahan Rakyat since June 2023, enabled the rakyat to benefit from the implementation of 2,181 high-impact small projects through direct request.",""],[1,"131","8","Turnkey and Design-Build Project Delivery Improvement","Turnkey as well as design-and-build project implementation models will also be improved and expanded, with more stringent cost control.",""],[1,"131","8","Multi-purpose Infrastructure Project Prioritisation","multi-purpose infrastructure projects will be prioritised in the Thirteenth Plan to optimise usage of resources.",""],[1,"131","8","Integrated Housing and Public Facilities Planning","Prospect of allocating part of spaces in large-scale high-rise residences for public facilities, such as schools and health clinics, will be explored to ensure housing development and provision of facilities are undertaken concurrently and in an integrated manner.",""],[1,"176","4","Integrated Infrastructure and Public Facilities Provision","The government is also responsible in ensuring the availability of comprehensive, integrated and quality infrastructure and public facilities to meet the needs of businesses, society and the rakyat in undertaking economic activities.",""]],"172":[[1,"131","9","Federal Land Bank Optimization for Federal Projects","The use of the Federal land bank will be maximised for development of the Federal projects through the improvement of land management procedures.",""],[1,"131","9","Centralized Federal Land Acquisition Process","land acquisition process will be centralised under the Department of Director General of Lands and Mines.",""],[1,"131","9","Private Delivery of Public Interest Projects on Surrendered Land","implementation of projects of public interest, such as schools and health clinics will be offered to private property developers to reduce issues related to abandoned and undeveloped surrendered land by developers.",""],[1,"151","3","Expanded Use of Federal Lands Commissioner, Malay Reserve and Waqf Lands","The use of the Federal Lands Commissioner, Malay Reserve and waqf lands will be expanded through collaboration between various parties to increase",""]],"173":[[1,"132","4","Revenue Base Expansion and Tax Reform Package","the expansion of the revenue base will continue to be undertaken, including through the revision of the rate and scope of the sales and services tax, the implementation of a global minimum tax and the introduction of carbon tax",""],[1,"132","4","Tax Incentive Optimization Linked to Investment Outcomes","the collection system will be enhanced by optimising the tax incentives to be closely correlated with investment outcomes",""],[1,"132","4","Digital Tax Administration Modernisation","Measures to enhance the efficiency of tax administration will also be continued through the digitalisation of the revenue collection system in order to reduce leakages and increase the taxpayer compliance level",""]],"174":[[1,"133","2","Integrated Social Economy Ecosystem Support","The setting of a clear policy direction as well as establishment of an integrated and holistic ecosystem support for the social economy, anchored on the thrust of good governance will enable the mainstreaming of the third sector as an important contributor to the socioeconomic development of the country.",""],[1,"133","2","Third Sector Participation for Social Mobility","The rakyat, as the target group, will have greater opportunities in enhancing social mobility by participating directly in economic activities together with the third sector players in line with the efforts to raise the floor.",""],[1,"133","2","Local Social Issue Resolution through Third Sector Engagement","The rakyat, as the third sector player, will also contribute in solving local social issues, such as poverty, education dropout and limitation in care services.",""],[1,"134","1","Social Economy Ecosystem Development","Efforts to establish a comprehensive and facilitative social economy ecosystem will be undertaken to enable the third sector players to continue scaling up and enhancing competitiveness as well as play a greater role, particularly in addressing socioeconomic issues of the rakyat.",""],[1,"134","2","Social Economy Expansion Action Plan","An action plan will be developed to expand social economy activities, based on an inclusive business model7.",""],[1,"134","3","Social Economy Awareness and Participation Campaign","Communication, education and public awareness activities will be intensified to increase awareness and foster greater involvement of organisations and the rakyat in the social economy activities.",""]],"175":[[1,"133","2","Transparent and Timely Service Delivery Improvement","The outcomes of these measures will enhance service delivery that is transparent, timely and thorough, as well as optimise the distribution of assistance to the rakyat.",""],[1,"133","5","Social Economy Policy Formulation","Formulation of a social economy policy",""],[1,"133","6","Social Economy Legislation Drafting","Drafting of legislation related to social economy",""],[1,"134","1","Social Economy Policy and Legislation Framework","focus will be given on establishing a comprehensive policy and legislation as well as strong governance.",""],[1,"134","2","Social Economy Policy Formulation","A policy on social economy will be formulated to provide direction for the development of a comprehensive and facilitative ecosystem.",""],[1,"134","2","Review and Alignment of Existing Social Economy Policies and Action Plans","existing policies and action plans will be reviewed and aligned to ensure no overlaps and fulfil the current needs of the third sector players inclusively.",""],[1,"134","3","Third Sector Procedures and Regulations Guideline","A guideline encompassing all aspects of procedures and regulations, including mechanisms for monitoring and reporting will be developed to enhance the capability of the third sector players.",""],[1,"134","3","Social Economy Impact Database","A comprehensive database will also be established to enable effective impact analysis and reporting of social economy.",""],[1,"134","4","Inclusive Legislation and Regulatory Reform","Inclusive legislation and regulations will be established, encompassing rules, licensing, auditing, resource allocation, oversight and enforcement aspects.",""],[1,"134","4","Streamlining of Business Oversight Laws","existing acts and regulations related to the oversight of business activities will be streamlined and realigned.",""],[1,"134","5","Social Economy Governance Rationalisation and Coordination Reform","Measures will be undertaken to rationalise relevant agencies in centralising governance and strengthening the management of the third sector.",""]],"176":[[1,"142","5","National Heritage Preservation and Access Enhancement","Malaysian artefacts abroad will be acquired to ensure the precious national treasures are preserved and valued by the rakyat.",""],[1,"142","5","National Heritage Digitalisation Initiative","In addition, digitalisation efforts will be intensified to preserve and expand access to the national treasures.",""],[1,"142","5","Library, Archive and Museum Services Enhancement","Library, archive and museum services will be enhanced in the efforts to increase awareness and preserve information related to the national heritage.",""]],"177":[[1,"142","6","Diplomatic Strengthening and International Engagement Initiative","Effective diplomacy in international relations will be intensified to strengthen the position and positive image of Malaysia at the global stage.",""],[1,"142","6","International Cooperation Expansion through Soft Power","Efforts will be enhanced to expand the involvement of the country in international cooperations, including through soft power and by showcasing the uniqueness of Malaysia to the international society.",""],[1,"142","6","Strategic Networks and Cultural Exhibition Participation","In addition, initiatives such as establishing strategic networks and participating in international art, culture and heritage exhibitions will be expanded.",""],[1,"142","6","Humanitarian Values Promotion Initiative","The humanitarian values of the rakyat will also be promoted to the international community, domestically and abroad.",""]],"178":[[1,"144","7","Sustainable Long-Term Care Ecosystem Development","This preparation will be intensified by establishing a sustainable LTC ecosystem, strengthening the labour market, skills and education, aligning fiscal priorities and improving social protection as well as enhancing the wellbeing of older persons.",""],[1,"144","8","Long-Term Care Legislation and Governance Reform","Legislation and governance related to LTC will be introduced to develop a sustainable LTC ecosystem.",""],[1,"144","8","Long-Term Care Policy and Regulatory Harmonisation","Legislation related to LTC will be enacted to streamline policies and regulations across agencies as well as ensure LTC services are of quality, easily accessible and affordable.",""],[1,"144","8","Care Ecosystem Regulatory Body","a specific entity will be identified to regulate the care ecosystem, including care centres for children, PWDs and older persons as well as religious learning centres that provide residential facilities.",""],[1,"144","8","Local Long-Term Care Expansion Action Plans","Local authorities (PBTs) will be encouraged to develop action plans in expanding the provision of LTC services at the local level.",""],[1,"145","2","Long-Term Care Insurance Scheme Exploration","a LTC insurance scheme will be explored to provide a structured and sustainable protection.",""]],"179":[[1,"144","2","Caregiver Skills Certification Programme","In 2024, a total of 8,000 caregivers in this sector received the Malaysian Skills Certificate.",""],[1,"144","9","Long-Term Care Workforce Standards and Skills Enhancement","Focus will be given to improve service quality and professionalism of LTC talent through the provision of standards and skills enhancement for caregivers and care workers.",""],[1,"144","9","National Care Profession Standards and Training Modules","national standards for the care profession as well as training modules for home- and community-care will be developed.",""],[1,"144","9","Caregiver Training and Certification Streamlining","Efforts in streamlining training and certification will be intensified in collaboration with various stakeholders based on the whole-of-nation approach.",""],[1,"144","9","Caregiver Social Protection and Benefits Enhancement","the provision of social protection and other benefits for caregivers and LTC workers, including informal caregivers will be improved.",""],[1,"144","9","TVET Incentives for Long-Term Care Industrial Training","Incentives will be introduced for the Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) students undergoing industrial training in the field of LTC to attract higher youth participation.",""]],"180":[[1,"145","1","Expansion of Home and Community Care Services","Home- and community-care for children, PWDs and older persons will be expanded to increase access to healthcare and welfare services as well as education.",""],[1,"145","1","Mobile Care Services Enhancement","Mobile care services and the Home Help Services Programme for those requiring care assistance will be enhanced.",""],[1,"145","1","Community-Based Domiciliary and Palliative Care Services","community-based domiciliary and palliative domiciliary care services with the involvement of families and local communities will also be introduced to provide physical and emotional support to patients and families.",""],[1,"146","2","Expanded Support Programmes and Services for Older Persons","In addition, access to more comprehensive support programmes and services will be expanded, comprising healthcare services as well as community-based care and support.",""],[1,"146","2","Expansion of PAWE-Based Older Persons Activities","Older persons activities based on the PAWE concept will also be expanded to areas independent of PAWE facilities.",""],[1,"146","3","Volunteer Services for Older Persons","Volunteer services for older persons will be intensified through the involvement of community and CSOs to strengthen intergenerational and community bonding.",""],[1,"146","3","Centralised Social Activity Hubs for Older Persons","existing facilities, such as multipurpose halls, as well as sports and community centres will be utilised as hubs to undertake centralised social activities.",""]],"181":[[1,"145","2","Quality Care Services Industry Development","The quality care services industry will continue to be developed for Malaysia to be a regional LTC services hub.",""],[1,"145","2","Care Economy MSME Promotion","Industry players, particularly the micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) will be encouraged to explore the potential in the care economy as a new source of growth.",""],[1,"146","4","One-Stop Centre for Ageing Society Technology Solutions","A one-stop centre to provide technology-based solutions for ageing society will be established through collaboration between local industry experts and researchers.",""]],"182":[[1,"145","3","Labour Market and Retirement Age Regulatory Reform","The labour market will be strengthened to ensure a more responsive labour ecosystem in line with the demographic shifts in the preparation towards an aged nation.",""],[1,"145","4","Flexible Work Arrangements Guidelines Adoption","The adoption of the Guidelines on the Implementation of Flexible Work Arrangements will also be encouraged to provide flexibility for employees with difficulties to work under the existing work arrangements.",""]],"183":[[1,"138","1","Health and Housing Reform Agenda","reforming health and housing",""],[1,"145","6","Fiscal Prioritization for Social Services and Infrastructure","Measures to align fiscal priorities will be undertaken to optimise the government financial resources, ensuring better provision of social services and infrastructure in the preparation for an aged nation.",""],[1,"145","6","Age-Friendly Premises and Infrastructure Development","Renovation and development of premises in compliance with the Garis Panduan Perancangan Reka Bentuk Sejagat will be facilitated and more age-friendly infrastructure will be provided in collaboration with the private sector.",""],[1,"145","6","Legislative Measures to Curb Cardiovascular Diseases and NCDs","legislative interventions will be implemented to curb the rising prevalence of cardiovascular diseases and non-communicable diseases (NCDs).",""],[1,"146","2","Older Persons Welfare and Participation Legislation","Specific legislation related to older persons will be enacted, encompassing the aspects of equitable protection, welfare and participation in the society.",""],[1,"146","3","Integrated Tracking System for Older Persons Safety","This initiative will be supported through the development of an integrated tracking system which adopts smart technologies to monitor the safety of older persons, particularly those at risk of suffering from deterioration of cognitive function.",""]],"184":[[1,"146","6","Strengthening the National Health Regulatory System","This health reform will enhance the competitiveness of local industry players in producing pharmaceuticals and medical devices by strengthening the national regulatory system.",""],[1,"147","8","Medicine and Medical Device Security Enhancement","as well as enhance security of medicine and medical devices.",""],[1,"149","4","Pharmaceutical and Medical Devices Production Capacity Expansion","Local pharmaceutical and medical devices manufacturers will be encouraged to increase production capacity, capability and infrastructure to reduce dependency on imported medicine and medical devices.",""],[1,"149","4","National Pharmaceutical Regulatory System Improvement","the national pharmaceutical regulatory system will be improved based on WHO standards to ensure a comprehensive pharmaceutical production ecosystem.",""],[1,"149","4","Pharmaceutical Logistics Efficiency Enhancement","the efficiency of logistics in product distribution will be enhanced to ensure preparedness of the country in facing global health crises.",""],[1,"149","5","National Vaccine Production Development and Training Enhancement","The Dana Pembangunan dan Pengukuhan Penghasilan Vaksin Negara and the Latihan Program Vaksin programme will be enhanced to strengthen research and development as well as talent in local vaccine production.",""],[1,"149","5","Expansion of International Pharmaceutical Ecosystem Participation","the participation of the country in the networks of the international pharmaceutical product ecosystem will continue to be expanded to elevate the national capability in producing quality and safe pharmaceutical products for the rakyat.",""],[1,"149","6","Pharmaceutical Product Tracking and Traceability System","A pharmaceutical product tracking and traceability system will be developed to ensure efficient, effective, safe, responsive and resilient pharmaceutical logistics management.",""]],"185":[[1,"148","1","Expansion of Behavioural Change Measures for High-Risk Products","mechanism will be expanded to high-risk products, such as tobacco, electronic cigarettes, vape and alcohol.",""],[1,"148","3","Integrated Health Literacy and NCD Prevention Policies","Integrated cross-sectoral policies and promotional programmes will be strengthened to build a health- literate society towards reducing the risk of NCDs.",""],[1,"148","3","Health Security Strengthening Measures","In addition, health security will be strengthened to safeguard the rakyat and the economy from health threats.",""],[1,"148","3","Mandatory Front-of-Pack Food Labelling Grading System","A grading system will be implemented through a mandatory front-of-pack labelling to reduce sugar and salt content in food and beverage products.",""],[1,"148","4","National Health Security Capacity Strategic Framework","The threat of emerging or re-emerging diseases as well as other public health threats will be curbed through the implementation of a national health security capacity strategic framework, in line with the requirements of the International Health Regulations 2005.",""],[1,"148","4","Infectious Disease Eradication and Elimination Initiative","Efforts will be intensified in eradicating, eliminating and ending 12 infectious diseases, such as polio, malaria, tuberculosis and leprosy by 2030, in accordance with the targets set by the World Health Organization (WHO).",""],[1,"148","4","Health in All Policies Mainstreaming Initiative","initiatives to mainstream healthcare to be comprehensive and equitable based on the 'Health in All Policies' concept will be implemented through cross-sector collaboration.",""]],"186":[[1,"148","6","Health Legislative Framework Update","The health legislative framework will be updated to take into consideration demographic changes, evolving disease epidemiology and technology advancements.",""],[1,"148","6","Organ and Tissue Transplantation Act Improvement","For this purpose, the act related to organ and tissue transplantation will be improved, and a mental capacity",""],[1,"149","1","National Health Bill Drafting","bill will be drafted.",""]],"187":[[1,"152","2","Compliance with National Housing Quality Standard CIS 26: 2019","In addition, housing developers will be encouraged to comply with the Standard Perumahan Kebangsaan CIS 26: 2019 during the planning and construction phases to ensure the provision of quality houses and maintenance are undertaken periodically for the safety and durability of buildings.",""],[1,"153","1","Green Building Index Certification Promotion for Housing Developers","Housing developers will also be encouraged to obtain the Green Building Index certification in ensuring sustainable, energy-efficient and eco-friendly buildings.",""]],"188":[[1,"138","1","Public Security and Defence Strengthening Initiative","efforts to strengthen public security and defence",""],[1,"154","1","Defence Readiness Enhancement through Aircraft and Littoral Mission Ship Deployment","Aircraft as well as the Littoral Mission Ship have been and are being implemented to enhance defence readiness.",""],[1,"155","3","Strengthening of Defence, Border Control and Enforcement Operations","National sovereignty will be upheld through the strengthening of defence, border control and enforcement operations, as well as the development of the defence industry ecosystem.",""],[1,"155","3","Strengthening of Future Forces Integration and Agility","Emphasis will continue to be given on strengthening the Future Forces to be more integrated, agile and focused.",""],[1,"155","4","Land Mobility Asset Enhancement Programme","the land mobility asset enhancement programme of the Malaysian Armed Forces will be implemented to ensure assets availability and a more systematic maintenance.",""],[1,"163","1","Security and Defence Strengthening","Focus will also be given in health and housing reform, strengthening of security and defence, preservation of planetary health as well as improvement in disaster management to raise the floor and strengthen governance.",""]],"189":[[1,"155","1","Cybercrime Prevention and Enforcement Strengthening","Efforts to combat cybercrime will continue to be intensified through improvement in infostructure and infrastructure, strengthening of enforcement and legislation, enhancement of international cooperation as well as development of local expertise.",""],[1,"155","1","Cybercrime Awareness and Public Education Campaigns","Educational programmes and awareness campaigns through social media and digital platforms will be expanded to increase public awareness on the risks and protective measures against cybercrime.",""],[1,"155","1","National Scam Response Centre Strengthening","The role of the National Scam Response Centre as a one-stop centre will be strengthened to address online financial fraud more effectively.",""]],"190":[[1,"155","2","Crisis Management Policy and SOP Strengthening","Crisis management will be strengthened through improvement in the policies and standard operating procedures (SOPs) as well as enhancement of capacity.",""],[1,"155","2","Joint Security Agency Training Programme","periodic joint training by security agencies will be intensified to ensure a coordinated and fast response.",""],[1,"155","2","Security Agency Asset Management Improvement","Asset management will be improved to enhance the capability and effectiveness of security agency operations.",""]],"191":[[1,"155","3","Development of the Defence Industry Ecosystem","National sovereignty will be upheld through the strengthening of defence, border control and enforcement operations, as well as the development of the defence industry ecosystem.",""],[1,"155","3","Expansion of International Cooperation for Effective Diplomacy","Effective diplomacy will be expanded through closer international cooperation.",""],[1,"155","4","International Defence Cooperation Enhancement","International defence cooperation will also be enhanced as part of the effective diplomacy strategy to safeguard national sovereignty.",""],[1,"155","4","United Nations Peacekeeping Participation","Malaysia will also continue participating in peacekeeping missions under the mandate of the United Nations.",""],[1,"155","6","National Defence Industry Ecosystem Development","The national defence industry ecosystem will be further developed to reduce dependency on foreign technology and expertise.",""]],"192":[[1,"156","2","Army Veterans Social Support Assistance Programme Improvement","Social support assistance programmes will be improved to ensure the welfare of army veterans and families are always safeguarded.",""],[1,"156","2","Veteran Skills Training and Employability Support","These programmes include skills training under TVET, entrepreneurship and modern agriculture to enhance the employability of retired personnel.",""]],"193":[[1,"156","4","Immigration Detention Depot Safety and Welfare Improvement","at immigration detention depots will be improved to ensure the safety and welfare of officers and detainees are well protected.",""],[1,"156","4","PATI Deportation Programme Enhancement","The programme for deporting PATI with the cooperation of relevant embassies will be enhanced to reduce overcrowding and operational cost of detention depots.",""]],"194":[[1,"157","3","National Climate and Biodiversity Policy Framework","Several policies and legislations were formulated in the efforts to address the impact of climate change and enhance natural resources management.",""],[1,"157","3","Long-Term Low-Emissions Development Strategy","The Long-Term Low Emissions Development Strategy of Malaysia was developed to achieve the national net-zero target by 2050.",""],[1,"157","9","Climate, Biodiversity, Circular Economy, and Waste Management Strategy","focus will be given to efforts in addressing issues related to climate change and environment, enhancing the conservation and preservation of biodiversity, as well as strengthening the implementation of the circular economy and waste management.",""],[1,"158","1","National Adaptation Plan","The National Adaptation Plan will be introduced to address climate change threats in various areas, including agriculture and food security, forestry and biodiversity as well as public health.",""],[1,"158","1","Climate Change Legislation","A specific legislation on climate change will also be enforced to regulate the implementation of climate action initiatives comprehensively.",""],[1,"158","1","Embodied Carbon Measurement Pilot Project","In addition, a pilot project to measure embodied carbon1 in the construction of public infrastructure will be implemented to reduce GHG emissions in the construction sector.",""],[1,"158","2","National Carbon Market Policy","The national carbon market policy will be implemented to facilitate carbon trading, either through compliance or on voluntary basis.",""],[1,"158","2","Forest Carbon Offset Instrument","The Forest Carbon Offset, as a national carbon credit instrument based on local needs and capabilities, will be developed to facilitate trading of carbon credit from the forestry sector.",""],[1,"158","2","Forest Conservation Certificate Expansion","The Forest Conservation Certificate, as a non-market green financing instrument, will be expanded to encourage financing by the private sector in implementing forest conservation and protection activities.",""],[1,"158","2","Blue Carbon Initiatives for Mangroves and Wetlands","Blue carbon initiatives for mangrove and wetland areas will also be explored to enhance efforts in mitigating climate change and protecting coastal areas from flood and erosion threats.",""],[1,"163","1","Environmental Sustainability Measures","During the Thirteenth Plan period, continuous efforts will be undertaken to address key issues and challenges that undermine the wellbeing of the rakyat, particularly the cost of living burden and environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"163","1","Planetary Health Preservation Measures","Focus will also be given in health and housing reform, strengthening of security and defence, preservation of planetary health as well as improvement in disaster management to raise the floor and strengthen governance.",""]],"195":[[1,"159","3","Green Lifestyle Public Awareness Campaign","communication, education and public awareness aspects incorporating behavioural insights, such as green lifestyle campaign will be strengthened to accelerate societal behavioural change",""],[1,"159","3","Environmental Sustainability R&D Collaboration Initiative","R&D&C&I activities will be intensified through strategic collaboration among various stakeholders, including industry players and research institutions to enhance environmental sustainability",""],[1,"159","3","International Environmental Financing and Technical Assistance Mobilization","technical assistance through cooperation with various stakeholders as well as international financing, such as the Global Environment Facility, the Green Climate Fund and the Adaptation Fund, will be leveraged",""],[1,"159","3","Integrated Environmental Data Sharing and Decision Support System","Data-driven interventions and decision- making processes will be facilitated through improved sharing of and access to a more integrated information",""]],"196":[[1,"159","4","Biodiversity Conservation Policy and Governance Strengthening","Conservation and preservation of biodiversity will be enhanced, encompassing measures to strengthen development planning and implementation as well as improve policies, legislation and governance.",""],[1,"159","4","Human-Wildlife Conflict Management and Forest Protection","Emphasis will be given in managing human-wildlife conflicts as well as preserving forest treasures, flora and fauna in risk areas through enhancement of development planning at all levels of government.",""],[1,"159","4","Nature-Based Biodiversity Restoration Programme","The adoption of nature-based solutions in biodiversity conservation, such as restoration of mangrove forest area and rehabilitation of coral reef will be expanded.",""],[1,"159","5","Expansion of Biodiversity and Protected Area Gazettement","More key biodiversity and protected areas, such as national parks, Ramsar sites, biosphere reserves as well as mangrove and peat swamp forests will be gazetted to preserve the balance and sustainability of the natural environment.",""],[1,"159","5","Integrated Enforcement Against Flora and Fauna Crimes","Enforcement through an integrated operation model will be strengthened to combat any forms of crimes related to flora and fauna.",""]],"197":[[1,"160","1","Integrated Solid Waste Management Upgrade","Solid waste management will be improved through transition to a more integrated, high-tech and sustainable approach, supported by modern recycling infrastructure, including material recovery facilities.",""],[1,"160","1","Community Waste Reduction and Recycling Initiatives","Community involvement will be strengthened through various initiatives, such as the expansion of the Program Komuniti Sifar Sisa, the implementation of the pay-as-you- throw scheme as well as the establishment of buy back and smart recycling centres.",""],[1,"160","1","Rural Solid Waste Service Improvement","Solid waste management services in rural areas will be improved through collaboration among district offices, PBTs and local communities.",""],[1,"160","1","Centralised Waste Management Coordination Agency","a proposal for a centralised waste management coordination under a dedicated agency will be explored.",""],[1,"160","2","Landfill Prohibition and Circular Waste Management Policy","A policy to prohibit the opening of new landfills will be implemented to accelerate the circular economy and improve waste management.",""],[1,"160","2","Waste-to-Energy Plant Expansion through Public-Private Partnership","The construction of waste-to-energy plants to reduce reliance on landfill will be expanded through public-private partnership.",""],[1,"160","2","Existing Landfill Rehabilitation and Alternative Waste Management Programme","efforts will be focused on rehabilitation of existing landfill sites and promotion of alternative waste management approaches, such as composting, biomass processing and implementing the 5R2.",""],[1,"160","3","Radioactive Waste Management Facilities Development","storage, treatment, conditioning and disposal facilities will also be developed to manage radioactive waste in a safer and more sustainable manner.",""]],"198":[[1,"162","1","Disaster Management SOP Streamlining","Existing SOPs will be streamlined to enhance coordination among all relevant agencies.",""],[1,"162","1","Interagency Disaster Response Training Exercises","joint training exercises involving various agencies will be intensified to ensure fast and integrated responses.",""],[1,"162","1","Disaster Response Asset Modernisation","Asset modernisation will also be continued",""],[1,"162","2","Multi-purpose Disaster Shelter Infrastructure Adaptation","The design of selected public infrastructure will be customised as multi-purpose disaster shelters, and the use of existing infrastructure will also be expanded.",""],[1,"162","2","Post-Disaster Support and Counselling Programme","Support programmes, including provision of counselling services will also be expanded to assist disaster victims in resuming normal life post-disaster.",""],[1,"162","2","Whole-of-Nation Disaster Response Coordination","The involvement of all stakeholders, including the private sector, CSOs, and NGOs, under the whole-of-nation approach will be intensified to provide support to communities affected by disasters.",""]],"199":[[1,"175","5","Comprehensive Social Development Policy and Legislation","The government ensures social equality for the rakyat by formulating comprehensive social development policies and legislation.",""]],"200":[[1,"150","1","SME Capacity and Competitiveness Support for Real Estate","New approaches to be introduced will offer opportunities for real estate industry players, particularly among the small and medium enterprises to increase capacity, scale and competitiveness.",""],[1,"176","4","Economic Ecosystem Facilitation and Policy Direction","The government serves as a responsive facilitator in strengthening the economic ecosystem, enabling all economic agents to assume their respective roles efficiently and effectively.",""]],"201":[[1,"177","3","Corporate ESG Mainstreaming Initiative","Companies reduce carbon footprint by enculturating the principles of environmental, social and governance (ESG) as standard practices in business activities and operations.",""],[1,"177","3","Community-Based Environmental and Natural Resource Management","Companies, in collaboration with communities also actively lead environmental and natural resource management efforts as well as implement conservation programmes.",""],[1,"177","3","Biodiversity Innovation Support Initiative","In addition, the third sector also plays an active role in preserving and conserving biodiversity endowment by introducing innovations to resolve local issues.",""],[1,"177","4","Cross-Sector Environmental Policy and Legislation Mainstreaming","The government continues to ensure the formulation of policy and legislation across sectors prioritises environment and sustainable use of resources",""],[1,"177","4","Stakeholder Transition Mechanisms for Sustainable Practices","the introduction of intervention mechanisms is able to motivate all stakeholders in transitioning towards sustainable practices",""],[1,"177","4","International Environmental Negotiation and Collaboration Engagement","The government also plays an active role at the international level in voicing the stance of Malaysia on environmental management and biodiversity preservation through various negotiation and collaboration platforms",""]],"202":[[1,"178","3","Good Governance Policy and Legislation Strengthening","The government leads good governance by strengthening policies and legislation as well as implementing best practices comprehensively at all levels.",""],[1,"178","3","Institutional Empowerment and Independence for Government Bodies","Relevant government institutions are granted authority, capability and independence to perform their functions without interference from any vested parties.",""],[1,"178","3","Open Public Information Sharing Initiative","Data and information of public interest are shared openly to enable the rakyat to assess the efficiency and effectiveness of government administration.",""],[1,"178","3","Integrity and Credibility Standards for Public Leaders","Leaders at all levels have high credibility and integrity as well as uphold the principle of serving the nation and the rakyat, independent of benefits and rewards from the positions.",""],[1,"202","1","Government-Linked Enterprises Activation and Reform Programme","Government-linked Enterprises Activation and Reform Programme",""]]}});